2 CONT William Spivey and his wife Mollie Stallings and son Henry are all buried together in an old abandoned grave yard east of Eatonton near the intersection of Ward's Chapel Road and Sparta Highway. There is a stone wall built around 
2 CONC all three (per Henry's will). Just outside the wall is another son and has a masonic marker. There was a plantation house that belonged to one son, but has since been torn down. William served in the Revolutionary War in Sampson, 
2 CONC North Carolina. They at least had: William Spivey Jr., Joshua Spivey, Henry Spivey, Moses Spivey, Sarah Elizabeth Spivey (Hardin), Mary Polly Spivey (Parrish), John Spivey, Caleb Spivey, Sally Spivey (Gordon), and Christian Spivey
2 CONC . These are mentioned in his will.
2 CONT As far as his birthdate, a book, An Ancestral History, by Thomas Ross Gambrell, 2001, p. 342 states that William's father George was 33 when he died in 1778 when his youngest son James was 3. That totally fits as James was born in
2 CONC  1775. Jonathan was the oldest, then George and the youngest three were David, William, and James. This is stated in George's will. This means that instead of being born in the 1720's as many have proposed, George was born about 1
2 CONC 745. He could not have had children born in the 1750's because he was a child himself. The earliest he could have married was about 1761-1763 as he would have been 16-18 years old. Jonathan was the oldest, George the second, so th
2 CONC ey would have been born about 1761-1765. I have estimated William's birth on his military service which was 1784-1786. If he was born in 1766, he would been 18. I know that sometimes 16 year olds fought in the Revolution, so I thi
2 CONC nk the earliest he could have been born was 1764. He did however have at least 2 possibly 3 older brothers and it really depends on when George married Esther. I think 1765 or 1766 is a pretty good guess. This means all the childr
2 CONC en were closer in age than previously thought, and Esther was not married for 30 years and had James in 1775. This makes far more sence.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/269515897/william-spivey Find A Grave Memori
2 CONC al] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 31 2026, 20:34:39 UTC''
