1 OCCU General Store Owner, Farmer, and Minister of Pine Grove Cumberland Presbyterian Church
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Religion: Presbyterian minister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Military Service: Civil War stationed in Vicksburg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elected Constable of Scott County, Mississippi.
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried buried in Pine Grove cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: operated a general store. Farmer. Minister of Pine Grove Cumberland Presbyterian church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph liked to play tricks on his grand-children. J.D. Brooks tells a story of his grand-father coming to their house in a horse drawn buggy. He would call J.D. and Lilly Mae to come out. They knew that he would have candy for th
2 CONC em. The candy would be wrapped up. He would give Lily Mae hers then J.D. his. J.D. would unwrap his and find a rat instead of candy. After he laughed he would give J.D. his candy. Joseph owned a grocery store . He was a donkey rid
2 CONC ing preacher.
