2 CONT Record of Deeds, Book P, 1789-1794, pages 248-249, images #249-250, Bertie County, North Carolina, United States.  FHL microfilm #18257, Family History Library, Salt Lake City, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 25 May 1786, David Standley of Bertie County, North Carolina, sold to Edmond Standley of same, for £40, one certain tract or parcel of land containing 105 acres in Bertie County, part of a patent granted to David Standley on 23
2 CONC  September 1785, beginning at the mouth of ? and the run of Cashy Swamp to a maple.  Signed by David Standley and witnessed by David Outlaw, Sol'n Cherry.
2 CONT
2 CONT November Term 1791.  The deed was proved and ordered to be registered.
