2 CONT First husband was Robert(?) Tuck or Tucker, who was said to have owned a plantation in Bermuda. (The Tuckers were a prominent Bermuda family.)
2 CONT
2 CONT TUCKER, Frances Mrs -- NELSON, Thomas 22 Feb 1723 http://www.vagenweb.net/dinwiddie/tucker/marriage/tucker1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Robert Tucker of Lower Norfolk Co Va dec’d, Mar 1722/3. Frances Tucker  Admix. “Merchandise belonging to sd Tucker, West India goods, in ye  Stores, & Come now in ye Brigantine ‘Providence’ valued at £450-9-9, in  the hands of 
2 CONC Mrs Frances Tucker.” Three children of sd Tucker, not named. http://perquimans.lostsoulsgenealogy.com/family/johntucker.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Second wife of Thomas Nelson, "Scotch Tom", of York Town and also the widow of Tucker, of Barbados, Bermuda, by who she had one child.  Frances Courtenay was born about 1682.[1] She married Robert Tucker and had at least four chil
2 CONC dren by him.[2][3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT On February 22, 1723 in Norfolk, Virginia,[5] Mrs. Frances Tucker, widow of Robert Tucker,[6] married Thomas Nelson as his second wife (his first wife had been Margaret Reade).[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances (Tucker, née Courtenay) Nelson died in June 1766, "in her 84th year of life."[8][9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Frances Norton Mason, ed. John Norton & Sons Merchants of London and Virginia: Being the Papers from their Counting House for the Years 1750 to 1795, David and Charles, Newton Abbot, Devon, pub. 1937 (reprinted 1968) ↑ see his p
2 CONC rofile for information about her marriage to Robert Tucker and their children ↑ Historical and Genealogical Notes, in William and Mary Quarterly, Vol. X, 1902 ↑ McIntosh, Charles Fleming. Brief Abstracts of Norfolk County Wills, 1
2 CONC 710-1753, Volume 2, Colonial Dames of America, Richmond, VA, 1922, pp 121-122 lists the abstract of the will of Frances Hodges, mother of Frances Nelson, naming her two daughters (Frances and Elizabeth) and her grandchildren, incl
2 CONC uding Sarah Tucker and Sarah Nelson.
2 CONT
