1 OCCU Pastor/Chaplain
1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Lee Butler
2 CONT
2 CONT    BIG  SPRING - Dr. Lee Butler, 70, died Thursday, Feb. 20, 1997, at his
2 CONT    residence.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Service  will  be  at  4  p.m.  today at the First Baptist Church with
2 CONT    burial   in   Trinity   Memorial   Mausoleum.   Arrangements   are  by
2 CONT    Nalley-Pickle & Welch Funeral Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT    He was born June 10, 1926, in Houston. A Navy veteran of World War II,
2 CONT    he  was  an  ordained Baptist minister, was director of chaplaincy and
2 CONT    pastoral  care  for  the Big Spring State Hospital and was a member of
2 CONT    the First Baptist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Survivors  include  his  wife,  Molly  Butler of Big Spring; two sons,
2 CONT    Tommy  Butler  of  Whitehouse and Terry Butler of De Soto; a daughter,
2 CONT    Janie  Strader  of  Houston;  a  sister,  Gloria Joyce Restelli of Big
2 CONT    Spring; and four grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary from the February 22,1997 edition of The San Angelo Standard-Times
