1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Spivey-361
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born about 1603 in England and his parents were possibly https://www.geni.com/people/Ann-Spivey/6000000091379304106?through=6000000091378723403 and https://www.geni.com/people/William-Spivey-Sr/6000000037492915101?through=6
2 CONC 000000091378723403.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Spivey married Margaret, perhaps Matthews.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died about 1673 in Nansemond County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT George Spivey, obtained a grant in Nansemond Co Va, Oct 22, 1666, “near the head of Southern Branch,” and John Spivey had a grant Oct 28, 1697, “at a place called ‘planters delight’ ” on E. side of Southern Branch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # George Spivey b by 1646
2 CONT # Matthew Spivey b abt 1658 m Judith Bowers 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1683, George Spivey's brother, Mathew Spivy, received 200 acres in Upper Nansemond, Virginia for the transport of four headrights. The property description clearly states the acreage bounded that of his brother, George Spivey: 
2 CONC [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Someone else's notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of the North Carolina Spiveys decend from George Adolphus Spivey, who descended from the Spivies of Yorkshire, England at Barnsley. George Adolphus Spivey was the son of Thomas Spivie (b 1583 in Barnsley, m Dorythie Escom, 16
2 CONC 06.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Spivie was the son of William Spivie (b about 1525 and m Elizabeth 1583). William was the son of William Spivye (note the change in the spelling of the names), who was born about 1530 according to the achives in Yorkshire. 
2 CONC Other than William Spivie, I have no other children listed for William Spivye.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Spivie's children were: Thomas b 1583, m 1606 to Dorythie Escom William b 1585 Jane b 1588 Esther b 1590
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Thomas Spivie and Dorythie Escom were: Isabell b 1607 John b 1610 George Adolphus b 1612 (christened 2 December 1612) Elizabeth b 1613 Ester b 1614 Thomas b 1617
2 CONT
2 CONT George Adolphus Spivey was married and there is speculation about his wife's name. Most people researching this line seem to agree she was Margaret Matthews. George and Margaret had at least two children: George Spivey, Jr. Matthe
2 CONC w …
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Someone else's notes Ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT This is what I was able to find on ancestry.com. I got conflicting information concerning William George Spivey (son of Thomas Benjamin Spivey) but I think this is correct.
2 CONT
2 CONT William George Spivey b 1603, d 1673 married Margaret Mathew
2 CONT
2 CONT Son: i.George Matthew Spivey b. 1620 in Hatfield, England d. 1690 married Virginia Hall in Nansemond Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons: i. Matthew William Spivey b. 1647, d. 1700 married Ellen James ii. James Angus Spivey b. 1648, d. 1715 married Katie Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons Of John Angus Spivey and Katie Thomas: i. Thomas Benjamin Spivey, b. 1668, d. 1730 in Chowan Co., NC married Mary Jane Jones. ii. George Angus Spivey, b 1671, d. 1720. ,married Martha Jane Littleton iii. Mathew Archibald Spiv
2 CONC ey, b. 1673, d. 1712 married Margaret Moses
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
