1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Berkeley&GSiman=1&GScid=516390&GRid=106595534& Mary Nelson Berkeley] Find A Grave Memorial# 106595534
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the "Genealogy of the Page Family of Virginia" and "Some Prominent Virginia Families, Vol 2", Mary was born in Yorktown, about 1713; married, on May 18, 1728, Col. Edmund Berkeley II, of Barn Elms, Middlesex County, V
2 CONC a. She died in Yorktown after 1772. Col Berkeley was appointed Justice of Middlesex, 1725; member of the House of Burgesses in 1736 and other years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lucy Berkeley, born - June 15, 1729, died young. 2. Edmund Berkeley, III born - Dec 5, 1730, who first married Mary Judith Randolph, of "Tuckahoe", on Nov 5, 1757 and secondly, Mary Burwell of "The Grove" on Jan 23, 1763. He wa
2 CONC s also a member of the House of Burgesses frm 1772 to 1774, and the convention of 1775-76. 3. Nelson Berkeley, born - May 16, 1733, of Airwell, Hanover County, Va, who married Elizabeth Wormeley Carter, granddaughter of Hon. Rober
2 CONC t (King) Carter, and had issue. 4. Mary (called Molly) Berkeley, born Jan 15, 1737, who married Dr. Corbin Griffin of Yorktown and had one child, Major Griffin. 5. Sally (Sarah) Berkeley, born - Jan 27, 1741, single. 6. Lucy Berke
2 CONC ley, born - June 9, 1744, single.
