3 CONT Nelson House
3 CONT
3 CONT "Scotch Tom" Nelson, founder of the Nelson family and fortune in Yorktown, built this mansion in the early 1700's.  Later it passed to Yorktown's most illustrious son Thomas Nelson, Jr., who signed the Declaration of Independence,
3 CONC  served as wartime Governor of Virginia, and commanded the Virginia militia during the siege of Yorktown.
