1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hugh Nelson (son of William Nelson) was born 1658 in Penrith, Cumbria, England, and died 1708 in Penrith, Cumbria, England.He married Sarah Jackson on 1673 in Penrith, Cumbria, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Hugh Nelson and Sarah Jackson:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 1673, Penrith, Cumbria, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hugh Nelson and Sarah Jackson are:
2 CONT *+Thomas Nelson, b. 20 Feb 1677, Penrith, , Cumberland, England1335, d. 07 Oct 1745, Yorktown, , Virginia, USA1335.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William Nelson and his wife, Bridget, were listed on a Nelson monument formerly in the Penrith Churchyard. In 1704, Bishop Nicolson, visited the church and noted what was listed: "Here lyeth also the body of William Nelson, third 
2 CONC Son who died upon the 28th of October 1670 aged 49 years: And also Bridget his wife who died upon the 18th of Dec. 1670, aged 50 years." (Ref: The Nelsons of Penrith, by G. Watson, Sep 18, 1900.) William Nelson and son Hugh after 
2 CONC him were cloth merchants.(The Nelsons, A Biographic Study of a Virginia Family in the Eighteenth Century, by Emory Gibbo Evans, 1957)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Andrew's_Church,_Penrith
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas "Scotch Tom" Nelson (1677-1745) was the progenitor of Yorktown, Virginia Nelsons. He was born to Hugh and Sarah Nelson who were cloth merchants in Penrith. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/g/l/a/Benjamin-Glasgow/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0901.html
