1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT When Edward Garrett Nelson Jr was born on 16 October 1803, in Craven, North Carolina, United States, his father, Edward Garrett Nelson Sr, was 43 and his mother, Winifred Johnson, was 35. He married Sarah "Sally" Mae Roach on 18 F
2 CONC ebruary 1825, in Craven, North Carolina, United States. They were the parents of at least 1 son and 3 daughters. He died on 29 December 1841, in his hometown, at the age of 38, and was buried in Vanceboro, Craven, North Carolina, 
2 CONC United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/205100324/edward-nelson
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT The Nelsons were all mechanics and blacksmiths.  In Our Family Genealogy P. 34: The will of Edward Nelson, Jr. was Made 9-6-1840, in which he left all his property to his wife, Sarah (Sally) Roach Nelson, to use as she sees best. 
2 CONC  At her death Augustus Washington Nelson was to get the plantation "where I now live, which I hold by deed from my father, Edward Nelson, Sr., decd.  Also 100 ac. deeded me from Sam I. Roach.  Also the land between Reedy and the m
2 CONC ain pocosin and that in the reedy pocosin.  The bottom lands beginning at the upper dam across Cabin Swamp at the edge of Palmetto Swamp.  400 ac. in all."   The balance of the land was to go to his daughters Polly (Nelson Smith),
2 CONC  Winnifred and Emily Freeman Nelson.  Several slaves were to be divided among the children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
