1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sarah Willson (b ca 1726, Londonderry, Ireland - bef 1790, Abbeville, SC); married John Roseman, b. UK ca 1710 (could have been England or Ireland); came to Annapolis, Maryland Dec 1725 on the ship Forward from Eng
2 CONC land as an indentured convict. He relocated to Augusta County, VA after 1740 and married Sarah Willson. This is one of our mysteries, when and where they were married. From Chalkley's Chronicles they owned land, 380 acres, on Moff
2 CONC ett's Creek which they sold in Nov 1765, after which they relocated with their children to the Old 96 District in SC. Their children were Samuel (married Sarah Hodges), James (married 1st ??, 2nd Mary Daugherty, widow of James Dau
2 CONC gherty in SC, in the 1790s), Margaret (married Bartholomew Weems), Jean (never married) and Sarah F. (married Richard Hodges, brother of Sarah who married Samuel). The birth dates of their children are unknown, as well as the date
2 CONC s they were married, and our other big mystery is the name of the wife of James Rosamond, but it could have been another Hodges sibling of Richard and Sarah, or Lettice Jones, sister of Adam Crain Jones. I have information on the 
2 CONC rest of their spouses as well extensive information on their numerous descendants.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LBZ7-VMC/sarah-wilson-1726-1790
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Sarah
2 CONT Sarah Wilson was christened on 24 November 1726, in Church of St Andrew, Holborn, Camden, London, England, United Kingdom as the daughter of Thomas Wilson and Elizabeth Berry. She married John Rosemond in 1742, in Augusta, Virgini
2 CONC a, United States. They were the parents of at least 2 sons and 3 daughters. She died on 23 October 1790, in Abbeville, South Carolina, United States, at the age of 63.
2 CONT
