2 CONT (7) Jimmy Rosamond <jdrosamond@comcast.net>:
2 CONT
2 CONT WILL OF SAMUEL ROSAMOND
2 CONT
2 CONT State of South Carolina, Pendleton District
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God, Amen. I, Samuel Rosamond, being in health and of a disposing mind, do make this my last will and testament and desire it may be received as such by all whom it may concern.
2 CONT
2 CONT First, I do will and positively order that all my just debts be paid.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, that the plantation whereon I now live consisting of three small tracts with the mill thereon be sold as soon as conveniency will admit of by my executors hereafter mentioned and titles made to the same and that a planta
2 CONC tion or tract of land at not more than One Thousand Dollars price be purchased by them for my wife and family to live on, either in Abbeville or Pendleton Districts, convenient to some place of public worship such as they make cho
2 CONC ice of, and at my wife’s death or a second marriage to fall to my male heirs. Notwithstanding, if my wife and family should incline to move to some other place, they are hereby empowered to sell said land and purchase other land f
2 CONC or the same purpose in any other place in this state or in any of the United States out of the monies arising from the sale of such land and to receive titles to it for the above mentioned purchase.
2 CONT
2 CONT I will and order as soon as conveniency will allow my three Negro women, Teeney, Tonny, and Sign, to be sold and that three other young wenches be purchased in their places at not more than Twelve Hundred Dollars price, and said N
2 CONC egroes and their increase, if any, shall remain with my wife and family that remains with her and to be under her direction for her benefit and the benefit of the family that remains with her. Notwithstanding, it is put in the pow
2 CONC er of my wife and executors, hereby, to dispose of to my children as they marry or come of age a certain portion of the property that is with the family so that that portion is not more than their equal divide of such property.
2 CONT
2 CONT As to Negro Peter, I allow to be sold or to remain with family as my wife and executors shall find to answer best. If sold the monies arising from his sale with the other money belonging to the estate to be put to interest and to 
2 CONC continue at interest until five of my children are come of age or married and has issue. Then the half of said money to be divided among the five and the remainder of the money to remain at interest until the remaining children sh
2 CONC all arrive at such state as the first five when it shall be equally divided amongst the minor children.
2 CONT
2 CONT And whereas, Negro Will, by his late mistress' will, at my death has the privilege of choosing his master or mistress amongst my children. When he has made his choice and that one child has confirmed his choice, he shall then be v
2 CONC alued by Sovorin appraisers, and that child shall take him as so much of their lawful divide, and whereas William Pyle and his wife was given their choice of the two Negro girls that they have yet the same privilege allowed them, 
2 CONC the other girl shall be accounted as part of the undivided estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT I will and order to be sold one horse wagon and my two stills, my desk and folding table with some other small articles, my stock of cows and hogs with three horse creations, Snip Tomeny and a yard filly, to remain with the family
2 CONC  for their use, my books (Scots Family Bible excepted which is to remain with the family) to be divided into lots for my children and the eldest to have the first choice and so on to the last. The land and negroes with other thing
2 CONC s ordered to be sold upon a credit of two years paying interest for the last year.
2 CONT
2 CONT I will that every one of my children shall have at my wife’s death their part as the law in such case has provided except the land mentioned in page first of this my will.
2 CONT
2 CONT I hereby empower my executors to make titles to Robert Young for two hundred and seventy nine acres of land sold to him in Abbeville, where I formerly lived. Upon his paying up, the purchase money according to bargain, I give to m
2 CONC y two executors, hereafter, named upon condition of their both acting the sum of Twenty Five Dollars more than commission.
2 CONT
2 CONT I do hereby appoint and ordain my son-in-law, William Pyles, of Abbeville, and Robert McCan, Esquire, of Pendleton my executors in witness whereof, I hereby do hereunto set my hand and seal this Second Day of September and in the 
2 CONC Year of Our Lord One Thousand Eight Hundred and Eight.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saml Rosmamond (SEAL)
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Westfield John Jones Ambrose Jones
2 CONT
2 CONT CODICIL
2 CONT
2 CONT I, Samuel Rosemon, in the foregoing or annexed last will and testament having further considered the same do think proper to make constitute and publish the following codicil thereto in the following manner-
2 CONT
2 CONT First, I will and request of my executors to dispose of the plantation and lands whereon I now reside at public sale.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, I leave my Negro man, Will, to be disposed of according to my will bearing date of September 2, 1808, and the residue of my Negroes namely, Peter, Jim, and Dudly, with Tenah, Sinah, Jenny, and Charlotte, are to be sold. 
2 CONC And further, I give to my affectionate wife all my household and kitchen furniture with six milk cows and the stock of hogs that belongs to the mill-with a sufficient quantity of corn for the support of the family for one year.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is my will that my executors pay yearly to my affectionate wife, Sarah Roseman, out of my estate, five pounds for each minor under age.
2 CONT
2 CONT It further is my will that the grist mill be kept in good repair and the expenses to be defrayed out of the income of the mill and the remainder to go to the use of the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT And, I do constitute Robert McCann, Esq. And Capt Barksdale Garrison, my true and lawful executors to my last will and testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand Seal this 18th Day of June 1812.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saml Rosamond (SEAL)
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness present:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wm Farip Sam (X) Tucker [his mark] David Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT Recorded in Will Book A, page 140 Recorded October 5, 1812 Proved October 5, 1812 John Harris, O.P.D.
2 CONT
