2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for SOUTH CAROLINA  (Soldier).  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A097617  DAR Ancestor # A097617]
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT James Rosamond BIRTH	1754 Virginia, USA DEATH	1806 (aged 51–52) Abbeville County, South Carolina, USA BURIAL	Non-Cemetery Burial, Specifically: burial location unknown  MEMORIAL ID	132721473 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 2 FLOWERS 1 James was married twice. First to Lettice Tillman about 1778 and from this union had the following children: Nathaniel, Thomas, Benjamin, Samuel and Mary. After Lettice's death, he secondly married Mary
2 CONC , widow of Daugherty after October 1795 when her husband died. They only had one child from this union. The son, James mentioned in his will was his second wife's son from her first marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT (special thanks to Karyl Lee Rodabough for the following info) James' birth was between 1750 and 1760 when John and Sarah were still in Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Rosamond, R255, M. Born ca 1754 in Augusta County, Virginia. James died in Abbeville District, SC bef 10 Jul 1806, he was about 52. Occupation: Farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT James served in the Revolutionary War in the Ninety-Six District before a nd after the fall of Charleston. The Siege of Charleston occurred in 1780 by the British Army led by Sir Henry Clinton. James furnished 150 lbs. of pork to 
2 CONC the militia in 1782. He obtained land grants as a result of his service in the war. An abstract of his service in the Revolutionary War is on file at the Historical Commission in South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the first national census in 1790, James, his brother Samuel, and his m other Sarah were the only Rosamond Heads of Household listed in South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his brother Samuel are mentioned in their sister Jean Rosamond's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage date to Mary Daugherty is based on the approximate date of death of her first husband around October 1795.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1800 Census Abbeville SC Name: James Rosemond County: Abbeville State: South Carolina Free White Males Under 10: 1 Free White Males - Benjamin 10 to 15: 2 Free White Males - Samuel E., Thomas A. 16 to 25: 1 Free White Males - Nath
2 CONC aniel Jones «b»45 and Over : 1 - James «/b»Free White Females - ) «b»45 and Over : 1 («/b»Mary (Doherty Number of Slaves: 9 Per: Emma A. Maughan
2 CONT
