2 PLAC Pine Log Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rydal
3 STAE GA
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 MAY 1807
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 DEC 1878
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of James and Agnes Elizabeth Gray Weems. He was three times happily married -- twice in South Carolina and once in Georgia. Each of the two former unions resulted in several children. In 1851 he moved from Sout
2 CONC h Carolina to Georgia, where he lived and died. After his removal to Georgia he lost his second wife; in 1864 he married his third wife Kesiah Ann Barton of Pine Log, GA, daughter of Vinson Anderson and Susan Ellis Barton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by wife Agnes (d 1864): those in brackets are possible children]
2 CONT
2 CONT * [John W. b. 1835 married Margaret; head of household 1860 Cass Co GA]
2 CONT * [William F. b. 1837 married Mary, head of household 1860 Cass Co GA]
2 CONT * Samuel C b 1839
2 CONT * Francis A b 1841 married Julia head of household 1880 Bartow (Cassville), a miller, children Minnie 1867, Franklin 1869, Hattie 1871, Lillie 1873, Luther 1879
2 CONT * David J b 1847
2 CONT * Mary A Winter b 1849
2 CONT * Emma M Winter b 1853
2 CONT * Alford or Albert C b 1856
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by wife Keziah:
2 CONT
2 CONT * James B. b 1865
2 CONT * Susan Leila b. 1867 married Richard A. Milner
2 CONT * Beatrice b 1868
2 CONT * Madison O. b 1869
2 CONT * Margaret b. 1875
2 CONT * Joseph b. 1876
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Pine Log Cemetery  Rydal Bartow County Georgia, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Free Press Cartersville, Georgia December 19, 1878, Page 3
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcribed by: Laurel Baty
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of a Good Citizen.
2 CONT
2 CONT We regret to learn of the death, which occurred on Friday last, of Mr. A. J. WEEMS, one of our best and most honored citizens. He had been ill for eight weeks and suffered intensely from the disease that terminated his most exempl
2 CONC ary life. During his illness he had no hopes of recovery, and fervently prayed that he might find relief in  death which had no terrors for such a good man as he. The funeral services were attended on Saturday last by the largest 
2 CONC crowd that had ever assembled at Pine Log church. He was conscious up to within twenty-four hours of his demise.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Weems was born in Abbeville district, S. C., on the 11th of May, 1807; and consequently, was 71 years, 7 months and 2 days old. He came to this country in 1851, where he has lived an honored and Christian citizen, beloved by a
2 CONC ll and mistrusted by none. We drop a tear to his memory and revere his virtues.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21154042/andrew-jefferson-weems
