1 NAME Benjamin /Youngblood/
2 GIVN Benjamin
2 SURN Youngblood
2 _MARNM Youngblood
1 NAME Judge Benjamin Youngblood
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 OCT 1773
2 PLAC Augusta, Richmond, Georgia, USA
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE JAN 1860
2 ADDR
3 STAE Marion Co (Old Pike Co)
3 CTRY Mississippi
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 JAN 1860
2 PLAC Walthall, Marion, Mississippi, USA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Capt. 14th Regiment of Militia
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Judge Benjamin Youngblood Quorum Justice, Marion Co., MS 1819-1822 By Ben Toney
2 CONT
2 CONT BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD was born October 20, 1773 in Richmond Co., GA, likely the son of JOHN MILES YOUNGBLOOD, JR. and his wife MARY.  Judge Youngblood died January 15, 1860 in Marion Co., MS.  On December 20, 1794 in Richmond Co., G
2 CONC A he married SUSANNAH COLLINS, born May 16, 1775 in Barnwell Co., SC.  She died November 19, 1866 at China Grove, MS.  Susannah was the daughter of MOSES COLLINS, SR. and his wife HANNAH (WILLIS) COLLINS.
2 CONT
2 CONT On August 8, 1801 ABRAHAM YOUNGBLOOD bought 124 acres of land on Little Kiokee Creek in Columbia Co., GA from his father JOHN YOUNGBLOOD.  This land abutted the lands of BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD and JACOB YOUNGBLOOD.  One JACOB YOUNGBL
2 CONC OOD had previously acted as bondsman in the marriage of Benjamin and Susannah, he and ABRAHAM YOUNGBLOOD were likely brothers of Benjamin.
2 CONT
2 CONT About two years after his marriage, on December 14, 1796, BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD purchased 300 acres of land on Spirit Creek in Richmond Co., GA.  This land was very near his father-in-law MOSES COLLINS and was about 11 or 12 miles S
2 CONC E of Augusta, GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT By February 8, 1808 Benjamin had sold off his lands in Columbia and Richmond counties and had purchased 202 acres in what was then Wilkinson Co., GA (now Laurens Co.).  He was there for a short time and sold his land on October 23
2 CONC , 1811.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the following month on November 13, 1811, a passport was issued by the governor of GA for passage through the Indian Nations, and reads as follows: “fo Messrs. BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD and JOHN POLLOCK (some think this is “BULLOCK”)
2 CONC , the former with his wife, seven children, and five negroes, all from the County of Laurens in this state.
2 CONT
2 CONT In December of 1812 when the organization of the County of Jackson MS Territory took place, four officers of the Mobile 14th Regiment were brought in to the 17th Regiment in Jackson Co., MS.  They were LT. BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD and 
2 CONC ENS. LARD WARE, BENJAMIN WILLIAMSON, and WILLIAM MILLS.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first civil officers of Jackson Co. were THOMAS BILBO, JAMES WARE, WHEELER GRESHAM, BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD and ROBERT WILLIAMSON, justices of the quorum court; MALCOLM MONROE, GEORGE DAVIS, and MOSES COLLINS justices of the peace
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1812 the civil officers of Mobile County were WHEELER GRESHAM, NOEL JOURDAN and ROBERT WILLIAMSON, justices of the quorum court; GEORGE DAVIS and BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD, justices of the peace.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three years later, it was time for Benjamin to move on.  On January 19, 1815 he signed a petition to Congress by the inhabitants of Marion and Lawrence Counties, Mississippi Territory.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the year 1816 BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD was listed in the Pike Co., MS Census, and on February 26, 1816 he was appointed Constable in Pike Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally, after many years of moving about, BENJAMIN and SUSANNAH YOUNGBLOOD found a permanent home in Marion Co., MS.  On February 20, 1819 BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD was appointed Justice of the Quorum for Marion Co., MS, a position he 
2 CONC held until late 1822.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his tenure as Quorum Justice, BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD concentrated on the development  of his plantation, which lay about 2 miles SE of the China Grove Church.  It was on this plantation that BENJAMIN and SUSANNAH YOUNGBLOOD wer
2 CONC e finally laid to rest, their graves having been discovered some years back by IRMA LAMPTON, wife of WILLIAM LAMPTON, a Youngblood descendant.  At the time of the discovery, the land was owned by MARGARET GRAVES.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following are the children of BENJAMIN and SUSANNAH YOUNGBLOOD:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. HENRY YOUNGBLOOD b. 12 Sept 1795 Richmond Co., GA  d. 2 June 1860 De Soto Parish, LA +SARAH HARVEY b. 12 May 1801 Warren Co., GA
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. HILLARY YOUNGBLOOD          b. 10 Sept 1797  Richmond Co., GA
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. ALBERT YOUNGBLOOD b. 11 Jan 1800  Richmond Co., GA  d. unknown Said to have married Lillian Toney, Daughter of William M. and Mary Toney.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  NANCY ANN YOUNGBLOOD      b. 5 April 1802  Richmond Co., GA  d. 30 Sept 1872  Scott Co., MS m. 23 Feb 1823  Marion Co., MS +CHARLES FRANKLIN TONEY  b. ca. 1796 MS Terr.? d. 1840-1850 Scott Co., MS Charles and Nancy Toney are b
2 CONC uried in the Bishop Cemetery (now called the Walker Cemetery) on the old Algie Bishop farm at Morton MS.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  LUCY ANN YOUNGBLOOD b. 8-04-1804  Richmond Co., GA d. 11-18-1887 Pike Co., MS m. 2 Feb 1824 +WILLIAM LAMPTON b. 2 Jan 1802  KY  d. 8 Oct 1868 Pike Co., MS
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.  VESTA ANN YOUNGBLOOD       b. 12 Feb 1807  Richmond Co., GA d.  17 Dec1872  Washington Parish LA +JAMES KENT    b. unknown   d. unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. HANNAH ANN YOUNGBLOOD b. 27 Sept 1808  Laurens Co., GA  d. 25 Mar 1885  Amite Co., MS m. 11 June 1830 +JESSE BRUMFIELD b.  12 Mar 1807  SC d.  25 July 1884  Amite Co., MS Both buried in Andrews Cemetery just east of Liberty, Am
2 CONC ite Co., MS.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. BENJAMIN YOUNGBLOOD, JR. b. 11 June 1811 Laurens Co., GA   died young 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. JOSEPH YOUNGBLOOD b. 25 Dec 1812  Marion Co., MS d.  16 Sept 1886 China Grove, Pike Co., MS +ELIZA BICKHAM b. 1 Sept 1822 Washington Parish, LA d.  28 July 1869 China Grove, Pike Co., MS
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. SUSANNA YOUNGBLOOD b. 13 May 1815  China Grove, Pike Co., MS d. 3 Mar-1882 +JOHN SIBLEY  b. unknown d. unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. REBECCA YOUNGBLOOD b.  6 Feb 1819  China Grove, Pike Co., MS d.  3 Mar 1819  China Grove, Pike Co., MS  (died young)
2 CONT
2 CONT Parts of this sketch were taken from American Shoots From the Baskerville Family by the late Reba Holmes Brown.  This book has been out of print for many years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.msmarion.com/youngbloodjudge.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=98443667
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT NOT the son of Thomas S. Youngblood and Amy Hopkins.
2 CONT
