2 CONT
2 CONT John Carroll House aka Hows Born 10 Jun 1776 in Wake County, North Carolina, USAmap Son of [father unknown] and [mother unknown] according to a Wiki Tree by MG Pitts. [sibling(s) unknown] Husband of Susan Penelope (King) House, Ho
2 CONC ws — married 11 Nov 1803 in NCmap Husband of Minerva (Rudy) House — married 21 Jun 1851 in Trigg Co., KYmap Father of Elizabeth (Hows) Pitts, Horatio Rasa Hows, Catherine (Hows) Pitts, Brinkley Hows, Squire John Hows and	Loruhamah
2 CONC  House Died 8 Dec 1855 in Trigg County, Kentucky, USAmap Profile manager: MG Pitts private message [send private message] House-45 created 22 Sep 2010 | Last modified 26 Nov 2014 (This page has been accessed 399 times. {Mar. 2 201
2 CONC 7})
2 CONT
2 CONT Categories: Wake County, North Carolina | Trigg County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John House came to Tenn. in 1814 from Wake Co. NC, near Raleigh. They came with others and entered a tract of land north of the Harpeth River at what later became known as Liberty Grove Methodist Church and still later Buffalo Met
2 CONC hodist Church. The Buffalo School was on the same land. John C. gave them the land with the understanding that if the church folded he would get the land back. When the Church folded years later his heirs received the money. On No
2 CONC v. 16, 1814 he purchased 209 Acres of land on Sams Creek, from James Lovell for $1,000 and the deed was filed May 3 1816 in Davidson Co. I have found many more land transactions for him but the one on Sams Creek was were my father
2 CONC  said he made his home. They were the parents of six children. I think John C had a brother named Warren and one named William. I have no proof. I also believe he was born in NC and his father was either James or Thomas House who 
2 CONC were early settlers in Wake Co. again no proof.
2 CONT
2 CONT John C. House appears on the 1820 Census of Davidson Co. TN. On the 1840, the only House's listed were John, Racey, and Brinkley. This John is the Squire John. and not John C. I could not find a second John listed. I find that Bri
2 CONC nkley went to Trigg Co..Ky. when checking him out I found a John C. House. I also found John C. on the 1840 Census of Trigg Co. Ky. so he went to Kentucky before Brinkley since Brinkley was in Davidson Co. in 1840. I did not find 
2 CONC John C. on either 1830 Census it could mean he was living with one of his children since by then he was already selling his land in Davidson County.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name House was the way the name was spelled in North Carolina, and it appears that the son's of John C. changed the way the named is spelled to Hows. The reason will probably always remain a mystery to his descendants. It also
2 CONC  seems that John C. finally changed his spelling of the name to Hows also, the reason being that on the deeds of the land he sold he had to sign the documents and they have it spelled Hows. The Hows- House men seemed to have been 
2 CONC able to write so I don't believe the change was an accident.
2 CONT
2 CONT John C. House lived in Linton, Trigg Co., KY on the Cumberland River.
2 CONT
