1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary was born about _____ , presumably England.
2 CONT
2 CONT As "Mary Lovett," she was among 20 admitted to the Salem church in 1650, and on 1 : 7 : 1650, baptisms at the church included, "Simon, Joseph & Mary chs of Sister Levett."[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lovett-497
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife is seen as Mary Grant without supporting evidence.  The children of John Lovett and Mary were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Lovett [Jr.], born, probably England, say 1638 (he was about age 32[23] in 1669, and about age 40[24] in 1678); married Bethiah Rootes 
2 CONT # Simon Lovett.  Married Agnes Sweetland.
2 CONT # Joseph Lovett. Married  Elizabeth Solart
2 CONT # Mary Lovett, probably born Mackerel Cove, then Salem (now Beverly), before 1643 (she was "above 80" at the time of her death in 1723); died Wenham, Essex County, 26 September 1723.[25] She married Thomas Patch, as his 1st or 2nd
2 CONC  wife ...
2 CONT # Bethia Lovett, probably Mackerel Cove, probably after 8 September 1650, baptized Salem, 13 June 1652;[26] died Beverly, before 25 July 1706; (date administration granted on estate of George Standley).[27] married before 18 July 
2 CONC 1698, George Standley.[28]
2 CONT # Abigail Lovett, probably born Mackerel Cove, 20 August 1654,[29] baptized Salem, 18 March 1655;[30] died, probably Mackerel Cove, 27 May 1659.[31]
2 CONT # Abigail Lovett, probably born Mackerel Cove, after 27 May 1659 (date sister of the same name died); married, probably Beverly, before 1684, Issac Randall, probably born at England, who died of Beverly before 23 April 1684.[32] A
2 CONC bigail probably married (2) about 1686, Thomas Woodbury, and then (3) Thomas Larcum as his second wife. Abigail may be the widow of Thomas Larkum who died Beverly between June and August, 1740.[33]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Lovett was at different periods, surveyor of highways, constable and selectman. By his Will, dated Nov. 8, 1686, it appears he held much real estate, which was devised principally to his children, John, Joseph, Abigail, Mary
2 CONC , Bethiah, and his grandson, George Stanley. He bequeathed a set of cooper's tools to his son, John, and also 20 acres of land on the east side of "dirty hole" lying between the lands of his son, Joseph, and his son-in-law George 
2 CONC Stanley. This land, now so valuable, is on the east side of Cabot St. somewhere between the South meeting house and the bank. M r Lovett's wife, Mary, was admitted to the Salem church Sept. 1, 1650 and.was one of the petitioners f
2 CONC or the forma- tion of the church in Beverly.
