1 NAME Mary /Lovett/
2 GIVN Mary
2 SURN Lovett
2 _MARNM Patch
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1643
2 ADDR
3 CITY Salem
3 STAE Massachusetts Bay Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 28 MAR 1707
2 ADDR
3 CITY Beverly
3 STAE Massachusetts Bay Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lovett-2048
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mary Lovett''' was born. probably Mackerel Cove, then Salem (now Beverly), Essex County, Massachusetts Bay Colony, say about 1645 (assums she was 21 or 22 at the date of marriage), the daughter of John Lovett and Mary _____. To
2 CONC gether with her brothers Simon and Joseph, Mary was baptized at Salem, 8 : 7 : 1650 [8 September 1650].[1] She died, probably Beverly, before 28 March 1707.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, probably Mackerel Cove, then Salem (now Beverly), say about 1667 (baptism of two children, July 1668), Thomas Patch. He was born about 1638,[3] died in Beverly, 28 September 1711,[4][5] the son of Nicholas Patch and h
2 CONC is wife, Elizabeth Owsley.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Mary (Lovett) Patch were the parents of at least three children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas Patch (Jr.), baptized Beverly, 19 July 1668.[12] Died Beverly, 16 Mar 1747.  Was his widow  Eliza?
2 CONT # William Patch, baptized Beverly, 19 July 1668.[13].  Died Beverly,  1 Nov 1742.  Married Eleanor (unknown).  
2 CONT # James Patch, baptized Beverly, 31 March 1678.[14].  Died Beverly, 1 Apr 1757.  Married Rebekah "Rebecca" Biles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Mary (Lovett) Patch became members of the new Beverly church shortly after its formation.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Patch most  likely married two women named Mary--(1) to Mary Scott by 1666 (first child, Sarah, is said baptized 08 December 1666, Wenham) and (2) to Mary Lovett.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>No, they were two different Thomas Patches.  Thomas Patch (d. 1721 at Wenham) married Mary Scott.  Thomas Patch (d. 1711 at Beverly) married Mary Lovett.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Stearns, Ezra S. Genealogical and Family History of the State of New Hampshire (Lewis Publishing Company, 1908) Vol. 2, Page 621 "was born in Salem Massachusetts in 1640. Savage mentions him as Thomas of Wenham and the year of hi
2 CONC s birth about 1638. He was made freeman in 1670 and representative in 1679. His wife was Mary A. Lovett (Savage says Scott) of Ipswich Massachusetts, daughter of Thomas Lovett, and among their children were Thomas, James, Stephen,
2 CONC  Isaac, Ephraim, Timothy, Simeon, Sarah, and Marah(Mariah)."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Space:Essex_County_contemporaries%2C_both_Thomas_Patch “Essex County contemporaries, both Thomas Patch”]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1707 deeds'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Patch Sr''' (yeoman) to '''James Patch''', deed dated 28 March 1707, "Massachusetts Land Records, 1620-1986"; images, FamilySearch ([https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L9ZZ-18H1?i=91&cc=2106411&cat=209907 i
2 CONC mage 92 of 605]), otherwise Essex County, Massachusetts, Deeds 38:84, recorded 17 May 1718; refers "Land Lying … in ye Township of Beverly … Containing about one Acre … one which my Dwellilng House now Standeth … bounded Westerly 
2 CONC with ye Town Highway & Southerly by ye meadow formerly Ensign John Patch's now in possession of his Son Benjamin Patch & Easterly by ye ten acres of Land '''given to my late wife Mary by her father Lovits''' Last Will and Testamen
2 CONC t."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Patch Junr''' & '''William Patch''' to '''James Patch''', deed dated 28 March 1707, "Massachusetts Land Records, 1620-1986"; images, FamilySearch ([https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-99ZZ-18V2?i=92&cc=21064
2 CONC 11&cat=209907 image 93 of 605]), otherwise Essex County, Massachusetts, Deeds 38:84, recorded 17 May 1718; refers to "Land ... given to our Hon'd Mother Mary Patch of Beverly ... Deceast as by our '''sd Grandfathrs''' Last will & 
2 CONC Testament."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *http://smithharper.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/BethiaLovett.pdf
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lovett-2048 cites 
2 CONT # Simon, Joseph & Mary Levett, 1650 baptisms in church register, Thomas Barnard (pastor), compiler, Records of the First Church of Salem, Mass. [1629-1843] (manuscript, bound volume), image 144; digital images, Congressional Libra
2 CONC ry and Archives, notes "copied from the original ..." and "the original manuscripts are owned by ... Phillips Library at the Peabody Essex Museum.
2 CONT # Thomas Patch Sr to James Patch, deed dated 28 March 1707, "Massachusetts Land Records, 1620-1986"; images, FamilySearch (image 92 of 605), otherwise Essex County Deeds 38:84, recorded 17 May 1718; refers to "Land given to my lat
2 CONC e wife Mary by her father Lovits Last Will and Testament."
2 CONT # George Francis Dow, Records and Files of the Quarterly Courts of Essex County, Massachusetts, 9 vols. (Salem, Mass. : Essex institute, 1911-1975), 6:348-349 at 349 (Court Held at Salem, 27 : 9 mo.: 1677 [27 November 1677]; digit
2 CONC al image, Hathi Trust, in the matter of Tho. Woodbery v. Richard Stackhouse regarding a length of sail, for "Thomas Patch, aged about thirty-nine years, deposed that Woodbury said he had taken out about thirty yards from the sale 
2 CONC for other uses. Sworn in Court."
2 CONT # Thomas Patch, sr., death entry, citing "C.R. 1. [church record, First Parish Unitarian Church]," Vital Records of Beverly, Massachusetts, to the end of the year 1849, 2 vols. (1906-1907) 2:523 (Patch); digital images, Hathi Trus
2 CONC t.
2 CONT # Thomas Patch 1711 death notation, William P. Upham, Records of the First Church in Beverly, Massachusetts, 1667-1772 (Salem, Mass., Essex Institute, 1905), 39; digital images, Hathi Trust.
2 CONT # John and Thomas Patch, "Massachusetts Land Records, 1620-1986"; images, FamiySearch, img. 77-78; deed index reports this as Essex (Mass.) Deeds 4:47.
2 CONT #  William P. Upham, Records of the First Church in Beverly, Massachusetts, 1667-1772 (Salem, Mass., Essex Institute, 1905), 11; digital images, Hathi Trust.
2 CONT # William P. Upham with annotations by Augustus A. Galloupe, Records of the First Church in Beverly, Massachusetts, 1667-1772 (Salem, Mass., Essex Institute, 1905), 86; digital images, Hathi Trust. Note: editors of NEHG Register h
2 CONC ave found Galloupe's annotations to be "often incorrect," see Errata.
2 CONT # William P. Upham with annotations by Augustus A. Galloupe, Records of the First Church in Beverly, Massachusetts, 1667-1772 (Salem, Mass., Essex Institute, 1905), 94; digital images, Hathi Trust. Note: editors of NEHG Register h
2 CONC ave found Galloupe's annotations to be "often incorrect," see Errata.
2 CONT # John and Thomas Patch, "Massachusetts Land Records, 1620-1986"; images, FamiySearch, img. 77-78; deed index reports this as Essex (Mass.) Deeds 4:47.
2 CONT #  John Lovet 1686 Will (image), citing "Probate records v. 12-12 1657-1697," "Suffolk County (Massachusetts) probate records, 1636-1899"; digital images, FamilySearch; transcript at Eugene Tappan, "Essex County Estates Administer
2 CONC ed in Suffolk County, Prior to 1701," Essex Institute Historical Collections, multiple vols. 40 (1904): 215; digital images, Internet Archive, cites "Docket, No. 1523."
