1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Parents: John Parker, II (1560–1613), Joanne Whytear (1562–1608). Spouse & Children: Jane Kember (1591–1620).
2 CONT     Thomas Parker b.1609;
2 CONT     James Parker (1617–1700);
2 CONT     John Parker, IV (1620–1686). According to Holmes' ''Directory of the Ancestral Heads of New England Families, 1630-1700'', Robert Park was born c. 1601/2 in Wollpit or Wollpitt, Bury St Edmonds, Suffolk, England to unknown par
2 CONC ents.  In 1634, he arrived in Boston, and in 1635, he married Judith (unknown surname); some sources reverse the order.  All sources agree that he was a butcher.  He is variously listed as having died on May 8, 1682 or April 17, 1
2 CONC 685 in Cambridge, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to ''Genealogy of the Parke Families of Connecticut'', Robert Parker of Wollpitt's first wife was Martha Chaplin or Chaplyn, sister of a Clement Chaplin, and she was the mother of all of his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT At this point, due to conflicting accounts and no readily available primary source documents, it seems that the only safe conclusion is that he existed, and that pertinent details related to his parentage, his wife, his date of bi
2 CONC rth, and his date of death are surmised.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Holmes, Frank R.  ''Directory of the Ancestral Heads of New England Families, 1620-1700''.  1923.
2 CONT * Parks, Frank Sylvester.  ''Genealogy of the Parke Families of Connecticut''.  Washington, D.C.: Private printing, 1906. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
