1 OCCU Minister, Deacon, Blacksmith
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He was a minister
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 3869. DEACON JOHN FOSTER (Thomas, Thomas), b. Oct. 7, 1642. in Weymouth, Mass., m. abt. 1663, Mary, dau. of Thomas Chillingsworth, of Marshfield, whod. Sept. 25, 17o2. He m., 2d, Sarah Thomas, Dec. 3o, 17o2. Was a blacksmith; sele
2 CONC ctman in 169o; was elected deacon April 6, 17oo, and ordained July 2o, 17o1. His death is recorded in Marsbfield thus: "Deacon John Foster deceased June the 13 day 1732 in the 91 year of his age and left 7 living children, 45 gran
2 CONC dchildren and 83 G. Grandchildren and had 26 G. children die before himself." Sarah died May 26, 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was the daughter of Thomas Chillingsworth who was first known as an inhabitant of Lynn, Mass., in 1637. He lived a short time in Lynn, removed to Sandwich and thence to Marshfield, where he settled. Was representative to Gene
2 CONC ral Court from Marshfield in 1648 and 1652. He died early in 1653. Administration
2 CONT
2 CONT of his estate was granted March, 1653. to his widow, Joanna , who m., 2d, May
2 CONT
2 CONT 17, 1654, Thomas Doggett, and was buried in Marshfield, Sept. 4, 1684. His children
2 CONT
2 CONT were: 1. Elizabeth, b. ;d. unm. Sept. 28, 1665. 2. Mehitable. b. ;m.
2 CONT
2 CONT Justus Earns, of Marshfield, May 2, 1661. 3. Mary, b. ;Deacon John Foster.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Sarah, b. ;m. Samuel Sprague, the last secretary of Plymouth Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT His gravestone, as well as that of his second wife, and his daughter Deborah, is still to be seen in the old graveyard at Marshfield. It is said he resided near South river, on lands inherited from Thomas Chillingsworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will—In the name of God amen I Sarah Foster wife to John Foster of Marshfield in ye County of Plymouth in ye Province of ye Massachusetts Bay in New England ye 2oth day of May anno-Domini 1731 Being very sick and weak in body but 
2 CONC of sound mind and memory and being desirous to settle what Estate I have Do make and ordain this my last will and Testament in manner and form following that is to say I Commend my soul to God my Creator and my body to ye Earth fr
2 CONC om whence it was taken to be buried in Decent Christian burial and as To such worldly goods and Estate and money and all whatsoever sort of Estate that shall anywise appear to be mine my mind & will is that ye same shall be imploy
2 CONC ed & disposed as followeth:
2 CONT
2 CONT That is to say I give and bequeath unto my Cousin John Balston my Cobirons. Item I give and bequeath unto Nehemiah Herrindon ye Lad which liveth with us that black heifer that is Called mine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give and bequeath all ye Remainder of my Estate whatsoever it is or of what sort forever it may be that appeareth to be mine unto my Cousin John Balston my Cousin mary Stetson and to my son in law Thomas Foster and to my d
2 CONC aughter in law Deborah Foster to be Equally divided between ye sd John Balston Mary _ - — ^
2 CONT
2 CONT Stetson Thomas Foster Deborah Foster and Lastly I do hereby Constitute & appoint my son in law Thomas Foster to be sole Executor of this my last will & testament, in witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand & seal ye day and ye
2 CONC ar above written
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed and declare by ye sd Sarah Foster to be her last will & testament in ye presence of her ) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Howland Sarah X Foster [ Seal
2 CONT
2 CONT William Howland mark )
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur Howland
2 CONT
2 CONT June the 23: 1731 The within named Robert Howland William Howland and Arthur Howland made oath that they saw the Within Named Sarah Foster Late of Marshfield in the County of Plymouth deceased signe seal and heard her declare the 
2 CONC within Written to be her last will and Testament and that they at the same time in the presence of the Testator set to their hands as Witnesses: and that according to the best of their observation she then was of a sound and dispo
2 CONC sing mind and memory.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before Isaac Winslow Judge of Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT Children born Marshfield:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3898. i. ELIZABETH, b. Sept . 24, 1664; m. William Carver, of Marshfield,
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan. 18, 1682-3. He was the centenarian. She d. June. 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3899. ii. JOHN, b. Oct. 12, 1666; m., 1692, Hannah Stetson, of Scituate.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3900. iii. JOSIAH, b. June 7, 1669; m. Sarah, dau. of Samuel Sherman, of
2 CONT
2 CONT Marshfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3901. iv. MARY, b. Sept. 13, 1671; m. John Hatch, of Marshfield, Dec. 30,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1606. She died April 3, 1750.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3902. v. JOSEPH, b. abt. 1674; m., Sept. 8, 1696, Rachel Bassett, of Sand
2 CONT
2 CONT wich.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3903. vi. SARAH, b. abt . 1677; d. April 7, 1702; m. Nathan Thomas: m.,
2 CONT
2 CONT 2d, Jedediah Bourne. Res., Plymouth, Mass. ,3904. vii. CHILLINGSWORTH, b. July 11, 1680; m. Mercy Freeman. _
2 CONT
2 CONT 3905. viii. JAMES, b. May 22, 1683; i. July 21, 1683.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3906. ix. THOMAS, b. 1n 1686; m. Faith (Oakman), widow of Benjamin
2 CONT
2 CONT White.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3907. x. DEBORAH, b. abt . 1691; d unm., Nov. 4, 1732.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will—The 10th day of July 1732. In ye name of God amen I Deborah Foster of Marshfield in the County of Plymouth in ye Province of ye Massachusetts in New England Being very weak & infirm of body but of perfect sound mind & memory 
2 CONC & Calling to mind the uncertainty of this Life & being desirous to settle things in order do make & ordain this my Last will & Testament in manner & form following viz: princ1pally I Commend my soul to God my Creator & my body to 
2 CONC ye Earth from whence it was taken to be buried in such decent manner as to my Executors hereafter named shall be thought most meet and Convenient and as to such worldly goods & Estate as ye Lord in mercy hath lent me my mind & w1l
2 CONC l is that ye same shall be employed & disposed of as in this my will 1s Expressed, that is to say—I give & bequeath unto my brother Thomas Foster my best feather bed one Coverled a blanket & apair of sheets & my goldneck lace and 
2 CONC my still & one half of all my silver money.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my sister Mary Hatch my best suit of Clothes & my best lace Cap my new bedticking my silk scarf and my new s1lk gloves & my new silk hood and ye other half of all my silver money.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath unto my Cousin Mary Mackfarland my oldest feather bed a coverled & blanket and a pair of sheets Item I give unto my Cousin Sarah Tailer Th1rty shillings in money or good Bills of Credit on sd Province. Ite
2 CONC m I gi%-e unto my Cousin Millicent Carver my Gold locket Item I give unto my sister Mary Hatch my Cousin Mary Stand1sh my Cousin Mary Mackfarland and my Cousin El1zabeth Tailer all ye Remainder of my wairing apparrel that is not a
2 CONC bove disposed of to be equally divided amongst them four. Item I g1ve all ye Remainder of my moveable Estate and all ye money which is due to me by bonds or bills that shall be
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John Foster  was born 7 Oct 1642 in Weymouth Norfolk MA. He died 13 Jun 1732 in Marshfield  Plymouth MA 	and was buried in Old Winslow Cemetery Marshfield. John married Mary Chillingworth  in MA. Three months after her 	death, he 
2 CONC married 2) Sarah Thomas (30 Dec 1702)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Savage Genealogical Dictionary:  JOHN, Marshfield, s. of Thomas of 	Weymouth, m. Mary, d. of Thomas Chillingworth, had Elizabeth b. 1664; John, 	1666; Josiah, 1669; Mary, 1671; Sarah; Chillingworth; James, 1683, d. soon; 	and
2 CONC  Thomas, 1686. His w. d. 1702, and sec. w. Sarah d. 1731, as did he, 13 	June 1732.
