1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Williams-27946
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 15 Dec 2021 | Created 3 Dec 2014
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Thomas Williams Jr. (1664 - 1723)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Thomas Williams Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 9 Apr 1664 in Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Thomas Williams Sr. and Anne (UNKNOWN) Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Thomas Williams, Charles Williams and Susanna Williams
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Sarah (Foster) Williams — married 22 Sep 1686 in Stow, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Joseph Williams, Thomas Williams III, Anna Williams, Anna Williams, Isaiah Williams and Sarah Williams
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 23 Feb 1723 in Plainfield, Windham, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Williams birth is entered as 9 Apr 1664 in Boston, MA[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Sarah Foster (daug of Dr. Thomas Foster & Sarah Parker), Sept 22, 1686, Stow, Middlesex County, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime after 1690, Thomas Williams moved from Stow, MA to land east of the Quinnebaug River which was purchased from the Winthrops. In May of 1699, approx. thirty families petitioned Gov. Jonathan Winthrop to incorporate the dis
2 CONC puted Quinebaug Plantation, which included land on both sides of the Quinebaug River, into the town of Plainfield. Thomas was chosen surveyor. Thomas also served on a committee to treat with the Reverand Mr. Coit to be their minis
2 CONC ter. In 1702, he was elected to keep a house of public entertainment on the east side of the Quinnebaug. In 1703, colonists living on the western banks of the river separated to settle what is now the town of Canterbury. The const
2 CONC ruction of roads during the 1700's from Providence to Norwich which ran through Plainfield made the town an important trading post of surplus crops. In 1704, Thomas Williams was selected to be ensign of the Train Band of Plainfiel
2 CONC d, formed in response to the Indian Wars. By 1708, he was promoted to Lieutenant and in 1711 was promoted Captain.
2 CONT Ref. "A Gen. of Some of the Des. of William Williams of Salem, MA", Geo. E. Williams, 1987, p. 6-7.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family of Thomas and Sarah from the Plainfield, CT Vital Records[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas, Capt., d. Feb. 3, 1722/3, in the 58th y. of his age; 1; 27
2 CONT Sarah, w. Capt. Thomas, d. Aug. 8, 1751; 2; 20
2 CONT Thomas, s. Thomas & Sarah, b. July 19, 1677; 1; 12 [prob should be 1787]
2 CONT Ebenezer, s. Thomas & Sarah, b. May 28, 1693; 1; 12
2 CONT Anna, d. Thomas & Sarah, b. June 30, 1696; d. Aug. 4, 1696; 1; 12
2 CONT Anna, d. Thomas & Sarah, b. Dec. 12, 1697; d. Feb. 22, 1698; 1; 12
2 CONT Joseph, s. Thomas & Sarah, b. Oct. 28, 1679; 1; 12
2 CONT Nathan, s. Thomas & Sarah, b. May 13, 1699; 1; 12
2 CONT Nathan, s. Tho(ma)s & Sarah, d. June 2, 1720, age 21 y. 21 d.; 1; 22
2 CONT Isaiah, s. Thomas & Sarah, b. Nov. 5, 1701; 1; 12
2 CONT Isaiah, m. Deb(o)ra(h) Billings, Aug. 8, 1725; 1; 56
2 CONT Sarah, d. Thomas & Sarah, b. Dec. 6, 1704; 1; 12
2 CONT Elizabeth, d. Thomas & Sarah, b. Aug. 25, 1707; 1; 12
2 CONT Birth and parentage[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Sarah Foster[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death must occurred about 9 months to the birth of his youngest known child, Elizabeth.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was born about 1632.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ another Thomas Williams was born Jul 19 1677 in Plainfield, CT ("Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F74Y-B57), but it's unlikely that this Plainsfield
2 CONC  CT birth is his because he came from Massachusetts and married in Massachusetts.
2 CONT ↑ http://www.ctgenweb.org/county/cowindham/records/barbour/barbourplainfieldwxyz.htm
2 CONT ↑ "Massachusetts Births and Christenings, 1639-1915", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FHYM-41M : 15 January 2020), Thomas Williams, 1664.
2 CONT ↑ "Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001," database with images, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FCSH-LZT : 10 November 2020), Thomas Williams, 22 Sep 1686; citing Marriage, Stow, M
2 CONC iddlesex, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, Massachusetts Secretary of the Commonwealth, Boston; FHL microfilm 004198966.
2 CONT ↑ "Connecticut, Vital Records, Prior to 1850," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QP7L-G3G4 : 21 September 2019), Elizabeth Williams, ; citing Birth, , Compiled by Lucius A. and Lucius B. Barbour, hous
2 CONC ed at State Library, Hartford, Connecticut; FHL microfilm 008100622.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Plainfield, CT vital records
2 CONT The New England Historical & Genealogical Register, 1847-2011, Ancestry.com
