1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Williams served as a United States Representative in 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Williams-24706
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Joseph Williams''', son of Thomas and Sarah, born in Plainfield, Connecticut 28 Oct 1679. This Joseph married in Plainfield, 13 Oct 1710, Susannah Lawrans, d. Peleg of Grotton.[2] It is in Plainfield that his children were born
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Plainfield May 1, 1752 the last will and testament of Joseph Williams of Plainfield - beloved wife Susannah, four sons Samuel, Nathan, Eliheu, Ebenezer, daughter Elizabeth Butts and husband Josiah, daughter Susannah Parrish. Eldes
2 CONC t son Samuel was executor. This will was presented in court June 8 1752.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth, daughter of Joseph and Susanna, was born 16 Oct 1711[2]
2 CONT # Joseph, son of Joseph and Suesanna, was born 18 April 1713; d. 24 May 1713.[2]
2 CONT # Joseph, son of Joseph and Susanah, was born 17 June 1714. Joseph, son of Joseph and Susanah, died 10 May 1730.[2]
2 CONT # Samuel, son of Joseph and Susannah, was born 14 Nov 1717[2]
2 CONT # Nathan, son of Joseph and Susanah, was born 1 Mar 1722/3[2]
2 CONT # Elisha, son of Joseph and Susannah, was born 23 May 1725.[2] Called Elihu is his father's will
2 CONT # Anne, daughter of Joseph and Suesanna, was born 14 Aug 1728; d. 13 Sept 1728[2]
2 CONT # Elezer, son of Joseph and Suesanna, was born 8 Sep 1730; d. the same day[2]
2 CONT # Ebenezer, son of Joseph and Suesanna, was born 8 Sep 1730[2]
2 CONT # Susannah, daughter of Joseph and Suesannah, was born 28 Nov 1732; m. Ebenezer Parish 13 Feb 1752.[2]
