1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was born September 26, 1710 in Billerica, Middlesex County, Massachusetts.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, on January 8, 1735, Susanna Hill, who was the daughter of Samuel Hill.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived in Billerica until 1743, when his name disappears from the tax-list.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 27 March 1787, in Nova Scotia, Canada, at the age of 76, and was buried in Belleisle, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Patten-658
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Patten (1710 - aft. 1787)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Joseph Patten===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 26 Sep 1710 in Billerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Thomas Patten and Hannah (Foster) Patten
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Thomas Patten III and John Patten Sr
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Susanna Hill — married 8 Jan 1734 in Bellerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Lucy (Patten) Moody, Joseph Patten and Mehitable (Patten) Shaw
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 27 Mar 1787 at about age 76 in Granville Centre, Annapolis, Nova Scotia, Canada
2 CONT
