1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Attracted by generous colonization laws in Texas, Stanley Sr came to TX in 1834 with his wife and 3 kids (Stephen Jr, William Carrol, and Elizabeth) alongside Lorenzo de Zavala's Colony, with Alexander Johnson as h
2 CONC is sponsor.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Stephen Jefferson STANLEY Sr. Born in 1784 in South Carolina. Stephen Jefferson died in Tx. in 1835, he was 51. Buried in 1835 in Stanley Cemetery. Was on the census for Tombigbee area of Mississippi Territory in 1804. Was on the 
2 CONC census for Wayne Co. in 1811. Was on the census for Monroe Co., Alabama in 1830. Was on the census for Province of Texas, Republic of Mexico in 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Johnson sponsored Stephen L. Stanley to enter the Providence of Texas, Republic of Mexico, in 1835.   By 1835 Stephen and Elizabeth were in Texas where Stephen died shortly afterward.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research: Stephen Jefferson Stanley Sr., was born in South Carolina in 1784, migrated to the Mississippi Territory, then on to the Republic of Texas around 1824.  His sponsor was Mr. Alexander Johnson and he came as a colonist to 
2 CONC the Lorenzo De Zavalla Colony.  He was issued a Character Certificate in 1834 showing he was good, honest, and had a family.  He applied for a land grant and thus he was issued a Entrance Certificate on 28 Feb 1835.  His Mexican L
2 CONC and Grant was issued 27 Jun 1835 for 4432 acres of land or one league, situated in what is now the County of Angelina, State of Texas.  To this land he brought his wife Elizabeth "Huff" Stanley, born in South Carolina in 1784 and 
2 CONC two of his sons, Stephen Jefferson and William Carroll.  Other children born to this couple were Willaford and Green B.  Stephen Sr. was overseer on lots of road building in his area.  He died in 1835 shortly after getting settled
2 CONC  in Tx, and he is buried on the old farm place of his son William Carroll in a small community cemetery called Stanley Cemetery.  It is below Zavalla and behind the Kitchens Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research: 1801 Greene Co. Tax lists show Isaac (possibly a brother) and Stephen Stanley in Molton District.  On 1 Jan 1802, Nancy Hough married Isaac Stanley.  There is another partly torn entry believed to be that of Elizabeth to
2 CONC  Stephen Stanley, in the time period of 1800-1801.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1810 Wayne County, Mississippi Territory, census may show Samuel Huff. Washington County census shows James Barnes, Isaac Stanley, Stephen Stanley and Francis Huff.  Stephen Stanley was in the Tombigbee area until 1811.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1811 Samuel Huff and Stephen Stanley in Wayne County, Mississippi.  Isaac Stanley in Washington County.  By 1812, Francis Huff was in Wayne County, and Isaac Stanley was in Wayne County by 1813.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1814:  Francis Huff, Isaac Stanley, and Stephen Stanley were all on Buckatunna Creek in Wayne County.  They were probably in the same location through the state census of 1816.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1816 Wayne County, Mississippi Territory pre-state census shows Samuel Huff and wife, Francis Huff family, James Barnes family, and Isaac Stanley family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1830 Census:  Monroe County, Alabama, pg. 36, Stephen Stanley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilcox County, Alabama, pg. 186, Isaac Stanley.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1837 San Augustine Co., Texas, Stanley families, Stephen J. and Carroll.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1840 Census:  San Augustine or Nacogdoches Counties, Tx. Elizabeth Stanley with her youngest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Angelina Co., Texas census, Elizabeth Stanley.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 Angelina Co., Texas census, Elizabeth Stanley.
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 Nov 1803:  Samuel Huff was in the Tombigbee area of Mississippi Territory, signing petition requesting a separate territory for that area.  Stephen Stanley was in the Tombigbee area by 1804.  Francis Hough and Isaac Stanley arr
2 CONC ived in the area about 1804.  Francis Hough had moved from Greene County to Jackson County, Georgia, Phillips District by 1801.  Francis was still in the same District in 1802 when it became part of Clarke County.  Francis was in 
2 CONC the Tombigbee area of Mississippi Territory by 1805.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1805 Mississippi Territory Washington County tax list shows Samuel Huff, Francis Huff, Isaac Stanley and Stephen Stanley.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 31 Dec 1801 when Stephen Jefferson was 17, he married Elizabeth HUFF, daughter of Samuel HUFF & Sarah HIX, in Greene Co., Georgia. Born in 1784 in Georgia. Elizabeth died in Texas  aft 1860, she was 76. Was on the census for An
2 CONC gelina Co., Texas in 1860.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Stanley claimed a league of land in Wichita Co., Tx, and it became known as the Elizabeth Stanley grant.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 		i.	Peyton. Born in 1803 in Georgia or Alabama.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	2	ii.	Olive (1807-)
2 CONT
2 CONT 		iii.	Lucretia Bachiba. Born on 19 Jun 1810 in Washington Co., Miss Territory.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucretia Bachiba married John F. CHEAIRS Jr..
2 CONT
2 CONT 	3	iv.	Stephen Jefferson (1813-)
2 CONT
2 CONT 	4	v.	William Carroll (1820-1862)
2 CONT
2 CONT 	5	vi.	Green B. (1823-)
2 CONT
2 CONT 		vii.	Mary. Born in 1824 in Alabama.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married Jackson EDDINGS.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	6	viii.	Willaford
2 CONT
2 CONT Second Generation 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------
2 CONT
