2 CONT 4. William Carroll STANLEY. Born in 1820 in Alabama. William Carroll died in Tx. on 2 Feb 1862, he was 42. Buried in Zavalla Tx., Angelina Co. Was on the census for Angelina Co., Texas in 1860.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Carroll may have been married to Margaret McFaddin.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 9 Oct 1837 when William Carroll was 17, he first married Margaret Rebecca CHEAIRS, daughter of John F. CHEAIRS & Eleanor BIDDIX, in San Augustine Co., Tx. Born in 1820 in Hempstead Co, Arkansas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Background on Rebecca Cheairs:  Her family had a Coat of Arms originating back to 1600's.  It has been passed from family to family to family since 1630.  It was given to Baronet Cheairs.  Then Nathaniel Cheairs a Huguenot from Fr
2 CONC ance came from France through England and settled in Queen Anne, Kent County Maryland.  The Cheairs all came from him.  Our great great grandmother is a descendent of Nathaniel Cheairs.  The Coat of Arms stood for Superiority, Nob
2 CONC le Birth, and Luuxurity.  It came with a blood sacrifice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca is a sister to  Mary Ann Cheairs, the wife of Stephen Jefferson Stanley, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
