2 CONT 8. Stephen STANLEY. Born in 1839 in Tx. Stephen died on 21 Nov 1907, he was 68.
2 CONT
2 CONT Donaldsonville:  Ascension Parish, (Campaign) Taylor's Operations in West Louisisna (1863), (Date)  28 Jun 1863, (Principal Commanders)  Maj. Joseph D. Bullen; Brig. Gen. Tom Green
2 CONT
2 CONT Estimated Casualties:  324 total (US 23, CS 301).
2 CONT
2 CONT Description:  On 28 Jun 1863, Confederate Brig. Gen. Jean Alfred Mouton ordered Brig. Gen. Tom Green's and Col. James P. Major's brigades to take Donaldsonville.  The Union had built Fort Butler, which the Rebels had to take befor
2 CONC e occupying the town.  On the night of June 27, Green, within a mile and a half of the Fort, began moving troops ahead to attack.  The attack started soon after midnight, and the Confederated quickly surrounded the Fort and began 
2 CONC passing through the various obstructions.  Unfortunately, those troops attacking along the levee came to a ditch, unknown to them, too wide to cross, that saved the day for the Union garrison.  A Union gunboat, Princess Royal, cam
2 CONC e to the garrison's aid also and began shelling the attackers.  Futile Confederate assaults continued for some time but they eventually ceased their operations and retired.  This point on the Mississippi remained in Union hands an
2 CONC d many other Mississippi River towns were occupied by the Yankees:  the Confederated could harass but not eliminate these Union enclaves.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research: Stanley, LA is located in DeSoto Parish on Hwy. 84, between Mansfield and Logansport (which is right on the banks of the Sabine River).  The Sabine is the boundary between LA and TX.  The community was originally called 
2 CONC Oak Grove, but incorporated in the 1950's.  Stanley was chosen as the name of this town beacuse there were a number of families by that name in the area.  This is a very small town.  There is a sawmill in operation, one store, Mt.
2 CONC  Olivet Baptist Church with a pretty large cemetery adjacent, and a couple of smaller churches.  Stanley High School is across the highway from Mt. Olivet Baptist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Military: Company D. 7th Texas Cavalry.  Locations mentioned in the Confederate Pension Application are located in western Louisiana.  Ft. Butler was where the 7th TX Cavalry (aka 7th TX Mounted Volunteers) had a fight with Union 
2 CONC Troops in 1863.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibley's Brigade was an organization commanded by Brigadier General H.H. Sibley and made up of various units which were put under Sibley's command in 1861.
2 CONT
2 CONT This force moved into Arizona in 1861, had a few small encounters with Indians and some Union folks, and then moved from there into western Louisiana where they spent the rest of the war.  They participated all through the Red Riv
2 CONC er campaign, among others.
2 CONT
2 CONT It's more the rule than the exception that Confederate records--especially as the war progressed into 1864-65--are rather sketchy.  This tendency is even more pronounced for Confederate forces in the Trans-Mississippi, such as the
2 CONC  one in question.  Many records were lost or destroyed; others aren't there simply because units just plain quit keeping them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Military: S.L. Stanley found in the Broadfoots Roster of Confederate Soldiers in the 7th, Co. D.  No roster had been located for the unit.
2 CONT
2 CONT Company D. Angelina Troop:  Stationed at Alto, Cherokee County, Texas, 16 Sept 1861.  Angelina Troop rank and file seventy-eight, which is hereby tendered for General Sibley's Brigade.  If you have not received the five companies,
2 CONC  I would be proud to know that Angelina will be represented.  We are expecting to be able to move from this county two weeks from tomorrow.  I have the honor to be very respectfully your obedient servant.
2 CONT
2 CONT (signed) W.H. Cleaver
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain, Angelina Troop
2 CONT
2 CONT General Joseph Lewis Hogg, Rusk, Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT Stationed at Alto, Cherokee County, Texas, 16 Sept 1861
2 CONT
2 CONT I have the honor to report Captain W.H. Cleaver's Company of "Angelina Troops" Cavalry.  The muster roll whereof is hereto appended.  The service is (?) during the war, unless sooner discharged.  I have ordered them to march with 
2 CONC the greatest dispatch from Homer, Angelina County on or before (if possible, sooner) September 30 to San Antonio, Texas and then to report to General Sibley.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have the honor to be very respectfully your obedient servant,
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph L. Hogg,
2 CONT
2 CONT Aide-de-Camp
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifth District, Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT William Byrd,
2 CONT
2 CONT Adjutant-General, Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT Stationed at San Antonio, 9 Dec 1861
2 CONT
2 CONT October 24--Muster-in roll of Captain William H. Cleaver's Company, in the Third Regiment (Sibley's Brigade) of Texas Mounted Volunteers, commanded by Colonel William Steele, called into the service of the Confederate States by Br
2 CONC igadier General H.H. Sibley under the provisions of the Act of Congress passed 28 Feb 1861 by Brigadier General H.H. Sibley from 24 Oct 1861 (date of this muster) for the term of the war, unless sooner discharged...
2 CONT
2 CONT (signed) Thomas  C. Howard,
2 CONT
2 CONT Mustering Officer
2 CONT
2 CONT On 21 Nov 1865 when Stephen was 26, he married Margaret California HILL, daughter of Francis HILL & Sarah Margaret SANDERS, in Tyler Co., Texas. Born in 1849 in Texas. Margaret California died in San Augustine Co., Texas on 3 Nov 
2 CONC 1928, she was 79. Was on the census for Angelina Co., Texas in 1860.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Margaret California was known as a pistol packing mamma.  It is said that she wore a gun strapped around her waist.  This was probably the only way that she could protect her children.  Many of them probably would not have surviv
2 CONC ed".
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 		i.	Mary. Born on 10 May 1869.
2 CONT
2 CONT 		ii.	Frank. Born on 3 Apr 1871.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	29	iii.	William Presley. Born on 30 Jan 1873.
2 CONT
2 CONT 		iv.	Lemma. Born on 6 Feb 1875.
2 CONT
2 CONT 		v.	Francis Everline. Born on 3 Sep 1878.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aunt Evie
2 CONT
2 CONT 		vi.	Alice Lenora. Born on 11 Sep 1880.
2 CONT
2 CONT 		vii.	Maltie (Mattie). Born on 3 Aug 1882.
2 CONT
2 CONT 		viii.	Delphena. Born on 6 Jul 1884.
2 CONT
2 CONT 		ix.	General Lee. Born on 30 Nov 1886. Buried in Broaddus Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note received from Faye Heil:  Uncle Lee's name was definately General Lee.  He was quite a character.  Grand-daddy used to be the law - sherrif or constable - in the Broaddus area.  Uncle Lee would get drunk and climb onto the to
2 CONC p of the jail and threaten to jump off.  Gran-dad just let him go, and when he hit ground , he was arrested and got to sleep off his drunk in the jail.  He didn't think his own brother would put him in jail.  But, Grand-dad said h
2 CONC e did that many times.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many of these individuals are buried in the Broaddus Cemetery.  I think Uncle Lee and Aunt Ola, his wife, are buried there, as it Aunt Nora.
2 CONT
2 CONT General Lee married Ola UNKNOWN. Buried in Broaddus Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. William Hollis "Hawk" STANLEY. Born on 22 Dec 1852 in Tx. William Hollis "Hawk" died in Tx. on 5 Feb 1918, he was 65. Buried in Cochran Cemetery. Was on the census for Angelina Co., Texas in 1860.
