2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 OCT 1705
2 ADDR
3 CITY Braintree
3 STAE Massachusetts
1 OCCU Wheelwright
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edmund SHEFFIELD, son of Edmund Sheffield (d 1631) & Thomasine, was christened on 6 Aug 1612 in All Saint's, Sudbury, Suffolk, England.  Edmund settled in Braintree, Mass., where he died 13 Oct. 1705, "aged about 9
2 CONC 0 years". He had issue eleven (SIC: twelve) children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund married 3 times.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife, of whom nothing is known, probably died in England before he emigrated.  Their daughter was
2 CONT
2 CONT * Elizabeth, baptized at All Saint's in Sudbury, Suffolk, England on 12 March 1635/6.  She probably died young, as no record of her in New England has been found.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund married Mary WOODY, daughter of Richard WOODY, on 17 Apr 1644 in Roxbury, Essex Co., Mass.. Mary died 30 Mar 1662 in Braintree, Essex Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *       	11 	M 	i 	    	John SHEFFIELD was born 6 Mar 1644/1645 in Roxbury, Essex Co., Massachusetts and was christened 23 Mar 1645 in Roxbury, Essex Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT *       	12 	M 	ii 	    	Edmund SHEFFIELD was born 15 Dec 1646 in Braintree, Norfolk Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT *       	13 	F 	iii 	    	Ann SHEFFIELD was born 1 Apr 1649 in Braintree, Norfolk Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT *       	14 	F 	iv 	    	Mary SHEFFIELD was born 14 Jun 1653 in Braintree, Norfolk Co., Massachusetts. She died 7 Dec 1660 in Braintree, Norfolk Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT *       	15 	M 	v 	    	Matthew SHEFFIELD was born 26 May 1655 in Braintree, Norfolk Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT *       	16 	M 	vi 	    	Samuel SHEFFIELD was born 26 Nov 1657 in Braintree, Norfolk Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT *       	17 	F 	vii 	    	Sarah SHEFFIELD was born 6 Jun 1660 in Braintree, Norfolk Co., Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 5 September 1662 Edmund, at age 50, married Sarah Beal, daughter of John Beal of Hingham and Frances Ripley.1 She was the widow of Thomas Marsh of Hingham.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children 
2 CONT * Mary Sheffield (26 Jun 1663 - )
2 CONT * Nathaniel Sheffield (16 March  1664/5 - )
2 CONT * Deborah Sheffield (23 Jun 1667 - ).  Died at Braintree, 18 Jan 1690/1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From Sheffield, Daggett and Allied Families, by Mrs. George St. John Sheffield, page 13 & 14:
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was a wheelwright by trade, and in 1641 settled in Roxbury, MA.
2 CONT *          He was made a freeman, May 29 1644. About 1646 he removed to Braintree, where he was one of the first settlers, and served as selectman in 1677-78.
2 CONT *          He was admitted to the First Church of Roxbury before 1650.
2 CONT *          Married 1st in England, a wife whose name is unknown, and who probably died in England.
2 CONT *          Daughter Elizabeth, baptized at All Saints, Sudbury, EN Mar. 12, 1635-6, probably died in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund Sheffield died on Tuesday, 13 October 1705 in Braintree, Norfolk County, Massachusetts, at age 93 years, 1 month and 27 days.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Volumes 76-77. Genealogical Gleanings in England: [https://books.google.com/books?id=FpAeAQAAMAAJ&lpg=RA1-PA192&ots=S06hVx7Ogb&dq=thomasine%20sheffield&pg=RA1-PA192#v=onepage
2 CONC &q=thomasine%20sheffield&f=true page 192]
2 CONT * [http://genealogy.theroyfamily.com/p21555.htm  Ancestry of Robert Roy and Related Families - Edmund Sheffield]
