1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/12401266/william-davenport-justus
2 CONT
2 CONT William Davenport Justus, Jr., was born January 22, 1851, the son of William D. and Elizabeth Tabor Justus. His paternal grandparents were John Justus and Elizabeth Thomas. On December 8, 1872, he married Sarah Elizabeth Stepp, da
2 CONC ughter of Robert and Jane McMurray Stepp. William, Jr., came from a large family, having fifteen brothers and sisters, and eight half brothers and sisters. His father, William D. Justus, Sr., was elected sheriff of Henderson Count
2 CONC y in 1862 and served two terms during the time of the Civil War. Sheriff Justus was elected to the House of Representatives of North Carolina in 1868, and was one of the first Republican representatives in North Carolina.  William
2 CONC  D. Justus, Jr., was a successful farmer in the Blue Ridge area of Henderson County. William and Sarah Elizabeth reared a family of nine children. William died August 22, 1913 and Sarah Elizabeth died June 13, 1936. They are burie
2 CONC d in the churchyard of the Refuge Baptist Church in the Dana Community.
2 CONT --------------------
