1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geneajourney.com/spivey.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Spivey [a] b abt 1674, Upper Parish, Nansemond, VA, d bef 5 Feb 1729/30, Chowan, NC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He md Mary Hill 1692, Nansemond, VA. She was b abt 1675.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Thomas Spivey and Mary Hill were:
2 CONT # Thomas Spivey b abt 1693, Upper Parish, Nansemond, VA, d 1768; md Unknown Rountree
2 CONT # Benjamin Spivey b abt 1695, Upper Parish, Nansemond, VA, d 1760.
2 CONT # Jacob Spivey b abt 1697.
2 CONT # William Spivey b abt 1698, Upper Parish, Nansemond, VA, d 1765; md Margaret Corbitt.
2 CONT # Mary Spivey b abt 1700, Chowan, NC, d 10 Jan 1770; md William Hill.
2 CONT # Abraham Spivey b abt 1703.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems like there is some confusion about the parents of Thomas.  I believe Thomas is actually the son of Matthew and Judith, and that the previous father Matthew (wife Sarah) is actually his brother.  I've looked at many other 
2 CONC family trees of the same people and the majority shows Thomas being the son of Matthew and Judith.  The birth date is also likely incorrect, with many saying 1675 as the birth date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Found a link that shows this part of the family tree as well as parents George and Margaret. http://www.geneajourney.com/spivey.html
2 CONT
2 CONT In March of 1702, the area was beginning to be settled, and a group of settlers petitioned the North Carolina General Assembly, as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Petitioners have right to considerable tracts of land on Bennet’s Creyke now known as Caret’s Creyke via patents and conveyances.  Chowan Indians have their hunting quarters upon petitioners lands and pretend the land is theirs an
2 CONC d destroy the stock of the petitioners and burn their houses saying they are under the protection of the English and that no Englishman ought to seat within 4 miles of their town…we implore the Indians lands be laid out for them a
2 CONC ccoriding to the aforesaid order of coucill and if petitioners hold land within the limits it shall be diserted and left to the said Indians.  Signed by Benjamin Blanchard, John Campbell, '''Thomas Spivey''', Francis Rountree, Rob
2 CONC ert Rountree, Robert Lacitar, George Laciter, Nicholas Stallings.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/4:1:LJ18-F3F
2 CONT * http://www.geneajourney.com/spivey.html
