3 STAE Tennessee
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 JAN 1822
2 ADDR
3 STAE Alabama
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note: A transcription of the Orphans Court Record of Limestone County, Alabama, variously spells her name as KerenHappuch and as Karenhappuch. Family stories hold that Keranhappuch's last name was Nelson and that s
2 CONC he was a sister to Thomas Nelson, a Signer of the Declaration of Independence. The appearance of the name Nelson in her son John Nelson Biard's name gives some credence to that having been her maiden name; however, no documentary 
2 CONC evidence has as yet been discovered to prove or to refute this. A variation of this family legend as reported by Doris McCarty Fugler holds that John Nelson Biard's [maternal?] grandfather was Thomas Nelson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible reference: The book, "Miscellaneous Alabama Newspaper Abstracts, Vol. 2" by Michael Kelsey, et. al. includes the following entries from the Cahawba Press and Alabama State Intelligencer: p. 59 5 Oct 1822; List of letters 
2 CONC in the post office at Cahawba for the quarter ending the 30th September: John or James Baird, Henry Baird p. 69 11 Jan 1823; A list of letters remaining in the post office at Cahawba, for the quarter ending 31st January 1823: John
2 CONC  Beard, Robert Bard, Henry Beard p. 136 19 Mar 1825; State of Alabama, Dallas County, March term 1825, on the application of the administrator on the estate of Kerenhappech [?] Beard, deceased, having presented his accounts for al
2 CONC lowance and final settlement of said estate . . . .
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT E-mail from Jan Elaine Biard Thomas on 21 June 2000: I found Kerrenhappuch Beards will records, and guess what, it mentions practically everybody we know of, A. Waller (good enough proof to me about Aaron Waller), it mentions Thom
2 CONC as Morrison (good enough proof to me), William Blair, Henry Beard, William Gwinn (the unknown Gwinn), Welcome Beard, John Beard, George Beard, Archibald Beard, and probably some of the others we didn't know about like C. Humphrey,
2 CONC  William Boswell, Nelson McDowell, etc....I'll transcribe them word for word later this week but here's a preview....
2 CONT
2 CONT The will records are from Dallas Co. AL She is also referred to as Happy Beard It mentions no husband. Her administrator was a man named Person Davis The records seem to be dated 1822-1829 regarding her estate, it lists her proper
2 CONC ty & who bought it (mostly Person Davis, some were bought by William Gwinn, some to Henry Beard, one thing to David McCord and one to Saml Parsons. Then her money seems to be divided out (or the first eight are listed as ? somethi
2 CONC ng, it looks like asprvoucher) to  No. 1 A. Waller 11.84 No. 2 William Blair 11.84 No. 3 C. Humphrey 57.50 No. 4 Henry Beard 11.84 No. 5 William Gwinn 11.84 No. 6 Welcome Beard 11.84 No. 7 Thomas Morrison 11.84 No. 8 William Boswe
2 CONC ll 6.00 then it lists "share of estate" to P. Davis 11.84 Archibald Beard 11.84 John Beard 11.84 George Beard 11.84 Nelson McDowell 11.84 charges for trouble expense 19.85 3/4 Total 225.43 3/4 then advertising 3.50, judge & clerk 
2 CONC fees 4.75 Also Henry Beard is in Baldwin County as a member of the Alabama State Militia in Beat No. 3, signed 6/17/1820 Also Henry Beard in 36th Regt. Wilcox, Ensign 10/8/1825 These two Henry Beard listings are probably her son a
2 CONC nd not her husband, I'm guessing.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Followup e-mail from Jan Elaine Biard Thomas on 22 June 2000:
2 CONT
2 CONT I did a little quick looking around on the internet last night, and it seems that Person Davis (listed in the probate records) has a daughter named Kerenhappuch Davis. Imagine that. Kerenhappuch Davis married a man named James Mad
2 CONC ison Sorelle. The web page is http://ccwf.cc.utexas.edu/~bans/gete/D0008/1752.html This web page doesn't show Person Davis's wifes name or his parents name, but I am going to try to contact the owner of the web page and see where 
2 CONC their info came from. I also ran the new names through the LDS site, FTM, and yahoo and altavista, but I didn't come up with anything. William is such a common first name, and believe it or not, their are quite a few men named Nel
2 CONC son McDowell. But, I feel very certain that those other names are the spouses of our unknown girls. I believe their were 13 names who received a share of the estate. There is one puzzling thing...somebody had added two more boys n
2 CONC ames (Robert and Richard) to the list of Henry's children in Mauds book. Those two boys are not in the will records. Maybe they were Henry No. 2's brothers and not his sons, or they were already dead. Does anybody know why Maud ad
2 CONC ded those names? It wouldn't be too far fetched to think that they might already be dead, it seems a little odd that none of Kerrenhappuch Beards children predeceased her during approximately 70 years, if there were 13.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Transcription of Keranhappuch Nelson Beard's estate records by Jan Elaine Biard Thomas: Notes by Jan Baird Thomas 6/28/00 Probate Minutes Dallas Co. AL Page 6 & 7
2 CONT
2 CONT An Appraisement of the estate of Happy Beard decd. agreeable to an order to us directed from the judge of the county court of Dallas this 2nd day of January 1822. When the following property was shown by the admr. And appraised as
2 CONC  follows (viz)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Bed furniture 25$, 1 bed furniture 30$	 55.00 4 Bed Sheets 4$ 1 chest 3$ 2 Pewter Basin dishes &c 6$	 13.00 2 tin buckets cups & coffee Pots	 1.00 1 Tackle?(looks like Heackle) & pr of cards	 2.00 1 Lot of Books 6.50 1 Lugg? 1.1
2 CONC 3	 7.62 ½ 1 Pot rack 2$ 1 pr Pot hooks & frying Pan &c 3$	 5.00 1 Cow bell 2$ 1 Side Saddle & Blanket 20$	 22.00 1 Looking Glass & bucket 1$ 1 Sorrel mare 50$	 51.00 13 head of Hogs 30$ 2 piggins? 1 tin dipper & 2? Cup .50$	 30.50
2 CONC  $187.12 ½ 1 Table Cloth	 $1 $188.12 ½ Given under our hands and seals this 2nd Jany 1822. David McCord {seal} W. Wolds (or Woods) {seal} John Kerida (or Kenida) {seal} Sworn to this 2nd Jany 1822. J.H. Thorington J. P. D6  Record
2 CONC ed May 26th 1829 J. D. Craig clk
2 CONT
2 CONT (I'm not sure about the initials of the clerk and the JP)
2 CONT
2 CONT (page 16) An Account of the articles sold at the sale fo Kerinhappuch Beard decd. this 2nd Jany 1822. By Person Davis admr. (viz) Person Davis 1 Sorrel Mare	 60.00 Person Davis	 1 Pot rack 2.25 Person Davis 1 Katchel? & bell	 4.00
2 CONC  Person Davis	 1 Tin bucket & dipper	 1.12 ½ Person Davis	 3 Basins & plate & 2 spoons 4.00 Person Davis	 2 Piggind & 1 pr cards	 1.00 Person Davis	 1 Bible & Hymn Book	 9.00 Person Davis	 1 Womans Saddle	 23.50 Person Davis	 1 Ch
2 CONC est	 2.00 William Gwinn	 13 head of Hogs	 32.50 William Gwinn	 1 book	 1.00 William Gwinn	 1 Table cloth	 .81 ¼ William Gwinn	 1 Bed & furniture	 33.50 David McCord	 1 pr Pot hooks	 .08 ½ Henry Beard	 1 Baker & Shovel	 .62 ½ Henry
2 CONC  Beard	 1 frying pan	 1.00 Henry Beard	 1 Tin bucket & tin cups	 1.00 Henry Beard	 1 Pewter dish	 1.25 Henry beard 1 Lugg?	 1.75 Saml Parsons	 4 Sheets 5$ 1 bed & furniture 33.25	 38.25 One note on Henry Beard	 11.00 Person Davis 
2 CONC 324 ? Pork? a 5$	 16.20 Person Davis	 $236.63 ¼ Peson Davis admr. Of Keronhappuch Beard dec. being sworn saith that the above is a complete inventory of the articles belonging to said Estate and sold by him at public auction this 
2 CONC 5th Feby 1822.  Sworn before me N. Sargent J.CC. D6 Recorded 27th May 1829 James D. Craig clk (page 17) Person Davis admr. In account the Estate of Kerenhappuch Beard decd. Person Davis To Amount of Sales as pr account	 $225.43 ¾ 
2 CONC Person Davis By Amt paid A. Waller as pr voucher	 No. 1	 11.84 Person Davis By Amt paid William Blair	 No. 2	 11.84 Person Davis By Amt paid C. Humphreys No. 3	 57.50 Person Davis By Amt paid Henry Beard No. 4	 11.84 Person Davis 
2 CONC By Amt paid William Gwinn	 No. 5	 11.84 Person Davis By Amt paid Welcome Beard	 No. 6	 11.84 Person Davis By Amt paid Thomas Morrison	 No. 7	 11.84 Person Davis By Amt paid William Boswell	 No. 8	 6.00 By P. Davis Share of Said Es
2 CONC tate	 11.84 By Archibald Beards share in my hands	 11.84 By John Beard Share in my hands	 11.84 By George Beard Share in my hands	 11.84 By Nelson McDowell Share in my hands	 11.84 By charge for trouble expense	 19.85 2/4 Advertis
2 CONC ing Settlement	 3.50 Judge & clerks fees	 4.75 8.25 Recorded 27th May 1829 J. D. Craig clk Source:  http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:3248715&id=I642621291
