1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	1752 Yorktown York County Virginia, USA Death: 	1818 Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Graduated from Willi1am & Marry College in 1769 and became a lawyer, a military officer in the Revolution, taught at William & Mary College after the turn of the century. He moved to "Malvern Hill", near James River, Charles City 
2 CONC County, Va. He married first, in October 20, 1774, Mary Grymes, 2nd daughter of Hon. Philip Grymes, of Middlesex County, Va. and Mary Randolph, his wife. Mary Grymes was the sister of Lucy, who married Gov. Thomas Nelson, the elde
2 CONC st son. By the first wife, Robert had one child, Elizabeth (called Betsy) Nelson, died single. He married, secondly, Susan, daughter of Speaker John Robinson, of the Virginia House of Burgesses. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and his brother, William, were captured by British troopers under Tarleton, at Castle Hill, the residence of Dr. Thomas Walker, Albemarle Co., Va., during the war of the American Revolution.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Robert Nelson by the second wife, were: 1. William Nelson 2. Mary Nelson married Prosser 3. Robert Nelson 4. Susan Nelson 5. Dr. Peyton Randolph Nelson 6. Nathaniel Nelson 7. Chiswell Nelson 
2 CONT
