1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA with the rank of LIEUTENANT COLONEL.  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A082101  DAR Ancestors # A082101]
2 CONT
2 CONT ======================================================
2 CONT Birth: 	1750 Yorktown York County Virginia, USA Death: 	Oct. 3, 1800 Yorktown York County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Col Hugh Nelson was the third child of President William Nelson and Elizabeth Burwell Nelson. He married, about 1775, Judith Page, the 2nd daughter and 5th surviving child of the Honorable John Page, of North End, Gloucester (now 
2 CONC Matthews) County, Va. and Jane Byrd, his wife. The children of Col Nelson and wife Judith were: 1. Jane Byrd Nelson, born about 1776; married, 1798, Honorable Francis Walker, of Castle Hill, Albemarle County, Va. 2. Lucy Nelson, b
2 CONC orn about 1778, married, May 16, 1798, Edmund Pendleton, Jr., of Caroline County, Va., and was his second wife. 3. Captain Thomas Nelson, born about 1780, removed to Oakland, Hanover County, Va., and married, 1804, Judith, younges
2 CONC t child of Governor Thomas Nelson, of Yorktown, Va. 4. Dr. Nathaniel Nelson, born about 1786, removed to The Lodge, Hanover County, Va., and married, about 1811, Lucy Mann, eldest daughter of Mann Page, of Shelly, Gloucester Count
2 CONC y, Va. 5. Carter Nelson, born about 1788, died single. 6. Frances Edmonia Nelson, born about 1790, died single. She had a talent for drawing and was an artist. 7. Maria Nelson, born about 1794; burned to death in the Richmond Thea
2 CONC tre, Dec 26, 1811, aged 17. Her body was identified by the watch of Hon. Francis Walker, her brother-in-law, of Castle Hill, Albermarle County, Va. Dr. Robert W. Nelson, of Charlottesville, had the watch, and a little diamond belo
2 CONC nging to it was in possession of Dr. R.C.M. Page of New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Ref: Genealogy of the Page Family of Virginia) 
