2 CONT Judge Nelson, of the District Court, died at age 59, and was buried in Yorktown. He is known as Uncle Judge Billy and Col. William Nelson, of Oakland, Hanover Co., Va.
2 CONT ==================================================================================Birth: 	1754
2 CONT Yorktown
2 CONT York County Virginia, USA Death: 	1813 Yorktown York County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Nelson, of the District Court, died at age 59, and was buried in Yorktown. He is known as Uncle Judge Billy and Col. William Nelson, of Oakland, Hanover Co., Va. He firat married, about 1779, Miss Taliaferro, of James City C
2 CONC ounty, Va, and had one child, Elizabeth (called Betsy) Nelson who married Edwards. He married secondly, Abby, daughter of Col. William E. Byrd, of Westover, on James River, Charles County, Va., and Mary Willing, of Philadelphia, P
2 CONC a., his wife.  William and his brother, Robert, were captured by British troopers under Tarleton, at Castle Hill, the residence of Dr. Thomas Walker, Albemarle Co., Va., during the war of the American Revolution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge William Nelson and his wife, Abby, had the following children: 1. Mary Nelson who married Pickens of South Carolia 2. Abby Byrd Nelson 3. Evelyn Byrd Nelson who married William Byrd Page, of Pagebrook, Clarke Coounty, Va. 4.
2 CONC  Lucy Nelson who married Harrison, of Berkeley (Harrison's Landing) on the James River, Charles City County, Va. 5. Rosalie Nelson 
