2 CONT COOMBS, MASON SR - DAR Ancestor #: A204414 Service:  NORTH CAROLINA    Rank: PATRIOTIC SERVICE Birth:  CIRCA 1714    Death:  ANTE 8-8-1785     SURRY CO NORTH CAROLINA Service Source:  WELLS, JOSEPH WINSTON: HIS ENTRY BOOK, P 28 Se
2 CONC rvice Description:  1) SIGNED OATH OF ALLEGIANCE TO MAKE LAND ENTRY, 23 JULY 1778 -tcd
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Mason Combs son of John Combs & Hannah Ann Mason was born circa 1713 near Peuman's End Creek in what is now Caroline County, Virginia. He married Sarah Ann Nelson/Mason? Ca 1734 in Caroline County, Virginia. They had seven known c
2 CONC hildren, John the eldest was most likely born in Caroline County, Virginia possibly in Stafford but the six remaining-William, Ann, Sarah, Mason, Winifred & Wilmot are all documented by church records in Overwharton Parish, Staffa
2 CONC rd County, Virginia. Mason died sometime after 16 Nov 1785 in Surry County, North Carolina according to his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason Combs was born in Puman's End Creek-Caroline County, Virgina, the son of John Combs and Hannah Ann 'Mason.' Mason was named in honor of his mother's maiden name. His grandparents were Archdale Combs and Elizabeth 'Butler' Co
2 CONC mbs. Also Josiah Mason and wife, Elizabeth. He died in Surry County, North Carolina
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason was married to Sarah Ann 'Nelson' in 1682, in Virginia. They were the parents of two known children: Joseph  Mason (Jr.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason's great grandfather, John Combs was the family immigrant that sailed to the new country in 1619, on the ship, "Margold." It sailed from London, England, to Jamestown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: More info will be added at a later date. 
