1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mason served in the Revolutionary War, in Daniel Trigg's Militia, 31 March 1781
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===COOMBS, MASON JR - [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A025631 DAR Ancestor #: A025631]
2 CONT *Service:  VIRGINIA - NORTH CAROLINA    Rank(s): PRIVATE, PATRIOTIC SERVICE
2 CONT *Birth:  2-21-1747    OVERWHARTON PAR STAFFORD CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT *Death:  POST 2-22-1802     HAWKINS CO TENNESSEE
2 CONT *Service Source:  KEGLEY, EARLY ADVENTURERS ON THE WESTERN WATERS, VOL 1, P 371; NC REV ARMY ACCTS, VOL XI, P 57, FOLIO 1, ROLL #S.115.57.5
2 CONT *Service Description:  
2 CONT 1) CAPT DANIEL TRIGG, MONTGOMERY CO MILITIA 
2 CONT 2) FURNISHED SUPPLIES OR SERVICE -tcd
2 CONT * Spouse: Dorothy X
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S. Southern Colonies Project logo
2 CONT Mason Combs Jr. was a Virginia colonist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason Combs Jr. was part of a Southern Pioneer Family.
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile is part of the Combs Name Study.
2 CONT Mason Combs was born on February 21, 1747 in Overwharton Parish, Stafford County, Virginia Colony, son of Mason Combs (1714–1785) and Sarah Ann Tucker (~1716–1785).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason (37) married Dorothy Mason (28) (born on February 13, 1756 in Hawkins, Tennessee) in 1785 in Montgomery County, VA. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Combs (1779–1829)
2 CONT Simon Combs (1780–1833)
2 CONT Jeremiah Calmes Combs (1788–1867)
2 CONT Nancy Jane Combs (1797–1881)
2 CONT Mason died on February 22, 1802 in Hawkins County, Tennessee, United States, aged 55.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT I also find birth place of Stafford, Virginia with a date of February 21, 1747, and christening in Over Wharton Parish, Stafford, Virginia, but no date on that.
2 CONT Mason Combs, Jr. was born 21 February 1746/7 in Overwharton Parish, Stafford County, Virginia Colony.[1] He is the son of Mason Combs and Sarah Ann Nelson. He passed away after 22 February 1802 in Hawkins County, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Combs-Coombs &c. Research Group, "Although Mason of Hawkins gives every indication of being the same individual who was Mason, Jr., b 1746/7, he is still not fully documented, and the collection of records continu
2 CONC es..."[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason Combs, Jr. (Mason, Sr., John, Archdale), b 21 Feb 1746/7, Overwharton Parish, Stafford Co, VA; d 1801-1808, probably in Hawkins Co, TN; m bef 1785, Dorothy UNKNOWN, b bef 1772, d aft 1828, probably in Warren Co, TN.[2]
2 CONT Note: Mason Combs Deed of Trust
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=fcebb3cc-912b-482f-bddf-ed7fcc1b7d8b&tid=46092103&pid=1664 [Link leads to Error 404, Page not found.]
2 CONT Sources
