1 NAME George /Walker/
2 GIVN George
2 SURN Walker
2 _MARNM Walker
1 NAME Col. George Walker
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Cantrell Gilliand Memorial Garden
2 ADDR
3 STAE South Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1720
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of Virginia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 DEC 1781
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Colonel
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAR Ancestor #: A119364
2 CONT
2 CONT George Walker was the son of Jacob Walker and Courtenay Tucker. He served in the American Revolution as an Adjutant of Baylor's Cavalry Regiment, known as "Lady Washington’s Own". A colleague who also served in the Regiment was He
2 CONC nry Lee who earned his nickname, "Light-Horse Harry", during this time for his horsemanship. For his service,the DAR designated George Walker, "Ancestor Number A119364".
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel Walker married Mary Meade and had several children. Three were documented by the DAR:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Walker married Nancy Hawkins John Walker married Sarah Sallie Caffery George Walker married Rachel Caffery
2 CONT
2 CONT Brothers, John and George, married sisters, Sarah and Rachel Caffery. They were the daughters of John Caffery, DAR Ancestor Number A206694, and Mary Donelson, daughter of Colonel John Donelson and Rachel Shockley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob and Nancy Walker were the parents of David Walker, lawyer, jurist, and early settler of Fayetteville, Arkansas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son George served as Senator from Kentucky: he was appointed to the United States Senate by Governor Isaac Shelby to fill the vacancy caused by the resignation of George M. Bibb. He served from August 30 to December 16, 1814, when
2 CONC  a successor, William T. Barry, was elected.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son John Walker was elected to the Senate from Howard County [Missouri] in 1828, and in 1832, he was elected State Treasurer of Missouri. He held that office until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per SAR Membership Number 96593 of Thomas Jefferson Vanzant, the 3XGGS of George Walker, "Among a number of officers recommended for promotion in 1781 appears the name of George Walker as Colonel. (He did not receive this promotio
2 CONC n before he died in December 1781.) Despite the fact that he did not receive the promotion, we have referred to him as "Colonel".
2 CONT
2 CONT The actual burial site of Colonel Walker has been lost to history. Nevertheless, we have placed a Memorial Stone in his honor in the Cantrell Gilliand Memorial Garden. May this memorial serve as an expression of the gratitude we o
2 CONC we him for risking his life and braving the unknown to help build a new country: our America.
2 CONT
2 CONT bio by Vonnie L. Cantrell
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Kidder Keith Walker, b. 1754 Susannah Everard Walker Eldridge Rep. David Walker (1763-1820) Mary Walker Stith Anne Walker Randolph Sen. George Walker Margaret Walker Temple Frances(?Courtenay) Walker Helen Walker Call An
2 CONC drew Meade Walker John Walker (1772-1838) Jacob Wythe Walker (1778-1838)
2 CONT
2 CONT George Walker's will was probated in Brunswick Co., VA on 25 Dec 1780/1, executors David Meade, William Withers and Andrew Meade. 
2 CONT
2 CONT www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=149009794
