1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The children of Colonel John2 Baylor ( 1705- 1772), and '''Frances Walker''' (?- 1783) were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1) Courtney Baylor m. Jasper Clayton of Gloucester County
2 CONT * 2) Lucy Baylor m. John Armistead
2 CONT * 3) Frances Baylor m. John Nicholson
2 CONT * 4) Elizabeth Baylor unmarried
2 CONT * 5) John Baylor 3 ( 1750- 1808) m. Frances Norton ( 1760- 1815) in 1778
2 CONT * 6) George Baylor ( 1752- 1784) m. Lucy Page in 1778
2 CONT * 7) Walker Baylor ( ? - 1823) m. Jane Bledsoe
2 CONT * 8) Robert Baylor m. Miss Gwynne
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT # [http://ead.lib.virginia.edu/vivaxtf/view?docId=uva-sc/viu00032.xml A  GUIDE TO THE BAYLOR FAMILY PAPERS] "John Baylor 1 ( 1650- 1720) resident of Gloucester County, Virginia, and later King and Queen County, Virginia, married L
2 CONC ucy Todd O'Brien (ca.1681-?) of New Kent County, Virginia, in 1698. They were believed to have had three offspring, Frances Baylor, Robert Baylor, and John Baylor 2."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-265946881-3-2199/frances-baylor-born-walker-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-2147b0e25bc9799fe2aba9c65ac65120&mrid=c524aa51a71a8017a155251532d8d3bd MyHe
2 CONC ritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 15 2021, 7:03:36 UTC''
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/211522995/frances-baylor
2 CONT * Dorman, John Frederick. 2004. Adventurers of Purse and Person, Virginia, 1607-1624/5. Genealogical Pub. Co. 4th edition. Vol 1, Page 267, book lookup by Hill, C. [03/04/2024]
2 CONT *The  profile previously  says that she died at New Market, Shenandoah County VA. (up in the Valley). She did not.  She died at the Baylor Plantation, New Market Plantation, Caroline County VA.
2 CONT * AP&P gives a citation of her death The Virginia Gazette, or Public Advertiser, Richmond Va. 19 July 1783: Baylor Bible. loc. cit.
