1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In "The Virginia Gazette" (Williamsburg, Va.), Friday, May 18, 1739, page 3, column 2: "Married- Yesterday Mr. Robert Tucker, merchant in the Borough of Norfolk, to Miss Hannah Corbin, daughter of Col. Gawin Corbin
2 CONC , of King and Queen County."
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  [http://services.dar.org/members/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A207426  DAR  Ancestor #: A207426] 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 20—4. Joanna, b. 1720; d. after 1779; m. 5-171739, Col. Robert Tucker, of Norfolk Co., Va.b. 1710; his will was probated in 1780; he was the son of Hon. Robert and Frances (Houston) Tucker, of Norfolk Co.,Va.; this Robert Tucker
2 CONC 's will was probated in 1722, and he was theson of John Tucker, of Barbadoes. Issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—1. Robert, b. 9-24-1741 of Norfolk Co., Va., will dated July 9, 1779, to which he added a codicil Sept. 19, 1779; he names his mother Joanna (Corbin) Tucker, and his brother and sisters, etc.; d. unm.
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—2. Gawin Corbin; untraced.b 1-31-1765
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—3. Ann, unm., in 1779.b 8-27-1757
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—4.Joanna, b. 4-12-1794 m. Nov. 17, 1762, her cousin Hon. Gawin Corbin, of "Buckingham House," Middlesex Co., Va., son of Col. Richard and Elizabeth (Tayloe) Corbin, of "Lanesville," King and Queen Co., Va., and had issue. 
2 CONC (See issue of Hon. Gawin Corbin.)
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—5. Sarah, b 10-17-1747 m. James Taylor, and had among other issue:  1. James; 2. Sarah. 1771-1811 m. 9-11-1790 James Hexon. 1751-1801)
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—6. Martha,b. 2-9-1743 m. Thomas Newton, and had issue: 1. Thomas; 2. Sarah; 3. Amy; and perhaps others.
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—7. Courtney,b. 4-30-1756 m. Joseph Hutchins, and had issue: 1. Elizabeth; and perhaps others.
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—8. Caroline Henrietta,3-16-1765 unm. 1779. m. Daniel Norton
2 CONT
2 CONT *    21—9. Frances,b. 3-21-1732 m. [2] Mr. Harvey; untraced. m(1)David Kerr
