1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maj-Gen Sir William Waller, Kt., MP and Lady Jane Reynell had only one surviving child, called [https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Courtenay/6000000007525163069 Margaret], who married Wiliam Courtney. Their son R
2 CONC ichard, predeceased without issue so a considerable fortune was settled on Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "When Margaret Waller was christened in February 1633, in St Peter's Cathedral Church, Exeter, Devon, England, her father, Sir William Waller, was 34 and her mother, Jane Reynell, was 32. She married Sir William Oughtred Courtenay
2 CONC  in 1641, in Powderham, Devon, England. They were the parents of at least 8 sons and 8 daughters. She died on 9 January 1694, in Devon, England, at the age of 60, and was buried in Wolborough, Devon, England, United Kingdom."
