1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Family and Education==
2 CONT b. c.1655, 4th s. of Sir William Courtenay, and bro. of Francis Courtenay and George Courtenay. m. (1) aft. 26 Mar. 1676, (with £2,000) Jane, da. of Sir Thomas Southwell, 1st Bt., of Castle Mattress, co. Limerick [I], 1s.; (2) Cat
2 CONC harine, da. of Sir William Waller II of Strutton Ground, Westminster, 2da. He was drowned with his only son on active service in the Mediterranean in January 1696.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1660-1690/member/courtenay-richard-1655-96 History of Parliament Online]
