1 OCCU Member (MP) of the Parliament of Great Britain for Honiton in 1741–1747 and 1754–30 April 1763
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Family and Education==
2 CONT b. 8 June 1714, 2nd surv. s. of Sir William Courtenay, 2nd Bt., and bro. of William Courtenay. educ. Westminster 1725; Magdalen, Oxf. 1731. m. 14 Apr. 1737, Lady Catherine Bathurst, da. of Allen Bathurst, M.P., 1st Earl Bathurst, 
2 CONC 2s. 2da.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Returned unopposed for Honiton as a Tory on the family interest, Courtenay voted against the Administration in all recorded divisions. He was defeated at Honiton in 1747 but re-elected in 1754, continuing to sit for it till his de
2 CONC ath, 30 Apr. 1763.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref Volumes: 1715-1754
2 CONT
2 CONT Author: Eveline Cruickshanks
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1715-1754/member/courtenay-henry-reginald-1714-63
2 CONT
