1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was the youngest daughter of Virginia Governor John Page and the poet, Margaret Lowther Page (1759-1835). She was married to Robert Saunders of Williamsburg, Virginia who died in 1868. After her husband's death
2 CONC , she moved to Washington, D.C. where she resided in the Louise Home for Women, established by W.W. Corcoran for ladies who have seen better days. She was the author of Leonora and the Ghost: A True Christmas Tale for Youth.
2 CONT
2 CONT The National Republican Thursday Morning, June 18, 1885 Minor Local Events Death in the Louise Home The death is announced at the Louise Home of Mrs. Lucy Burwell Page Saunders, relict of the late Robert Saunders, of Virginia and 
2 CONC daughter of ex-Governor John Page, of the same state. The funeral will occur from the home today.
