2 CONT In Our Family Genealogy p. 35: Sallie (sic)  Nelson on 12-29-1855, made over her slaves to the children.  In this division she states that: l. Her daughter Mary has married William Henry Smith 2.Her daughter Winifred has married B
2 CONC enjamin F. Harding 3.Son Agustus Washington Nelson has attained his lawful age 4.Her daughter Emily F. Nelson is still under age Benjamin Harding & William Henry Smith & Agustus W. Nelson each pay Sallie Nelson 5 shillings for the
2 CONC  use of the slaves. (Craven Co. Deed Bk. 63 p. 13).  On 8-8-1866 SARAH NELSON made her will, which was probated in Dec. Court 1867.  1. Son Agustus W. Nelson gets some furniture and a hand mill. 2. Daughters Mary Smith and Winifre
2 CONC d Harding get a tract of land know as Elisha Griffin land which Sally acquired after death of her husband, Edward Nelson, Jr.. 3. Grandchildren William E. Brown and Sarah P. Brown get the Street tract "where I now live".  The Grif
2 CONC fin land between the Street tract running from the main road to Swift Creek and the Cambell (sic) Mill Race to be attached to the Street land for the benefit of her grandchildren, children of EMILY NELSON BROWN, decd.   4. The chi
2 CONC ldren of Augustus W. Nelson to get the land I purchased from him and a tract he purchased from James Gaskins and Clarissa, his wife. (Craven Co. Will Bk. D, p. 453).  THE STREET LAND was purchased by SARAH ROACH NELSON after death
2 CONC  of her husband and she moved the family graveyard there.  It is situated on the southern edge of VANCEBORO, across the SWIFT CREEK. Following her death, the lands of EDWARD NELSON, JR. decd. were divided by commissioners appointe
2 CONC d by Superior Court on 4-6-1868.  Their report made on that day gives; WILLIAM HENRY SMITH & wife, MARY NELSON SMITH, 217 ac. on Fork Swamp joining Cross Branch, Reedy Pocosin. Value $317. Wm. and sister Sarah P. Brown, heirs of E
2 CONC mily F. Nelson Brown, get 355 ac. on the Run of Palmetto Swamp to the mouth of Fork Swamp, including all the land the late Edward Nelson, Jr. owned on both sides of Fork Swamp. Value $257. Winnifred Nelson Harding gets the King la
2 CONC nd on Palmetto Swamp next to Joel King`s patent, down Briery Branch and to the southern edge of the old cart road.  192 ac. Value $287.  (Craven Co. Deed Bk. 72, p. 136).  There were other lands which presumably the children recei
2 CONC ved according to the will of their father sometime earlier.  See page 35 of Our Family Genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
