1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Marriage
2 CONT *1695 14 Apr; Bartel Jacobs, ym, fr Midwout, L.I.; Ellinor Douglas, wid Jan De Lenni, both liv. Pemmerepoch (c.) [Bergen DRC Marriages - 1666-1788]
2 CONT
2 CONT ''~• Seems to have left NY province between 1702 and 1710 for he (now as Bartholomew) and his sister (Hendrickje) are on a parish list in Northampton township Bucks County, PA Province.
2 CONT ''This congregation has its roots in the Neshaminy & Bensalem congregation, and has, over the years, been served by churches at several locations. The oldest site, having been built in 1738-39, was located in Feasterville area of 
2 CONC Southampton township, adjacent to the community's old burying ground. A second church was built in 1751, at Addisville, Northampton township, to aid in serving the growing congregation. Finally a third church was built in 1814, at
2 CONC  Smoketown, now called Churchville, in Northampton township, to replace both of the older ones. This was the forerunner of the church that exists at that location today.''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''On May 20, 1710, the church at Bensalem & Neshaminy was formally established with the Reverand Paulus Van Vlecq as pastor of this congregation, as well as one at Germantown. On the same day Rev. Van Vlecq established a church co
2 CONC uncil at Neshaminy & Bensalem,'' ` including: Bartholomew
2 CONT
