1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=102835758 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1763 Abbeville County South Carolina, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Aug. 11, 1848 Pickens County South Carolina, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT *Benjamin Lawrence (1747 - 1826)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Benjamin Lawrence Cemetery Clemson Pickens County South Carolina, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Nancy Brown Record added: Dec 30, 2012 Find A Grave Memorial# 102835758
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Source: http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=mspeed&id=I2130
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I2130
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Rachel Weems
2 CONT
2 CONT Given Name: Rachel
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname: Weems
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: F
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 1765 in Abbeville District, South Carolina
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 11 Aug 1848 in Pickens County, South Carolina 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wills of Pickens County, South Carolina 1828-1862
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Book No. 1, pages 129-130
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will and Testament of Rachel Lawrence
2 CONT
2 CONT The State of South Carolina
2 CONT
2 CONT I, Rachel Lawrence, of Pickens District in the State aforesaid, for the disposition of such property as it has pleased God to bless me in this world, do make and ordain this my last Will and Testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT FIRST. I desire that all my just debts and my funeral expenses be paid by my executors for which purpose he will appropriate any money which I may die possessed of & collect any debts which may be due me.
2 CONT
2 CONT SECOND. I give and bequeath to my son Elisha Lawrence and his wife Martha Lawrence One Hundred dollars which has been already delivered to the latter, and in addition to the above I give to my said Daughter-in-law Martha Lawrence 
2 CONC Fifty dollars, and half the interest on the price of the negro man Bill (which was given by my husband to me during my lifetime, then to be sold and the proceeds equally divided between my two sons, James and Elisha) from the time
2 CONC  he was sold by my said son James, until the day of my death, all of which is in the hands of my said son James.
2 CONT
2 CONT THIRD. I give and bequeath to my son James Lawrence Fifty Dollars and desire that he pay (according to contract to pay interest on the price of the said Boy Bill) one half the interest on the said sum of Five hundred and fifty dol
2 CONC lars, to be appropriated as above, he having also had the use of my interest in the land whereon my husband lives.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOURTH. I give and bequeath to my daughter Margaret Deal Fifty dollars.
2 CONT
2 CONT FIFTH. I give and bequeath to my Gr. Grand-Daughter Esther Margaret Craig, daughter of Robert Craig, a negro girl named Virginia, aged about eleven months.
2 CONT
2 CONT SIXTH. I have already given to my Grand-daughter Rachel Craig, wife of Robert Craig, for the affection which I have for her, and for her kindness to me, eight hundred dollars, and in addition to which I give to her any balance tha
2 CONC t may be left of my Estate, after paying all the foregoing bequests.
2 CONT
2 CONT SEVENTH. I nominate and appoint my friend Miles M. Norton, Executor of this my last will and testament to carry into effect the same according to the desires therein expressed.
2 CONT
2 CONT WITNESS my hand and seal this thirteenth day of November one thousand eight hundred and forty six and seventy-first year of American Independence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed & sealed in presence
2 CONT
2 CONT of us with the word half interlined RACHEL her X mark LAWRENCE
2 CONT
2 CONT before signing.
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM D. STEELE.
2 CONT
2 CONT SIDNEY McDOW.
2 CONT
2 CONT JEPTHA NORTON.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOUTH CAROLINA. }
2 CONT
2 CONT PICKENS DISTRICT. }
2 CONT
2 CONT PERSONALLY appeared before me Col. Jeptha Norton and made oath that he was present and did see Rachel Lawrence sign the within (by making her mark) as her last will and that W.D. Steele & Sidney McDow were with himself subscribing
2 CONC  witnesses to the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT SWORN to before me 2\\\\\\\\super nd\\\\\\\\nosupersub October, 1848.JEPTHAH NORTON.
2 CONT
2 CONT W. D. STEELE
2 CONT
2 CONT BE IT REMEMBERED that on the second day of October in the year of our Lord One thousand eight hundred and forty eight the last will of Rachel Lawrence late of Pickens District was proved in common form by the oath of Col. Jeptha N
2 CONC orton.
2 CONT
