1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Willson, b. prob. Edinburgh Scotland, ca. 1670. d. 1746, Augusta County, VA. married Jane Lee, b. 7 Nov 1672, Direlton, Scotland in abt. 1683/4. She was still alive when Robert died. Jane's parents are shown as Thomas Lee a
2 CONC nd Anne Davis. Robert and Jane moved to Londenderry, Ireland where their children were born, and then immigrated to PA, and later to the Augusta County, VA area. They had nine known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Thomas Willson (our main interest), b. abt 1695, will proved 18 May 1773 in Augusta County, VA. (There is an abstract of Thomas' will in Chalkley's Chronicles.) He married Elizabeth Dinwiddie abt. 1718, I believe in Ireland. Ac
2 CONC cording to my Rosamond cousin who made the connection between John Roseman/Rosamond and Sarah Willson, who was the daughter of Thomas Willson and Elizabeth Dinwiddie Willson, Thomas came to VA in 1737, while Elizabeth and the chil
2 CONC dren didn't come until 1740, immigrating through Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT The book shows Elizabeth Dinwiddie as the daughter of either Robert Dinwiddie and Elizabeth Cuming, or Lawrence Dinwiddie and Sarah Gartshore. This would make her birth date either April 1689, or October 1695 In Glasgow, Lanark, S
2 CONC cotland. They located finally in Fairfield, Rockbridge County, VA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had eight children. The dates I'm showing came from the Wilson researcher I was in touch with and I haven't personally confirmed them. These children are not mentioned in the book, other than a sentence saying Thomas and Eliz
2 CONC abeth had eight known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT * a. Matthew Willson (1718 - 1783) 
2 CONT *b. Samuel Willson (abt 1720 - ?) 
2 CONT *c. Nathaniel Willson (abt 1724 - ?) 
2 CONT *d. Rebekah Willson (abt 1728 - ?) 
2 CONT *e. Martha Willson
2 CONT * f. Elizabeth Willson 
2 CONT *g. Rhoda Willson 
2 CONT * h. Sarah Willson (b ca 1726, Londonderry, Ireland - bef 1790, Abbeville, SC); married John Roseman, b. UK ca 1710 (could have been England or Ireland); came to Annapolis, Maryland Dec 1725 on the ship Forward from England as an 
2 CONC indentured convict. He relocated to Augusta County, VA after 1740 and married Sarah Willson. This is one of our mysteries, when and where they were married. From Chalkley's Chronicles they owned land, 380 acres, on Moffett's Creek
2 CONC  which they sold in Nov 1765, after which they relocated with their children to the Old 96 District in SC. Their children were Samuel (married Sarah Hodges), James (married 1st ??, 2nd Mary Daugherty, widow of James Daugherty in S
2 CONC C, in the 1790s), Margaret (married Bartholomew Weems), Jean (never married) and Sarah F. (married Richard Hodges, brother of Sarah who married Samuel). The birth dates of their children are unknown, as well as the dates they were
2 CONC  married, and our other big mystery is the name of the wife of James Rosamond, but it could have been another Hodges sibling of Richard and Sarah, or Lettice Jones, sister of Adam Crain Jones. I have information on the rest of the
2 CONC ir spouses as well extensive information on their numerous descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
