2 CONT (3) A household headed by Richard HODGES is listed in the 1850 census of Brown Township, Ripley County, IN. [His surname is listed as HADGES in the index to the 1850 census.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard is listed in the 1850 census as a farmer who was then 59 years of age; therefore, according to the 1850 census, he was born in about 1791. According to the 1850 census, he was born in SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Listed with Richard is his wife, Jenet, who was then 58 years of age; therefore, according to the 1850 census, she was born in about 1792. According to the 1850 census, she was born in Scotland. [Her first name is listed as Lenet 
2 CONC in the index to the 1850 census.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Also listed with Richard is his daughter, Margaret, who was then 18 years of age; therefore, according to the 1850 census, she was born in about 1832. According to the 1850 census, she was born in IN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also listed with Richard is his son, Richard, a farmer who was then 16 years of age; therefore, according to the 1850 census, he was born in about 1834. According to the 1850 census, he was born in IN.
2 CONT
2 CONT (6) A household headed by Richard HODGES is listed in the 1860 census of Washington Township, Lafayette County, MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard is listed in the 1860 census as a farmer who was then 69 years of age; therefore, according to the 1860 census, he was born in about 1791. According to the 1860 census, he was born in SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Listed with Richard is a male[?], James[?] HODGES, who was then 68 years of age; therefore, according to the 1860 census, he[?] was born in about 1792. According to the 1860 census, he[?] was born in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also listed with Richard is his son, Richard, who was then 26 years of age; therefore, according to the 1860 census, he was born in about 1834. According to the 1860 census, he was born in IN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also listed with Richard is his daughter-in-law, Catherine, who was then 23 years of age; therefore, according to the 1860 census, she was born in about 1837. According to the 1860 census, she was born in VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also listed with Richard is his granddaughter, Innus A., who was then 2 years of age; therefore, according to the 1860 census, she was born in about 1858. According to the 1860 census, she was born in MO.
2 CONT
