1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Susannah married her first cousin Robert Williamson, son of John Williamson, her father's brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The dwelling at Brook Hill, the home of Robert Williamson, who married his cousin Susanna Williamson, was built prior to 1735, and five generations of the family were born in the same house - most of them in the same room.  The dw
2 CONC elling No. 707 E. Franklin Street, which was occupied by General Lee from 1861 to 1865 as his wartime residence, was in 1892 given to the Virginia Historical Society and has since that time been home of that Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Historic Virginia Homes and Churches" by Robert Alexander Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 Dec 1796, Robert Williamson sold 200 acres in Cumberland Co, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
