2 CONT Sarah Harvey Youngblood deeded her estate to her grandson, James T. Peace in 1889 at 4:00 PM as shown in the following abstract: Deed Book J. P. 607 Sabine County State of Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Youngblood to James T. Peace (grandson)
2 CONT
2 CONT Block #28 in Town of Hemphill; also 2 acres of land, beginning NE corner, Blk. #28 N. 97 yds., W. 100 yds; S. 97 yds to NW corner, Blk. 28.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness my hand this 4th day of June, 1889.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wit/ Wm. Gellatly, Jp. Her
2 CONT
2 CONT W.T. Arnold Sgd. Sarah X Youngblood
2 CONT
2 CONT Clk. Ct. Mark ( She was blind)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sabine Co. Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Sarah Youngblood was an educated woman, and I have her signature on earlier documents. (photocopies)
2 CONT
2 CONT Above is take from page 60 of "The Youngblood Family" by Reba Holmes Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Below is from The Youngblood Family by Reba Holmes Brwon page 51
2 CONT
2 CONT The burial place of Henry Youngbood, a soldier of the War of 1812
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=33339552
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Miller (Harvey) Youngblood was the daughter of Michael Harvey and his wife Mary "Polly" Clower. She married Henry Youngblood son of Benjamin Youngblood and his wife, Susannah Collins on 27 February 1817 in Marion County, Mis
2 CONC sissippi. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They were the parents of 13 children: James Youngblood, Benjamin Youngblood, Mary Youngblood, Michael Youngblood, Susannah Youngblood, Julia Ann Youngblood, Albert W. Youngblood, Henry A. Youngblood, Thomas Harvey Youngblood, Char
2 CONC les Stuart Youngblood, William A. Youngblood, John Pearl Youngblood, and Sarah Jane Youngblood. Sarah Miller (Harvey) Youngblood died in Hemphill, Texas in 1895. 
2 CONT --------------------
