1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Pearl Youngblood was wounded at the Battle of Helena, Arkansas on July 4th, 1863, in the War Between the Stats. He was struck by a 11-inch shell from a gunboat on the river, necessitating amputation of his
2 CONT
2 CONT righ foot. He supported his family by teaching school and farming. He died at Noble, Sabine Parish, La. and is buried in the little cemetary there. John and Matilda eloped to Shelby County, Texas and were married by
2 CONT
2 CONT Parson Pressly. Matilda was a teacher, and at the time of her death in 1931, she was teaching retarded children.
