1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Grandson Robt. F. Sanders in 1912 wrote in a letter to daughter Gertrude that he was "just 6 ft. and weighed 180...finest pair I ever saw hitched together...a raw boned giant with the bluest eyes you ever saw...gra
2 CONC ndma had the blackest of eyes & hair and was by long odds the most queenly Woman I have ever seen...at 92, as erect as an Indian, Eyes bright as ever."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...uncle James House the handsomest man I ever saw, while your Grand Ma was the prettiest Woman...these 3 had the most Magnificent Black Eyes Imaginable."
2 CONT
2 CONT Of English parentage.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1830 - Clarke Co., GA';1840 - Randolph Co., Alabama; late 1840 - Chulahoma, MS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Willis had an uncle b.1791/1800 No. Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Willis' great nephew was Col. Edward Mandell House who started the  Federal Reserve Bank and the League of Nations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas William "T.W." House (b. England 1814>NY>TX d. 1880). Father of TW may have been brother to Willis & Simon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:  Sihon House, Thomas House, Carren Huppuk Millican
