1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rasa How stayed in Davidson Co. TN and made his home on land his father sold them.  He raised a large family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rasa Hows's Will - In the will he leaves his grandson James Parkerson Work  $300.  Then her refers to him as the said James P. Work.
2 CONT
2 CONT RASA2 HOWS (JOHN C1 HOUSE) (Source: (1) The Lovells Come To Tennessee By Gordon Lovell., (2) 1850 Census of Davidson Co. TN, page 206  # 209, It list Rasa Hows as head of household.) was born January 29, 1806 in Wake Co. N. C. (So
2 CONC urce: Headstone with birth and death date.), and died December 03, 1858 in Davidson Co. Tenn.  He married (1) CAROLYN PITTS (Source: The Lovells Come To Tennessee By Gordon Lovell, He list Rasa first wife as Caroline Pitts.), daug
2 CONC hter of BURRELL PITTS and NANCY HOLLAND.  She was born Abt. 1806, and died August 12, 1831 in Davidson Co. Tennessee (Source: Headstone, with death date, Rasa Hows Cemetery.).  He married (2) NANCY LOCKHART LOVELL (Source: (1) 186
2 CONC 0 Census for  Davidson  Co. TN, It list Nancy Hows as head of household age 45 years., (2) 1850 Census of Davidson Co. TN, page 206  #209, In the household of Rasa Hows it list Nancy age 35 years.) May 15, 1834 (Source: John Monro
2 CONC e Lovell Bible.), daughter of JOHN LOVELL and SUSANNAH PACK.  She was born February 08, 1815 (Source: (1) Headstone with birth and death date., (2) John Monroe Lovell Bible.), and died September 26, 1888 in Davidson Co. TN.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Name ==
2 CONT
2 CONT alternative spelling of name includes Racy and sometime Hows is written as House and Haus
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Tennessee State Marriages, 1780-2002 
2 CONT Name: Rasa Hows  Spouse: Nancy Lovell  Marriage Date: 15 May 1834  Marriage County: Davidson 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was previously married to Catherine Pitts in the 1820's. She died in 1831. She is also buried in this same cemetery 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Burial ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Rasa Hows Cemetery. This Cemetery is on Hwy 70 not far from Newson Station Rd. and Buffalo Rd. now called Hows-Hutton Cemetery, Nashville, Davidson Co., TN
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcription of the cemetery: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sterling M. Hows b. May 21, 1849  d. March 31, 1882  Gone but not forgotten    ( This is the son of Rasa)
2 CONT
2 CONT John M. Hows Son of Rasa & Nancy L. Hows b. March 1, 1835  d. July 11, 1852
2 CONT
2 CONT In memory of  Nancy Work  Daughter of Rasa and Caroline Hows  b. July 24, 1828 d. March 5, 1852
2 CONT
2 CONT in Memory of Leanah Hows  daughter off R. and C. Hows b.Oct. 9, 1826 dd. Nov. 21, 1846 ( This is the daughter of Rasa)
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles B. Hows; son of Rasa and Nancy L. Hows b. July 21, 1836 d. April 20, 1838
2 CONT
2 CONT In memory of  Wm.W. son of Wm. H. and L. Lovell  b. July 22, 1838  dd. March 29, 1844
2 CONT
2 CONT Rasa Jerome Hows  Co. A 1 Tenn Inf.  C.S.A.  (This is the son of Rasa)
2 CONT
2 CONT John H. Hutton  b. June 11, 1837  d. May 20, 1885  Maggie L. wife of John H. Hutton b. Oct 6, 1842  d. Dec 9 1919
2 CONT
2 CONT Memory of Caroline Hows wife of Rasa Hows d. Aug 12, 1831
2 CONT
2 CONT In memory of  Rasa Hows  b. Jan 29, 1806  d  Dec. 3, 1858
2 CONT
2 CONT Our Mother Nancy L. wife of Rasa Hows b. Feb 8, 1815  d. Sept. 24, 1888
2 CONT
2 CONT Leanah C. Hows  b. June 24 1848  d. Sept 18 1864  May she rest in peace
2 CONT
2 CONT Carline wife of J.A.J. Shelton Dau of  W.H. and L. Lovell b. Dec 12, 1840  d. July 16, 1862  Those that sleep in Jesus God will bring with him
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas R. son of  W.H. and L. Lovell  b. June 22, 1836  d. March 6, 1869  Gone but not forgotten
2 CONT
2 CONT In Memory of  Ida T. Hows daughter of  R. and N. L. Hows  b. May 27, 1858  d. Oct 20, 1860
2 CONT
2 CONT C. E. Hows  b. Oct 1, l874  d. Dec 10, 1875  (This is the son of Sterling Hows)
2 CONT
2 CONT W. J. Hows  b. March 8, 1870 d. Dec, 4, 1875  (This is the son of Sterling Hows)
2 CONT
2 CONT J. T. Hows  b. Sept 10, 1872  d. Dec 7, 1875  ( This is the son of Sterling Hows)
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Stephen Hutton b. Aug 11, 1862  d, March 6, 1867    (son of John Hutton)
2 CONT
2 CONT James N. Hutton  b. Aug 19, 1867  d. Oct 4, 1872  (this is the son of John Hutton)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jerome Hutton b. July 21 1871  d, Dec. 14 1875  (This is the son of John Hutton)
2 CONT
2 CONT == Will ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Racy Hows Dec'd Will                  Recorded Oct 27/59
2 CONT
2 CONT I Racy Hows of the county of Davidson and State of Tennessee being of sound mind make this my last will and testament. 1st After all my just debts are paid.  I will and bequeath unto my beloved wife Nancy L. Hows to have and to ho
2 CONC ld possession of the farm in which I now reside, all except the river tract in south of the road and adjoining the lands of Joseph M. Newson , during her natural life.  The said river tract of land to be rented out.  I further wis
2 CONC h J. M. Newsom to have the refusal of the renting of said land except my own children. I also will that the land be sown in small grain every other year. And that the renter is to have the privilege of cutting timber on my other l
2 CONC ands. Keep up the fencing.  I further will and bequeath unto my wife four horses or mules such as she may choose .  Four milk cows and calves, all my sheep and all my household and kitchen furniture.  I also will and bequeath to m
2 CONC y beloved wife during her natural life the following slaves,  George, Jane and Maria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd  It is my wish and desire that the remainder of my slaves be hired out except Sarah, which I want sold for cash to the highest bidder publicly or privately, as my Executor may think best  ?  ?  ?  ?
2 CONT
2 CONT children  ?  ?  .
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd  It is my will and desire that my Executor shall sell my land in Trigg County, Kentucky publicly or privately as he may think proper. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4th  I will and desire my children be sent to school and the expense thereof be paid out of the proceeds of my estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5th  It is my will and desire that the sum of five hundred dollars be given to each of my children when they become twenty one years of age: Susan C., Racey J., Margaret L, Stephen H, Franklin B., Leanna C,
2 CONT
2 CONT Sterling M,  Joseph N, Elizabeth P, Ida T,  or as many of my children as should become of age during my wife's lifetime..  At my beloved wife's death each one of the above named children who may not have received his or her portio
2 CONC n as above directed shall be made equal and the balance of my estate after making all equal shall be equally divided between all of my children, except my grandson James Parkerson Worke to whom I will and bequeath the sum of three
2 CONC  hundred dollars to be paid at my wife's death, and in case the said James P. Work should die without issue the above named sum is to be devided  equally between my several children.  It is my wish and desire that Joseph M. Newsom
2 CONC  be and act as my Executor set under my hand and seal in the presence of the following witnesses.  Oct 11, 1858
2 CONT
2 CONT Racy Hows [seal]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Williams
2 CONT
2 CONT William Jordan
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Rasa was the brother of my great grandfather on my grandfather John Carroll Hows side but he is also the grandfather of John's wife Ella, so he is my great uncle and my great-great grandfather.  Rasa's daughter Margaret Lewidew Ho
2 CONC ws married John Hutton, who are Ella's parents.
