1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Bethia Lovett''', daughter of John Lovett & Bethia Rootes, was married 1st to Peter Shaw on 14 October 1705 in Beverly, Essex County, Massachusetts. [3]. She married 2nd to Nehemiah Hayward, Ruth Clarke’s widowe
2 CONC r,in 1711.
2 CONT
2 CONT # They had a son Peter in 1706/7 [4] He was christened in 1708. [5] Jemima Woodbury, daughter of Isaac & Elizabeth (Herrick) Woodbury, married Peter Shaw (son of Peter Shaw and Bethia Lovett) at Ipswich. 
2 CONT # Daughter Bethiah born in 1709. [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first husband died about 1709.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Nehemiah Hayward in 1711. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT # They had a son Josiah in 1712. [8]
2 CONT # Son Jabez christened in 1714. [9]
2 CONT # Daughter Eunice in 1717. [10]
2 CONT # Son Andrew in 1719. [11]
2 CONT # Daughter Rose in 1722. [12]
2 CONT # Son Gideon in 1731. [13]
2 CONT # Daughter Ruth in 1733. [14]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Her death date is unknown.
