1 NOTE He came to America on the ship Martin in 1638, and was a member of the court of trials in Newport in 1648 and was on a committee at Portsmouth 16 May 1651.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Weeden emigrated to New England in the ship Martin in the summer of 1638, as is proved by his testimony, dated in Boston 13 July 1638, that he had witnessed the will of Sylvester Baldwin, a fellow passenger and also a native
2 CONC  of Buckinghamshire.
1 SOUR
2 DATA
3 DATE 29 APR 2020
3 TEXT Last Name
3 TEXT Grandson of Robert Weeden, James Weeden, born 1585, came to America in July 1638 from Buckingham Co., England, with his two sons William and James on the ship "MARTIN". They landed in Boston and then moved to the state of Rhode Is
4 CONC land. From there they have spread out all around the United States. 
