2 CONT ===Disproved Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT For the most recent research see [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/american-genealogist-the/image/?pageName=219&volumeId=13263 Leslie Mahler (2005) TAG 80:219] and [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/great-migr
2 CONC ation-immigrants-to-new-england-1634-1635-volume-vi-r-s/image/?pageName=456&volumeId=12124&filterQuery=category:Great%20Migration%20Study%20Project GM 2:6:462-66]. '''He was son of Robert and Ruth (Garland) Stanley.''' Caution muc
2 CONC h of the older published genealogies are incorrect. Use these sources. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigrated from England to Lynn, Massachusetts in 1634
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas raised nephew Captain John Stanley, later of Farmington, CT. His father, John, died at sea enroute to New England. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth:  bp 12 APR 1601 • Tenterden, Kent, England  Death:  Jan. 31, 1663 Hadley Hampshire County Massachusetts, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT He removed to Hartford in 1636, and in 1659 removed to Hadley, MA. Freeman in MA 4 March 1635, and a member of the Ancient and Honorable Artillery Company in 1640. He was Deputy to the General Court from Lynn in 1635 when the remo
2 CONC val to Connecticut was decided upon. He was an original proprietor at Hartford and his home lot in 1639 was on what is now Main Street just north of Little River, extending to the present Center Church. Was constable in Hartford i
2 CONC n 1644, 48, and 53. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married Bennet Tritton on August 3, 1630 in Ashford, Kent, England. To this union, 5 children were born:
2 CONT
2 CONT An original proprietor of Hartford, his name is on the Founders Monument. He probably came to America with his brothers, John & Timothy, he was a freeman in Mass. on Marach 4, 1634-5 and settled in Lynn. He was a deputy & constabl
2 CONC e there, but soon removed to Hartford. His homelot in 1639 was on Main Street just north of the Little River extending to Center Church. He was also a constable in Hartford. In 1659, he removed to Hadly and was a townsman there. H
2 CONC e married Benet Shepard, daughter of John and Rebecca (Waller) Shepard.  (Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut, p. 566) 
2 CONT
