2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=charles%2Dparker&id=I225
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *    Has Children John Parker b: 17 AUG 1687 in Cambridge Village (Newton),Middlesex,Massachusetts
2 CONT *    Has Children Mary Parker b: 3 MAR 1690/1691 in Newton,Middlesex,Massachusetts
2 CONT *    Has No Children Deborah Parker b: 11 FEB 1692/1693 in Newton,Middlesex,Massachusetts
2 CONT *    Has No Children Sarah Parker b: 24 MAR 1694/1695 in Newton,Middlesex,Massachusetts
2 CONT *    Has Children Thomas Parker b: 9 JAN 1698/1699 in Newton,Middlesex,Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: John's birth date sometimes appears as 15 Dec 1651, but Newton Vital Records clearly record it as February 15. Doubtless, the mistake is due to misunderstandings relating to the old Julian calendar, under which February was 
2 CONC the twelfth month of the year, not the second; the Julian New Year was March 25, but March was still considered the first month. This is demonstrated by Francis Jackson ("History of the Early Settlement of Newton, County of Middle
2 CONC sex, Massachusetts") who lists John's birth (p. 376) as: "John, Camb. Village, 15. 12. 1651".
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From A History of the Early Settlement of Newton: County of Middlesex ... By Francis Jackson.  Page 377.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=4n_ZIXrSssgC&lpg=PA262&ots=uY4CTrVQyQ&dq=Esther%20(Parker)%20Child&pg=PA377#v=onepage&q&f
2 CONC =true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT II. PARKER, JOHN, JR., m. Mary —, and had 
2 CONT #John, Aug. 17, 1687; 
2 CONT #Mary, March 3, 1690; Mary m. Robert Fuller, of Need. ham, 1713
2 CONT #Deborah, Feb. 11, 1693; Sarah d. 1724, left a will
2 CONT #Sarah, March 24, 1695; 
2 CONT #Thomas, Jan. 9, 1699. Thomas went to Worcester. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. Oct. 1713, ac. 62. She d. Mareh, 1715. Son John, admin. Inventory, £412, 2s.
2 CONT
