2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John was born in 1651. He is the son of John or Jonathan Parker and Joanna James.
2 CONT
2 CONT John (35) married Mary Turner (28) (born on 18 November 1658 in Medfield, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony; daughter of John Turner and Deborah (Williams) Turner) in 1687 in Massachusetts Bay Colony. Their known children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Parker b17 August 1687 [This could be John Parker d 1742 m Mary Parker and resided in Needham or John Parker d 1762 m Esther Dewing and widow Hannah Pierce and resided in Newton
2 CONT Mary Parker (3 March 1690 – 7 March 1719) m Robert Fuller and resided in Needham
2 CONT Deborah Parker (11 February 1693 – aft. 1743) m Elijah Cook. Resided in Needham and Worcester.
2 CONT Sarah Parker (24 March 1695 – 1724) d unmarried in Newton
2 CONT Thomas Parker (9 January 1699 – unknown) m Amity Taylor, resided in Worcester.
2 CONT John Parker Senr died 23 October 1713 in Newton, Massachusetts.[1] John Trowbridge was appointed guardian for the minor Thomas. His probate names his eldest son John, daughter Mary, wife of Robert Fuller, and other children Thomas
2 CONC , Deborah and Sarah.[2] Deborah married Elijah Cook.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional probate proceedings: https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-99D5-YLB?view=fullText&keywords=John%20Parker%2CNewton&groupId=TH-1971-38546-13842-13
2 CONT
2 CONT Deed Grantors John and Mary Parker of Newton to Ebenezer Stone.
2 CONT
