2 CONT Name: Isaac Parker Sex: M Birth: 15 MAR 1662/1663 in Cambridge Village (Newton),Middlesex,Massachusetts 1 2 3 4 Death: Bef 15 APR 1728 in Needham,Norfolk,Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Isaac took part in the 1690 Canada Expedition and was granted land by the Massachusetts General Court. (Francis Jackson, "History of the Early Settlement of Newton, County of Middlesex, Massachusetts" - p. 377)
2 CONT
2 CONT     Date of Isaac's birth from Cambridge and Newton Vital Records. Edward C Parker supplied location of marriage, although I have been unable to find any trace of the marriage in the Lexington vital records; it is listed only in t
2 CONC he Cambridge and Newton records. The maiden name of his wife was also Parker, but there is no indication of any relationship. Date of death is based on Isaac's will being administered April 15, 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Some sources show an additional son, John. Edward C. Parker records him in his notes, but designates him as "supposed son". Francis Jackson records the three children shown here, but adds "and probably others"; he also provide
2 CONC s an entry for this John, listing him as "sup. s. of Isaac", recording that he married a woman named Abigail, and had children John and Sarah.
2 CONT
