2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.irving-fam.com/tng/getperson.php?personID=I1135&tree=Irv01 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Rev. Thomas Foster: [Bruce3.fbk.FTW] In the latter part of the 16th Century, one Rev. Thomas Foster, a descendant of the Bromborough Castle branch of The Fosters, lived in Ipswich and Biddenham ENG.  Records show he had 
2 CONC houses in the parishes of St Mary and St Matthew, Ipswich, Suffolk County. His will, dated 21 Sep in the 12th "year of the reign of our Sovereign Lord Charles by Grace of God King of England, Scotland, France and Ireland, king def
2 CONC ender of the faith de Annogue dui 1638."The will was proved on 5 Dec 1638. __ Foster Genealogy by F.C. Pierce, Chicago Ill, 1899 [rcu.ftw] In the latter part of the 16th Century, one Rev. Thomas Foster, a descendant of the Brambor
2 CONC ough Castle branch of the Fosters, lived in Ipswich and Biddenham ENG.  Records show he had houses in the parishes of St Mary and St Matthew, Ipswich, Suffolk County. His will, dated 21 Sep in the 12th "year of the reign of our So
2 CONC vereign Lord Charles by Grace of God King of England, Scotland, France and Ireland, king defender of the faith de Annogue dui 1638."The will was proved on 5 Dec 1638.
2 CONT
2 CONT __ Foster Genealogy by F.C. Pierce, Chicago Ill, 1899 More About Rev. Thomas Foster and Abigail Wimes: Marriage: 8 Jan 1626/27, Ipswich ENG.1713 Children of Rev. Thomas Foster and Abigail Wimes are: 4 Others Foster, d. date unknow
2 CONC n. +Sgt. Thomas Foster, b. 1600, Ipswich, ENG1713, 1714, d. 20 Apr 1682, Billerica MA1715, 1716. +William Foster, b. date unknown1717, 1718, d. date unknown.
