2 CONT Born 9 Apr 1643 in Cambridge, Middlesex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Edmund Frost [uncertain] and Thomasine (Clench) Frost
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Frost Sr, Thomas Frost, Samuel Frost Sr., Joseph Frost Sr, Ephraim Frost Sr, Mary (Frost) Bradish, Thomas Frost Sr and Sarah Frost
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Rebecca (Hamlet) Frost — married 7 Dec 1664 in Billerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Elizabeth (Foster) Frost — married 22 Jan 1667 in Billerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of James Frost Jr, Thomas Frost Sr, John Frost, Samuel Frost Sr, Elizabeth Frost, Edmund Frost, Mary (Frost) Walker, Sarah Frost, Hannah Frost, Joseph Frost Sr, Abigail (Frost) Kidder and Benjamin Frost
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 12 Aug 1711 in Billerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT James was born about 1645. He passed away in 1711.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bio from Find a Grave
2 CONT
2 CONT James FROST (1643-1711), son of Elder Edmund FROST (1593-1672) of Cambridge, was born there Apr. 9, 1643 [1]. In the division of Shawshine, now called Billerica, Lot No. 49, of two hundred acres, was assigned to the Elder, which l
2 CONC ot he divided among his sons. On the fourth of January, 1663, James FROST and his brother Samuel were accepted as inhabitants of the town, and James settled there at once, where he seems to have led a quiet uneventful life, taking
2 CONC  but little part in the Indian troubles or of the affairs of the town, but devoted to the church, of which he was a Deacon.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife, whom he married Dec. 17, 1664, was Rebecca, daughter of William HAMLET. He was born about 1614, and married Sarah, the widow of James HUBBARD. She died at Woburn, Jan. 18, 1689, having survived her second husband, 
2 CONC William HAMLET. Rebecca died Aug. 20, 1666, having survived the birth of her first child only six days.
2 CONT
2 CONT (m. 1st) 7 Dec 1664, Billerica, Middlesex Co., MA Rebecca HAMLET b. ?? ??? 16?? d. 20 Aug 1666
2 CONT
2 CONT (m. 2nd) 22 Jan.1667 Elizabeth FOSTER(1646-1726)[2]
2 CONT
