2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Wilson formerly Foster
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 7 Oct 1673 in Billerica, Middlesex County, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Joseph Foster and Alice (Gorton) Foster
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Joseph Foster, Thomas Foster, Sarah Foster and John Foster
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Wilson III — married 27 Oct 1694 in Billerica, Middlesex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of John Wilson IV, Elizabeth (Wilson) Frost, Joseph Wilson, Joanna (Wilson) Sawtell, Alice (Wilson) Stearns, Jacob Wilson, Sarah Wilson, Mary Wilson, Esther Wilson, Dorcas (Wilson) Wyman, Seth Wilson, Benjamin Wilson and Re
2 CONC becca Wilson
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1 Aug 1742 in Tewksbury, Middlesex, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 31 Jul 2017 | Created 21 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: The John Wilson, Jr. who married Alice Tatman in 1748[1] is Elizabeth's grandson.[2] The Vital Records of Billerica get very confusing here. Elizabeth's husband is called John Jr., their son is called John 3, and their grand
2 CONC son is called John Jr. again. To complicate matters further, seven of the grandson's eight children have the same names as the children of John and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Removed Thomas Foster and Sarah Parker as parents. This was an obvious misidentification. This Elizabeth Foster's parents were Joseph Foster of Billerica and Alice Gorton, originally of Roxbury. Susan Anderson
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Foster was born at Billerica in the Massachusetts Bay Colony on October 7, 1673. Her parents were Joseph Foster and Alice Gorton.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married Lt. John Wilson at Woburn on December 3, 1691.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT John, born 26 Dec 1695.[4]
2 CONT Elizabeth, born 8 Nov 1697.[5] Joseph, 21 May 1699.[6] Joanna, born 6 Jan 1701/02.[7] Alice, born 12 Nov 1703.[8] Jacob, born 22 Jan 1704/05.[9] Sarah, born 17 April 1706.[10] Mary, born 21 Jan, 1707/08.[11] Esther, born 29 Jan, 1
2 CONC 709/10;[12] died 28 Feb 1728/29.[13] Dorcas, born 2 Dec 1711.[14] Seth, born 14 Nov 1713.[15] Benjamin, born 18 Sep 1715.[16] Rebecca, born 19 Jun 1717;[17] died 11 Mar 1728/29.[18] Sources
2 CONT
