1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT with the rank of PRIVATE.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A126044  DAR Ancestor # A126044]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/KPSK-XQ4/elihu-williams-1725-1779
2 CONT
2 CONT Elihu Williams
2 CONT 23 March 1725–18 February 1779 (Age 53)
2 CONT New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT The Life Summary of Elihu
2 CONT
2 CONT When Elihu Williams was born on 23 March 1725, in New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America, his father, Dr Joseph Williams MD, was 35 and his mother, Susanna Lawrence, was 35. He married Desire Fish on 17 November 
2 CONC 1747, in Plainfield, Windham, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 3 sons and 5 daughters. He died on 18 February 1779, in Kingston Township, Luzerne, Pennsylvania, United States, at the 
2 CONC age of 53, and was buried in Wyoming, Luzerne, Pennsylvania, United States.
2 CONT
