1 NAME Mehitable /Patten/
2 GIVN Mehitable
2 SURN Patten
2 _MARNM Shaw
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1744
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1812
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehitable (Patten) Hall, was the daughter of Joseph Patten (MLA for Annapolis County) and Susanna Hill
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehitabel married twice; 1st to Zachariah Hall in Medford, Middlesex, Massachusetts before 1772, when son Samuel was born, followed by David Hall in 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd Mehitebel married Moses Shaw, 24 Jan 1781 in Granville Township, Annapolis, Nova Scotia,widow of Zachariah Hall of Boston, and their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanah Shaw was born Nov 1781 died 2 Feb 1784. Susannah, born March 7, 1784. Susannah married James Reed, and then Benjamin Reed. Anna, born June 5, 1786[14]. Anna married Guilford Reed, and then Mr. Smith. (MLA for Annapolis Cou
2 CONC nty)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehitable died in Granville, Nova Scotia on July 3, 1818, and was buried in Stoney Beach Cemetery, Granville Beach, Nova Scotia[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Patten-201
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehitable (Patten) Shaw (1744 - 1818)
2 CONT
2 CONT
