2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Kent (historic flag)
2 CONT Richard Woody II was born in Kent, England.
2 CONT Birth and Christening
2 CONT
2 CONT When Richard Woody was born in 1590 in Kent, England, his father, Richard, was 22 and his mother, Margaret, was 12.
2 CONT He married Ann Daun in 1614 in Guildford, Surrey, England. They had three children in 16 years. He died on December 6, 1658, in Roxbury, Massachusetts, at the age of 68.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard /Woody born 1590 Place: Kent, England, died 6 DEC 1658: Place: Roxbury, Suffolk, Massachusetts. Will: Will deposed: Date: 16 DEC 1658
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigration
2 CONT
2 CONT He is believed to have emigrated between 1635 AND 1638 from Kent, England to Roxbury, Mass (Plymouth Colony). Richard was in a record.[1]
2 CONT Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Woody married Mary Ann Hayle in c1615 in Kent, England
2 CONT Richard Woody
2 CONT Mary Woody
2 CONT John Woody Sr.
2 CONT Isaac Woody Sr.
2 CONT Death and Burial
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Woodie Sr. died on 6 Dec. 1858 in Roxbury. His death record was from the First Religious Society (Unitarian) church records.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
