2 CONT Cross of St George
2 CONT Richard Woody II was born in England.
2 CONT Richard Woody married Francis Dexter December 29, 1646, at Roxbury, Massachusetts.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: soapboiler, Captain [citation needed]
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1666 made saltpeter for gunpowder with his brother Isaac. Richard II was a Ensign and later a Captain in the Militia and was a Freeman on 5-29-1644[citation needed]
