1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sarah Beal''' was born in 1625 in England. She was the daughter of John Beal and Frances Ripley. Name has also been spelled as Beale.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 22 March 1648/49 Sarah, married Thomas Marsh, son of George Marsh and Elizabeth Key, in Hingham, Plymouth County, Massachusetts.1 On 31 August 1658 in Hingham, Plymouth County, Massachusetts, Sarah Beal was mentioned in the wil
2 CONC l of Thomas Marsh.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 5 September 1662 Sarah, married Edmund Sheffield, at age 50, son of Edmund Sheffield and Thamazine unknown.1 Sarah Beal died on Sunday, 9 November 1710 in Braintree, Norfolk County, Massachusetts, at age 85 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sarah Beal and Thomas Marsh
2 CONT # Sarah Marsh (22 Dec 1649 - )
2 CONT # Thomas Marsh (4 Dec 1651 - )
2 CONT # John Marsh (20 Feb 1653/54 - 14 Feb 1653/54)
2 CONT # Ephraim Marsh (11 Jul 1655 - )
2 CONT # Mary Marsh (22 Feb 1657/58 - )
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sarah Beal and Edmund Sheffield
2 CONT # Mary Sheffield (26 Jun 1663 - )
2 CONT # Nathaniel Sheffield (16 March 1664/5 - )
2 CONT # Deborah Sheffield (23 Jun 1667 - ). Died at Braintree, 18 Jan 1690/1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://genealogy.theroyfamily.com/p3922.htm Ancestry of Robert Roy and Related Families - Sarah Beal]
2 CONT **Ancestral File. Family History Library, Salt Lake City, Salt Lake County, Utah, 1994.
2 CONT **Trask, William B.. "Abstracts From the Earliest Wills on Record in the County of Suffolk, Mass.", The New England Historical and Genealogical Register volume IX (1855).
2 CONT * The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Volumes 76-77. Genealogical Gleanings in England: [https://books.google.com/books?id=FpAeAQAAMAAJ&lpg=RA1-PA193&ots=S06hVx7Ogb&dq=thomasine%20sheffield&pg=RA1-PA193#v=onepage
2 CONC &q=thomasine%20sheffield&f=true page 193]
2 CONT * https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr02/rr02_267.html#P4486
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Sarah Beal''' Daughter of Frances Ripley (1580-1630) and John Beal (1588-1688)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Beal's baptismal record has never been found based upon such records of her siblings and her age at death, Sarah was born in Wymondham, Norfolkshire, England in 1625.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah BEAL married twice.
2 CONT
2 CONT FIRST: Thomas Marcsh, Sr. on March 22, 1648/1649 in Hingham, Plymouth Co, Massachusetts and had five children.
2 CONT
2 CONT FIVE Children of Sarah Beal and Thomas Marsh, Sr.:
2 CONT # Sarah Marsh -     1649–1727 
2 CONT # Thomas Marsh -  1651–1723 
2 CONT # John Marsh -     1654–1654 
2 CONT # Ephraim Marsh -     1655–1715 
2 CONT # Mary Marsh -    1658–1719 
2 CONT
2 CONT SECOND: Edmund SHEFFIELD (widower) on September 5, 1662 in  Braintree, Norfolk Co, Massachusetts and had three children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Son - died at infantcy - year unknown
2 CONT # Mary Sheffield - 1663–1718
2 CONT # Deborah Sheffield - 1667–1691
2 CONT
2 CONT Of Sarah's combined eight children from both marriages, one son died in infancy, one daughter as a young lady at age 13, son Ephraim had four children of his only but one one grandchild who died in infancy. Thus Sarah has living d
2 CONC escendants today from five of her eight children.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/69718433/sarah-sheffield
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Though her baptismal record has never been found, based upon such records of her siblings and her age at death, Sarah was born in Wymondham, Norfolkshire, England in 1625.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah BEAL married (1st) Thomas Sr. MARSH of 22d 3m 1648/49 in Hingham, Plymouth Co, Massachusetts and had five children and married (2nd) the widowed Edmund SHEFFIELD 5d 9m 1662 at Braintree, Norfolk Co, Massachusetts and had thr
2 CONC ee children. Of Sarah's combined eight children from both marriages, one son died in infancy, one daughter as a young lady at age 13, son Ephraim had four children of his only but one one grandchild who died in infancy. Thus Sarah
2 CONC  has living descendants today from five of her eight children.
2 CONT
2 CONT FROM FIND A GRAVE
