1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Volumes 76-77. Genealogical Gleanings in England: [https://books.google.com/books?id=FpAeAQAAMAAJ&lpg=RA1-PA192&ots=S06hVx7Ogb&dq=thomasine%20sheffield&pg=RA1-PA192#v=onep
2 CONC age&q=thomasine%20sheffield&f=true page 192] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. William Sheffield (Edmund, ? Thomas), of Sudbury, co. Suffolk, England, and of New England, baptized at All Saints', Sudbury, 15 Nov. 1619, died at Sherborn, Mass., 6 Dec. 1700. He married, about 1659, Mary , who died at Sherbo
2 CONC rn 31 Oct. 1714, aged 78.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not known at what date he came to New England; but he was residing at Dover, N. H., together with his brother Ichabod, in 1658. In 1660 he was of Braintree, Mass., in 1673 he was among the first settlers of Holliston and She
2 CONC rborn, Mass., and in 1686 he paid the third highest tax in the lastmentioned town. He appears, with his brother Edmund, to have bought, prior to 1672, a tract of land of Lieut. Joshua Fisher of Dedham, Mass., at Chabboquasset, in 
2 CONC what afterwards became Sherborn. In his will, dated 14 Oct. 1698.and proved at Cambridge 24 Mar. 1700/1, he mentions his house in Boston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT * i. Rachel, b. at Braintree 24 May 1660; d. young.
2 CONT * ii. Hannah, b. 18 Apr. 1663.*
2 CONT * iii. Daniel, b. 3 Mar. 1665.*
2 CONT * iv. William, b. 19 Mar. 1667.*
2 CONT * v. Martha, b. 8 Jan. 1668.*
2 CONT * vi. Joseph, b. 3 Mar. 1671;* of Dover, N. H., 9 May 1733.
2 CONT * vii. Thamasine, b. at Sherborn (?) 25 May 1673; m. Jonathan Adams.
2 CONT * viii. Susanna, b. at Sherborn 12 Dec. 1675; m. at Sherborn, 1 Sept. 1697, Zuriel Hall.
2 CONT * ix. Elizabeth, b. at Sherborn 28 Nov. 1678.
2 CONT * x. Nathaniel, b. at Sherborn 7 Mar. 1681.
2 CONT * xi. Mart, m. John Clark.
2 CONT * xii. Rachel, m. .
