2 CONT Cadiz Record obituary. Mrs Martha Jane Adams, wife of the late John Wiley Adams and a native of Trigg county, died Sat morning at 3 am at New Madrid Mo, where she had made her home for some years. A paralytic stroke caused her dea
2 CONC th. Mrs Adams was a daughter of the late Alfred B and Alphia Thomas Coleman and was born at what is known as the Alfred Coleman place in Canton district, five miles west of Cadiz. She was born 25 Dec 1837 and was 85 years of age l
2 CONC ast Dec. In the year 1872 she was married to John Wiley Adams and 7 children were born to them, 4 sons and 3 daughters. Four are now living; John Q Adams of Trigg county, Stirling Adams of Missouri, Mrs John Bell of Missouri and M
2 CONC rs Pack Hendon of Flint Mich. She had 30 grandchildren and 29 g-grandchildren. Will S Coleman of Calloway county is the surviving brother. Burial in New Madrid Cemetery by the side of her husband who died some years ago.
