1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kentucky New Era obit posted 31 Dec 1969 reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Alice Thomas Fowler, 69 year old resident of Rt. 1, Gracey, died at 3 pm Tuesday at her home following a brief illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral arrangements were incomplete early this afternoon pending arrival of relatives.  The body is at Goodwin Funeral Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Trigg County, Mrs. Fowler was born March 3, 1900, the daughter of the late Chilton A and Amanda Chewning Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of Locust Grove Baptist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her husband, Joe Fowler; six sons, Kenneth J, John C, Maxie K, and Dorris Ray Fowler, all of Chicago, Joe B Fowler Jr., Louisville, and Lonnie H Fowler, serving in Vietnam with the US Army; three daughters, Mrs. 
2 CONC Lacy Sholar, Hopkinsville, Mrs. Leroy Sholar and Mrs. Kenneth Allen, both of Rt. 1 Gracey; 20 grandchildren and one great grandchild.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/50857694/alice-fowler Find A Grave Memorial] - 
