1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT <p>OBITUARY: Cadiz Record Feb 1946 - Death Claims Wesley Gunn Thomas</p><p>     At three o'clock Tuesday morning, February 3, Wesley Gunn Thomas, after years of feeble health, was claimed by death at his home in Cadiz at the ripe 
2 CONC age of 86.  He was a men who had played a fine part in the point of good citizenship and neighborliness, in the annals of his native county.</p><p>     Mr. Thomas was a member of the large family of Thomases who came up through Cu
2 CONC mberland Gap with those early pioneers of "The Yadkin" from North Carolina, his ancestors arriving and making a settlement on the "the waters of Donaldson" about 1806.  His parents were Stanley Thomas and Emily Light Thomas.  This
2 CONC  couple bought land in the Oak Grove community and it was there Wesley Gunn was born on April 1, 1858.  On March 17, 1881 he was united in marriage to Elizabeth Henderson, who passed away in Match of 1936.  To this union were born
2 CONC  eleven children, eight of these survive him.  His religious belief was of the Primitive Baptist, and he was deeply religious.  The days of his active life were engaged in farming and he was successful in this pursuit.</p>     The
2 CONC  children who survive him are, Mrs. Mason Hughes, Miss Hazie Thomas, Mrs. Peachy Terrell, Mrs. Averitt Francis, Leslie, Lucian, James and Luther Thomas; also twenty-six grand children.  The deceased are Eura Thomas, Mrs. Garland B
2 CONC ridges and an infant.  Being of a genial and kindly disposition his friends and relatives enjoyed their relations with him.  His funeral services were held Wednesday at Dyer's Chapel at 2:00 p.m. and conducted by Rev. J.A. McDowel
2 CONC l.  Burial was at the Lawrence graveyard near the chapel.  Pallbearers included Herschell Thomas, Hugh Thomas, Elzie Light, Allen Lawrence, Clarence Bruce and D. Bruce.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
