1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Dec. 26, 1770 Yorktown York County Virginia, USA Death: 	May 7, 1853 Gloucester County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Page, of Shelly, Gloucester County, Va.,was the eldest daughter of sixth child of Governor Thomas Nelson, Jr. of Yorktown and Lucy Grymes, his wife. Her husband, Mann Page founded Shelly, on the York River, in 1794. It i
2 CONC s situated on the hill opposite Rosewell, across Carter's Creek. The original house was destroyed by a fire in 1883, but was subsequently rebuilt. She married on June 5th, 1788, Mann Page. He died at Shelly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT * 1. John Page - born Mar 7, 1789
2 CONT * 2. Lucy Mann Page - born Feb 9, 1790. 
2 CONT *3. Frances Burwell Page - born Jul 15, 1791.
2 CONT * 4. Thomas Nelson Page - born Oct 5, 1792. 
2 CONT *5. Mann Page - born Jun 9, 1794. 
2 CONT *6. Eliza Nelson Page - born Oct 15, 1795. 
2 CONT *7. Willian Nelson Page - born Jul 20, 1797. 
2 CONT *8. Mary Jane Page - born Oct 30, 1798. 
2 CONT *9. Dr. Warner Lewis Page - born Mar 10, 1800.
2 CONT * 10. Sally Burwell Page - born May 8, 1802. 
2 CONT *11. Ann Page - born Feb 10, 1803.
2 CONT * 12. Philip L. G. Page - born Sep 28, 1804. 
2 CONT *13. Robert Nelson Page - born Dec 13, 1805.
2 CONT * 14. Thomas Jefferson Page - born Jan 4, 1807.
