1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth Nelson Thompson
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Nelson, born about 1793, is the only daughter of President Willliam Nelson and Elizabeth Burwell. She married Captain (Samuel) Thompson, of the H. M. S. Ripon (Rippon) when he came over with Lord Botetourt on board. She 
2 CONC went back to England with her husband and lived there. (Norborne Berkeley, Baron de Botetourt, arrived in Virginia in October, 1769, being the first governor in chief who had come to reside in Virginia since Lord Culpeper. He open
2 CONC ed the spring session of the General Assembly on Monday afternoon, May 8, 1769. He died in October, 1770.) (HMS Rippon - British - launched Jan 20, 1758 from Woolwich Dockyard. She was broken up in 1808. Rippon was a 60-gun fourth
2 CONC  rate ship of the line of the Royal Navy.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Nelson Thompson Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   William Nelson (1711 - 1772)
2 CONT   Elizabeth Burwell Nelson (1718 - 1798)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Siblings:
2 CONT   Elizabeth Nelson Thompson
2 CONT   Thomas Nelson (1738 - 1789)*
2 CONT   Nathaniel Nelson (1745 - ____)*
2 CONT   Hugh Nelson (1750 - 1800)*
2 CONT   Robert Nelson (1752 - 1818)*
2 CONT   William Nelson (1754 - 1813)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Edit Virtual Cemetery info [?]
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Thomas Record added: Mar 09, 2013  Find A Grave Memorial# 106417949
