1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1850 census has him living in Campbell, Campbell County, Georgia, age 44.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	 16 May 1827 m. Delilah Walton, GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Household	Gender	Age	Birthplace James F Nelson	M	44	 Virginia Delila Nelson	F	36	 Georgia Thomas Nelson	M	14	 Georgia Andrew J Nelson	M	11	 Georgia Permelia E Nelson	F	9	 Georgia Delila P Nelson	F	5	 Georgia James F Nelson	M	2	 Ge
2 CONC orgia
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a winner of the 1832 GA Land Lottery--Cherokee Co.--while still living in Walton Co. As an adult lived in Campbell Co. GA (1840 & 1850 Censuses), had a plantation near Douglasville on the Chattahoochee River. He enlisted in
2 CONC  Campbellton Blues during the Creek Indian wars, ca. May 1836, while resident of Campbellton, GA. (Lt.) He served as deputy sheriff & sheriff in Campbell Co. for 12 years. Served at least one term as an Inferior Court Judge in Cam
2 CONC pbell Co (12 Apr 1851-1853). Migrated to Claiborne Parish, LA ca. 1854. 
2 CONT
2 CONT James F. Nelson enlisted in the Creek Indian War at Campbellton, GA on May 1, 1836. He served under Capt. Benjamin Camps Co. He was discharged Aug. 1, 1836. He also made application for bounty land as provided to certain officers 
2 CONC engaged in military service of U.S. signed Sept. 28, 1830. After his death in Claiborne Parish, LA his widow, Delilah applied for a pension provided under act by govt. He was a first Sergeant in Capt. Camp's Company. He was born i
2 CONC n Monroe, Walton Co, GA., also Douglasville, GA and finally Claiborne Parish, LA.
2 CONT
2 CONT When they moved to Louisiana a number of their friends and relatives came with them. There is some doubt where he was born. Cookie says Virginia and son of William Nelson. Records in Utah, LDS Church say Georgia, by heir William C
2 CONC amp in 1852, Aug. 18. Records in Salt Lake say JFN & DC were baptized on Aug. 18, 1852, JFN "endowed" on June 17, 1853 and DC "endowed" on March 19, 1955 with heir listed as Williams Washington Camp. By: George G. Nelson He served
2 CONC  as a Deputy Sheriff and Sheriff of Campbell Co, GA for twelve years, this from bio of A.T. Nelson. He was also Justice of the Inferior Court of Campbell Co., GA. He owned a plantation on the Chattahoochee River,about 6 miles from
2 CONC  Douglasville. He and family migrated to LA in 1954.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Alfred T. Nelson, of Homer, La., is a native of Georgia, his birth occurring in  Campbell County on June 19, 1835, his father being Lieut. James F. Nelson, a native of  Virginia, and a prominent man. The latter went to Georgi
2 CONC a with his parents when a child,  and there grew to manhood and married Delilah Camp, a native of Georgia. He followed the  occupation of farming in Georgia, and there reared his family, moving to Claiborne Parish  in 1854, where 
2 CONC he made a farm and resided until his death in 1872. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Franklin Nelson and Delilah Permelia Camp are: Lucy Jane Nelson, b. 1829, Walton County, GA, d., Died as child in GA. +Frances Fannie Nelson, b. 17 Mar 1831, Campbell County, GA, d. 11 Nov 1863, Claiborne Parish,
2 CONC LA-Mt Zion Cemetery. m. John A. Abercrombie +Alfred Thomas Nelson, b. 13 Jun 1835, Campbell County, Georgia, d. 23 Jan 1916, Homer, La. Burial @Arlington Cemetery-Homer. +Andrew Jackson Nelson, b. 1838, Campbell County Georgia, d.
2 CONC  1922, Claiborn Parish, La.. +Permelia E. Nelson, b. 18 Feb 1841, Campbell County, GA, d. 30 Apr 1868, Claiborn Parish, La.. m. Joseph Walter Camp +Delilah P. Nelson, b. 26 Apr 1845, Campbell County, GA, d. 23 Oct 1884. m. J.H.M. 
2 CONC Hart Taylor in GA. +James Franklin, Jr., Nelson, b. 17 Oct 1847, Campbell County, GA, d. 1916. +William J. Nelson, b. 06 Oct 1851, Campbell Co, GA. Lucy T. Nelson, b. 1858, Claiborn Parish, La.. (died as a child)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of WILLIAM NELSON and SARAH SMITH are: i. JAMES6
2 CONT  NELSON, b. Bet. 1796 - 1814. ii. LUCY NELSON, b. Bet. 1796 - 1814; m. JOHN SWAILES, 08 Dec 1822. iii. MARY NELSON, b. Bet. 1796 - 1814. iv. SARAH NELSON, b. Bet. 1796 - 1814; m. LEWIS FERRELL, 08 Jan 1837. v. WASHINGTON NELSON, b
2 CONC . Bet. 1796 - 1814. 10. vi. AGNES NELSON, b. 23 Jan 1808, Orange County, Virginia; d. 08 Mar 1865, Livingston, Ky.. 11. vii. GARLAND GARFIELD NELSON, b. 1812, Livingston Co. Ky. Near Salem, Ky.; d. 28 Nov 1872, Panola County (Bate
2 CONC sville), Mississippi.
