2 CONT "Danger Nick" Nickolas was called "Danger" because it was said he had an irascible temper. "Danger" came to Perry County in 1790's, probably at the same time as his brother John.  He came through Pound Gap, from around Holston whe
2 CONC re he had been living for some time and settled on the North Fork of the Kentucky River, near what is now Combs, KY.  He was one of the largest land owners in Perry Co. at that time.  He received his first land grant in 1810 when 
2 CONC this was Clay County and he had other grants on Ball Creek, Lotts Creek, Combs Mill, and Trace Creek. He remained a Troy and tradition says that because of this he became unpopular with other Combs.  "Danger" Nick died  in Perry C
2 CONC ounty near 1838.  He is burried in the Old Combs Cemetery on Meadow Branch Near Combs Bends.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Rich Combs... Descendants of Nicholas "Danger Nick" CombsGeneration 11.NICHOLAS "DANGER NICK" COMBS was born about 1763 in Frederick County, Virginia, USA. Son of John Combs and Nancy Harding. He died about 1859 in Perry Coun
2 CONC ty, Kentucky, USA. He was a known Tory (Sympathizer to the Crown), he may of even committed murder which is why he fled Virginia. I believe he later pledged allegiance to the Colonies. He married Nancy Grigsby, daughter of Richard
2 CONC  Grigsby and Amie Rush in 1780 in Virginia, USA. She was born about 1754 in Frederick County, Virginia, USA. She died in Jan 1850 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA (Age: 96). Nicholas "Danger Nick" Combs and Nancy Grigsby had the fol
2 CONC lowing children: i.NANCY ALICIA "LISSIE" COMBS was born on 20 Jun 1772 in Virginia, USA. She died on 11 Mar 1858 in Ary, Perry, Kentucky, USA. She was a step or adopted daughter of Nick, Nancy's child from a previous man. She marr
2 CONC ied Richard Smith Rev in 1794 in Kingsport, Sullivan, Tennessee, USA (Have also seen Knott and Clay County Kentucky as possible marriage places). He was born on 06 Mar 1771 in St Brides Parish, Norfolk, Virginia, USA. He died on 2
2 CONC 8 Nov 1836 in Ary, Perry, Kentucky, USA. ii.JEREMIAH "CHUNKY JERRY" COMBS was born about 1780 in Shenandoah County, Virginia, USA. He died on 10 Jan 1853 in Troublesome Creek, Perry, Kentucky, USA. He married (1) SARAH SALLIE GRIG
2 CONC SBY on 09 Jun 1835 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA. She was born about 1817 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA. She died after 1880 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA. He married (2) NANCY CYNTHIA SUMNER, daughter of Samuel Sumner and Winn
2 CONC ifred Combs about 1805 in Clay County, Kentucky, USA. She was born about 1787 in Kentucky, USA. She died about 1850 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA. He met MATILDA "TILDY" COMBS. She was born about 1813 in Perry County, Kentucky, U
2 CONC SA. She died about 1905 in Knott County, Kentucky, USA. iii.NICHOLAS "BIRDS EYE" COMBS was born about 1793 in Kingsport, Sullivan, Tennessee, USA. He died about 1892 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA. He married Elizabeth Combs, daug
2 CONC hter of John "Soldier" Combs and Margaret Unknown on 01 Jun 1817 in Floyd County, Kentucky, USA. She was born about 1796 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA. She died about 1880 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA. iv.REBECCA COMBS was born
2 CONC  about 1795 in Kingsport, Sullivan, Tennessee, USA. She died about 1860 in Perry County, Kentucky, USA. She married JOHN WILLIAMS. v.SAMUEL COMBS was born on 16 Jan 1799 in Kingsport, Sullivan, Tennessee, USA. He died on 11 Nov 18
2 CONC 81 in Booneville, Owsley, Kentucky, USA. He married Nancy Cornett on 12 Dec 1819 in Clay County, Kentucky, USA. She was born on 24 Dec 1803 in Bull Creek, Perry, Kentucky, USA. She died on 15 May 1885 in Booneville, Owsley, Kentuc
2 CONC ky, USA. vi.MILLIE COMBS was born about 1802 in Sullivan County, Tennessee, USA. She died about 1876 in Knott County, Kentucky, USA.∼Nicholas "Danger Nick" Combs was born circa 1760 +/- a couple years not 1737 as his marker incorr
2 CONC ectly states (see his 1850 Census aged 86 living next to his son Jeremiah "Chunky Jerry" and his family).  He also died about 20 year later in 1859.  He is one of the eight brothers born to John Combs & Nancy Harding and not an un
2 CONC cle to them.  His wife Nancy Euphemia Grigsby is about 3-10 years his elder and she had a daughter Nancy Elitia prior to their marriage. Stories have it that Nick was a known Tory and trouble maker and may have been on the run for
2 CONC  murder which is why he left Virginia.  I believe that he signed allegiance to these United States towards the end of the war.  Besides his step or adopted daughter Nancy Elitia, he had 4 possibly 5 known children with his wife- J
2 CONC eremiah "Chunky Jerry", Nicholas "Bird Eye", Rebecca, Samuel & Millie?.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.combs-families.org/combs/families/c-n1736.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.comteck.com/~jjackson/searchdn.html∼NICHOLAS "NICK" DANGER COMBS, My 5th Great Uncle ❤
2 CONT
2 CONT Second Creek, Perry County, Kentucky, USA - Location of death.  When Nicholas Danger Nick Combs was born in 1763 in Frederick, Virginia, his father, John, was 27 and his mother, Nancy, was 22. He had six brothers and one sister. H
2 CONC e died in 1859 in Perry, Kentucky, at the impressive age of 96.--Unknown Contributor
2 CONT ----------------------
