1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~brockfamily/CombsFamily.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Dicy L. Combs, first wife of Millard Lee Brock, was born abt 1880 in Clay Co., KY, or more likely in Leslie Co., formed off Clay in 1878. She died abt Sep 1902 at Catlettsburg, Boyd Co., KY, probably at a diphtheria camp at same t
2 CONC ime as her infant daughter Nellie, soon after daughter Bertha; buried at Catlettsburg, KY, one of about 150 graves across the road from Catlettsburg Grave Yard, on the hill behind the house at 8412 Catlettsburg Rd, Catlettsburg, K
2 CONC Y, 41129. No one takes care of the graves or is able to go up in the area because of snakes and out-of-control weeds, said Linda Baker who searched for Dicy's grave in Apr 2007 while visiting from Oregon.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Jackson "Jack" Combs (1858-bef Feb 1916) and his wife Nancy Shepherd (1852- ?).
2 CONT
2 CONT Jack Combs was born abt 1858, prob. in Perry Co., KY, for on the Census taken 5 July 1860 in District 2, Perry Co., p. 750, he was two years old:
2 CONT
2 CONT  hh 365-363: Ephraim Combs 35 farmer $400-$100 b. KY (can't read or write), Eliza 28 spinner KY, William 5 KY, Jackson 2 KY, and Jane Johnson 18 spinner KY
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Several nearby households had spinners, and Flax was grown in that area for linen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leslie Co. was created in 1878 from parts of Clay, Perry and Harlan Cos. Clay Co. was organized in 1806 from parts of Madison, Floyd, and Knox Cos. Perry Co. was created in 1820 out of Clay and Knox. Harlan Co. was created in 1819
2 CONC  out of Knox. Knox was created 1799 out of Lincoln Co., one of three original Kentucky counties in 1780 in Kentucky when it was no longer Kentucky Co., VA as designated in Dec 1776. He and his parents may never have moved.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jack Combs' wife (Dicy's mother), Nancy Shephard was the daughter of Shadrack "Shade" Shepherd (1785-1844) and his wife Malinda Roark (ca 1810-aft 1887). Malinda Roark was the daughter of John Roark, Sr., and Elizabeth Brock. Shad
2 CONC rack "Shade" Shepherd was son of James, son of Nimrod Shepherd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jack Combs' parents, Ephraim Combs and Eliza Combs, were 1st cousins, grandchildren of Henry H. Combs I and his wife Rachel Clements.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ephraim's was the son of Jeremiah "Curly Jerry" Combs (b. 1788, Shenandoah Co., VA, d. 28 Feb 1838, Perry Co., KY) and Nancy Grigsby (b. 1753, VA, d. 1850, KY).
2 CONT
2 CONT Curly Jerry Combs was the son of Nicholas "Danger Nick" Combs (21 Feb 1737 Frederick Co. VA now Caroline Co.-28 Feb 1838 Perry Co., KY, lived to be 101) and Nancy Grigsby (ca 1753 VA-Jan 1850 Perry Co. KY age 97 after a mo.-long i
2 CONC llness).
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas "Danger Nick" Combs was son of Mason Combs, Sr. (b. 1714 Putnam's End Creek, Caroline Co., VA, d. 1784, Surry Co., NC) and Sarah Ann Harding (b. 1718 King George Co. VA or Aqua Creek, Stafford Co., VA, d. 1785, Aqua Creek
2 CONC , Stafford Co.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason Combs Sr. was son of "Old John" Combs (b. aft 1663, Old Rappahannock Co., VA, d. 11 Dec 1716, Richmond Co., VA) and his 2nd wife Hannah Tutt(?) (b. 1770, Peuman's End Creek, Caroline Co., VA, d. 1717).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Old John" was a tobacco planter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eliza was daughter of Henry H. Combs II b. 1797 TN and wife Nancy Ann Brown b. 1797, NC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry H. Combs II was son of Henry H. Combs (b. 1765-68 Frederick Co., VA), and Rachel Clements (b. 1770), md. 26 Sep 1788, Montgomery Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry H. Combs was the son of John Combs, Sr. (b. 1733 Stafford Co., VA [another source says 1735-38, another says Westmoreland-King George Co.]-d. 1819 Floyd Co., KY buried Perry Co.), and Nancy Harding (b. ca 1735).
2 CONT
2 CONT John Combs Sr. was son of "Old John" Combs (b. aft 1663, Old Rappahannock Co., VA, d. 11 Dec 1716, Richmond Co., VA) and his 2nd wife Hannah Tutt(?) (b. 1770, Peuman's End Creek, Caroline Co., VA, d. 1717).
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy Harding was daughter of Henry Harding II (ca 1710-1779) and Wilmoth George; HH II was son of Henry Harding I (ca 1685, d. bef 1756. We don't know their relation to Sarah Ann Harding but both families were from Stafford Co., 
2 CONC VA
2 CONT
