3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DNA match MRCA George Rogers-Winifred Combs to descendants confirmed Gedmatch #M010052
2 CONT
2 CONT See bio of her husband, https://www.geni.com/people/Reverend-Robert-Hicks-Sr/6000000084104029055, for more information.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Combs-610<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy is the daughter of William Combs and Sytha Stacy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy Winnifred Combs, born about 1765/1770 (1765)[1]), probably in Frederick County, Virginia or Rowan County, North Carolina; died after 1840 in Wright County, Missouri[2] (possibly circa 1860[3]). <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Winnifred married (1) Samuel Sumner (1760-1787/8) bef 1784, possibly in Montgomery County, Virginia; (2) Rev. Robert Hicks, Sr. (c1770-aft 1840), before 1798,[2] in Virginia.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT By Samuel, she had a son and three daughters:[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT *     John Sumner, born about 1782, married Judy (Judah) Stewart[5] 
2 CONT *     Elizabeth Sumner, born about 1783,[2] married John Cody[4] 
2 CONT *     Synthia Sumner, born between 1785 and 1791 in Tennessee, married before 1807 Jeremiah C. Combs, son of Nicholas and Nancy (Grigsby) Combs[6][2] 
2 CONT *     Mary Summers, married George Stacy[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was dead by 1788 ("kild, wife gone to Washington."[2]) and Winnifred married Robert Hicks in Virginia. They had moved to Kentucky by 1806.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT By Robert, she had 
2 CONT *     James Hicks, born 1797/98,[2] married Hester Cox[4] 
2 CONT *     Mary Hicks, married Mr. Ingram (also Ingrain)[4] 
2 CONT *     Sarah Hicks, married Joshua Rippee[4] 
2 CONT *     Robert Hicks Jr., born Clay County, Kentucky, 28 May 1804, married Elizabeth Polley[4] 
2 CONT *     Frances Hicks, born Clay County, Kentucky, married George Rogers[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Hicks, Sr. died October 8, 1845, in Kentucky. His wife, Winifred, proceeded him in death as when he sold property in Perry County, Kentucky, no wife signed the deed.[4] (I think because she was not in Kentucky. The followin
2 CONC g says she died in Wright County, Missouri. This Rootsweb post also has her death in Wright County, c1860.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 'According to the 1889 Wright County, Missouri biography of Winnifred Combs' grandson, Samuel Coday, Winnifred died in that county "at a very old age." Samuel Coday also states that his grandfather, Samuel Sumner was a miller by o
2 CONC ccupation and that he was "waylaid and shot;" however, the Dickey Diary Interview of Winnifred's grandson, John S. Combs (s/o Jeremiah C. "Chunky" and Synthia Sumner Combs), states that he was killed "resisting arrest" (not necess
2 CONC arily mutually exclusive).'<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT DO NOT CONFUSE WITH https://www.geni.com/people/Nancy-Hicks/6000000013062003042, wife of Robert Hicks
