1 NAME Dorothy /Mason/
2 GIVN Dorothy
2 SURN Mason
2 _MARNM Combs
2 NICK Dolly
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1750 AND 1753
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Hawkins County, TN or Stratford, Westmoreland County, VA, United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1828
2 ADDR
3 STAE TN
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mason COMBS, Jr., b 21 Feb 1746/47, Overwharton Parish, Stafford Co, VA; d 1801-1808, probably in Hawkins Co, TN; m bef 1786, possibly in Surry Co, NC, Dorothy "Dolly" UNKNOWN, d aft 1828, probably in Warren Co, TN
2 CONC . Also recorded in Montgomery and Russell Cos, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT (Hawkins Co, TN DB3:69) Dtd. 2/22/1802 Reg. 11/1/1802  Trust Mason Combs to his Wife & Children  Registered 1 November 1802 Trans from Leber E, page 385
2 CONT
2 CONT Know all men by these presents that I Mason Combs of the county of Hawkins and State of Tennessee for devers Good Causes & reasons well known, I do give & bequeath unto my wife Dorothy Combs Two Choice Cows all the Hogs & Sheep,tw
2 CONC o Sorrel mares all the beds & Furniture that now belongs to me to dispose of at her will after my decease the Tract of Land that I now live on I give and bequeath to my two Sons Simeon & Jeremiah to be Equally Divided between them
2 CONC  Simeon to have the Lower end and Jeremiah Combs to have the upper End only Reserving to the use of their mother Dorothy Combs Ten acres out of each half when divided as She thinks proper to choose also the use of what Timber She 
2 CONC may want for her use during her the two boys to have all the profits arising from Said Lands and their Mother to have the privilege of Renting and Seeing to the Said Land untill the boys comes of age [---] for all my Goods & chatt
2 CONC les of every kinds whatsoever that now belongs to me I leive to my wife Dorothy Combs during her life or widowhood for the use and benefit of my children in Trust at the end of which it is to be Equally Divided among my surviving 
2 CONC children only Simeon is to have the first Colt that the Big Sorrel mare brings and Jerry is to have as his own the yearlin colt now belonging to the Roan Mare Ther mother to have the charge & care of them untill the boys become of
2 CONC  age and the Increase of sd colts young to Dispose of as She thinks fit. All these things I do Give and Grant as before mentioned and do hereby confirm.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Witness of which I here unto set my hand & seal this 22nd day of February in the year of our Lord 1802.  Mason [M] Combs (Seal) [his mark]
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed and Delivered in presence of Wm Paine, Jacob Manus, Martin Johnson.  State of Tennessee ) Hawkins County ) August Session 1802
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.combs-families.org/combs/families/c-mas1.htm#children
2 CONT
2 CONT "Pedigree Resource File," database, FamilySearch (http://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.2.1/9W98-JXD : accessed 25 September 2012), entry for Dorothy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT See also: http://www.combs-families.org/combs/dna/index.html?virtual_archive/index.htm
