1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Lucinda Page “Lucy” Baylor Armistead
2 CONT *BIRTH	12 Oct 1747 Milford, Caroline County, Virginia
2 CONT *DEATH	26 Nov 1816 (aged 69) Alexandria City, Virginia, USA
2 CONT *BURIAL	 Baylor Family Cemetery Bowling Green, Caroline County, Virginia, USA
2 CONT * Daughter of John Baylor, III and Frances Lucy (Walker) Baylor 
2 CONT *Wife of John Armistead (son of William Armistead and Mary Bowles)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.ancestraltrackers.net/va/resources/family-armistead-virginia.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT 24. V. John Armistead, of Caroline County, of College of William and Mary 1755 ; m. 17 March, 1764, Lucy, daughter of John Baylor of Newmarket. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT * i. John Baylor. 41 
2 CONT *ii. Mary, m. Landon Carter of Richmond County.
2 CONT * iii. William. 42
2 CONT * iv. Frances, m. Gillis of Alexandria. 
2 CONT * V. Addison Bowles. 43
2 CONT *vi. George, b. at Newmarket 10 April, 1779. 44
2 CONT * vii. Lewis Gustavus Adolphus, Captain U. S. A., killed in the sortie from Fort Erie, Canada, 17 September, 1814.
2 CONT * viii. Walker Keith, b. in 1783. 45
2 CONT * ix. Eleanor Bowles, m. Col. John Dangeriield of Essex County.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Usually referred to as Lucy
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/104352148/lucinda-page-armistead
2 CONT * Dorman, John Frederick. 2004. Adventurers of Purse and Person, Virginia, 1607-1624/5. Genealogical Pub. Co. 4th edition. Vol 1, Page 267 and 279, book lookup by Hill, C. [03/04/2024]
