1 NOTE !BIRTH - See Death Reference
2 CONT Mrs. Lucinda Armistead died in 1816 in her 71st year, her birth would have been about 1745.
2 CONT
2 CONT GENEALOGY OF THE KNOWN DESCENDANTS OF ROBERT CARTER OF COROTOMAN compiled by Florence Tyler Carlton, p. 372
2 CONT Lucy Baylor was the wife of John Armistead and mother of Mary Burwell Armistead.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - SELDENS OF VIRGINIA AND ALLIED FAMILIES VOL I by Mary Selden Kennedy, p. 183
2 CONT Lucy Baylor of New Market, Caroline Co. married John Armistead March 17, 1764.  She was the daughter of John Baylor, who died at his home in Caroline Co., VA., April 16, 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - MARRIAGES AND DEATHS FROM BALTIMORE NEWSPAPERS 1796-1816 by Robert Barnes, p. 8 - BALTIMORE FEDERAL GAZETTE 1796-1816
2 CONT Armistead, Mrs. Lucinda, relict of the late John Armistead of Caroline Co., VA., died in Alexandria, 26 ult., in her 71st year.  At one time she had four sons in the service of their country; one was a captain in the Rifle Corps. 
2 CONC and fell at Fort Erie.  (BFG, 2 Dec. 1816)
2 CONT Note:  Date of death would be 26 Nov 1816. - JMC
