1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Major Walker Baylor''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/19818269/walker-baylor
2 CONT
2 CONT Served as lieutenant of the Third Continental Dragoons, 1777, and rose to the rank of captain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Walker Baylor commanded General George Washington's Life Guard in the Third Continental Division at the Battle of Germantown. Disabled at Germantown when a bullet shattered his foot progenitor of the Baylor families of Ken
2 CONC tucky and Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT ''REVOLUTIONARY WAR DISABILITY AFFIDAVIT - WALKER BAYLOR''
2 CONT
2 CONT Baylor, Walker Pen 21 1786-1789
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain--3rd Regt Light Dragoons
2 CONT
2 CONT Caroline County 
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother John
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife Fanny
2 CONT
2 CONT I do, with the advice of council, hereby certify that, Walker Baylor, about 26 years of age, late a captain in the 3rd Regiment of Light Dragoons, appears to have been disabled in such a manner while in the service of The United S
2 CONC tates as to entitle him to the sum of forty five pounds yearly; which allowance accordingly made him, to commence on the first day of January 1786. Given under my hand this 27th day of November 1786.
2 CONT
2 CONT P. Henry
2 CONT
2 CONT It is hereby certified that Walker Baylor was a captain in the 3rd Regiment of Light Dragoons and was wounded by a cannon ball at the Battle of German Town having been in the service of the United States. November 27 1786 
2 CONT
2 CONT signature unreadable
2 CONT
2 CONT Received of Benjamin Taylor deputy for W. Taylor of Caroline twenty two pounds ten shillings in part of the within.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Assistant Surgeon, USA, Brevet Major, Continental Army Capt of Lady Washington's Life Guards, Trenton 1777
2 CONT
