1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Thomas Newton, III was a Colonel in the Virginia Militia. He was in command of the milita of Norfolk Borough in 1780 and 1781, was commissioner of supplies, supplying the French Army and the fleet during the siege
2 CONC  of Yorktown. Commissioner of Admiralty 1776. Colonel Commandant militia of Norfolk Co., Sept. 1781." The references for this information were listed as: Vol 29, p. 516-519, and Vol. 30, p. 85-88, Virginia Magazine of History and 
2 CONC Biography.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/m/e/t/Mildred-Methvin/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0120.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Newton,_Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Newton, Jr. (November 21, 1768 – August 5, 1847) was an American politician. He was born in Norfolk, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Newton was a member of the Virginia House of Delegates from 1796 to 1799. He served as a Democratic-Republican in the United States House of Representatives from March 4, 1801 to March 9, 1830, losing his seat when George Loyall c
2 CONC ontested his election. He regained his seat at the next election and served a final term from March 4, 1831 to March 3, 1833. In the bitterly contested 1824 presidential election, Newton was the only Virginia representative to sup
2 CONC port the Adams-Clay coalition.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=7024471&ref=wvr
