1 CONT Newspaper Obiturary for Margaret Stephens Gracy 
1 CONT Mrs. Gracy, 86, dies at home; rites tomorrow 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Mrs. Margaret Stephens Gracy, 86, Gainesville resident since 1907, diedtoday at her home, 314 NW 4th Ave. She had been confined to her bed sincebreaking her hip last September. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT She was born Dec. 28, 1864 in Troy, Tenn., and was the widow of Luther C.Gracy, whom she married in December, 1895. They lived their entiremarried life in Alachua County, first moving to High Springs. Mr. Gracydied April 5, 1922. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Mrs. Gracy was one of the founders and the first president of the NewCentury Woman's Club in High Springs, and was twice president of the 20thCentury Club in Gainesville. She was a member of the First MethodistChurch here. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Survivors include two daughters, Mrs. Sam P. Harn, Gainesville: and Mrs.Gordon W. Graham, San Carlos, Calif: one son, L. C. Gracy, Jr.,Gainesville: and 11 grandchildren and three great grandchildren. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Also surviving is a sister, Mrs. J.W. Brantley, Louisville, Ky.; twonephews, Lt. Col. John S. Neel, Peterburg, Va., and Enoch Brantley,Hollywood, Calif.; and two nieces, Mrs. Otto Kalich, High Springs, Fl;and Mrs. Ashby Miller, Lo
1 CONC uisville. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Services will be held at 4 p. m. Thursday in the Thomas Funeral Home, Dr.R.C. Holmes, pastor of the First Methodist Church, will officiate.Interment will be in Evergreen Cemetary. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Pallbearers will be Wade Hampton, Sam McK Mixson, P.C. Keeter, H.G.Florida, Arthur C. Brown, J.E. Relihan, Logan Hill and Robert Lassiter. 
1 CONT ------------------ 
1 CONT
