0 @N6000000005965685172@ NOTE July 22, 2006
1 CONT
1 CONT Clyde "Jim" Lewis III
1 CONT
1 CONT Brandon
1 CONT
1 CONT Clyde James "Jim" Lewis, III, 41, a devoted Christian, family man and friend to many, went to be with his Lord on Wednesday, July 19, 2006 in Cresco, Iowa as the result of injuries sustained in an aviation accident. Visitation is 
1 CONC 4-8 p.m. today at Ott & Lee Funeral Home in Brandon. Services are 3 p.m. Sunday at Pinelake Baptist Church with burial in Lakeland Place Cemetery. Dr. Chip Henderson will officiate.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jim was born in Jackson, and was a member of the 1982 graduating class of Jim Hill High School. He was an accomplished black belt in Karate having earned his degree while in high school. From an early age, Jim loved to fly airplan
1 CONC es, having flown solo at the age of 15 and later earning his pilot's license. Jim continued his formal education at Mississippi College and then on to Delta State University where he completed his aviation degree.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jim began his career as a pilot with AV Charter Company at the early age of 21. He continued his career with US Airways where he was employed as a pilot for 16 years. After leaving US Airways, Jim began flying privately for SAKS C
1 CONC orporation and later with Jackson Aviation Charter Services. He was an active member of the MS Soaring Association.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jim was best known by all as a devoted Christian, husband, father, son, brother and friend. He was a friend to all who knew him. To those who met and knew Jim, his smile and kindness captured the essence of his spirit and his hear
1 CONC t. Although Jim's passion was flying, his true love was his family, his wife Leslie and son Zachary, and his daily spiritual walk with his Lord. Jim was an active member of Pinelake Baptist Church family where he will be deeply mi
1 CONC ssed. Jim's approach to business reflected his walk with his Lord and his devotion to his family and friends. Jim was a principal partner and developer of WoodBridge subdivision at the Northshore in Rankin County. Jim's vision for
1 CONC  WoodBridge was to be a place where common Christian families and friends could share and live in a community that would glorify the Lord. Jim was a mentor to others as he touched their lives.
1 CONT
1 CONT Survivors include his wife, Leslie Lewis of Brandon; son, Zachary Lewis of Brandon; mother, Judy Lewis of Brandon; father, Dr. Jimmy Lewis, Jr., and his wife Laura of Terry; brothers, Jay Lewis and his wife Wendy of Flower Mound, 
1 CONC Texas; Jon Lewis and his wife Tricia of Byram and Jeff Lewis and his wife Crystal of Brandon; stepsisters, Kristin Smith of Terry and Kandice Rowe and her husband Mark of Terry. He is also survived by numerous nephews and nieces. 
1 CONC Pallbearers will be Ken Bailey, Ken Blaine, William Cummins, Jeff Lewis, Ray Montgomery and Curt Summerlin. Honorary Pallbearers are Mike King, Jay Lewis, Jon Lewis, Dean Melton, Eugine Starks and Andy Stewart.
1 CONT
1 CONT Memorials may be made to Son Valley, a division of Baptist Homes. Inc., P. O. Box 406, Canton, MS 39046.
1 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------
