1 CONT July 21, 2006
1 CONT
1 CONT Jackson Clarion Ledger
1 CONT July 21, 2006
1 CONT
1 CONT Investigations ongoing in pair of plane crashes
1 CONT
1 CONT Families, friends mourn four men killed in two separate accidents
1 CONT
1 CONT By Chris Joyner
1 CONT chris.joyner@jackson.gannett.com
1 CONT
1 CONT Friends and family are mourning two Jackson-area pilots killed in Wednesday's plane crash in Cresco, Iowa.
1 CONT
1 CONT Clyde James "Jim" Lewis, 41, of Brandon and William Eisner of Pearl were killed when the plane overshot the runway, crossed a highway and plowed into a cornfield. The men were employed by Jackson Air Charter, a private charter pla
1 CONC ne service that operates out of Jackson-Evers International Airport.
1 CONT
1 CONT Little information about the accident was released Thursday as investigators with the National Transportation Security Board and the Federal Aviation Administration continued to gather information at the scene just south of the Mi
1 CONC nnesota border. NTSB officials did not return calls seeking comment.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jeff Lewis said his brother, a Jackson native, had 26 years experience as a pilot, including 15 years with US Airways. He said the family has not been told much about what caused the crash.
1 CONT
1 CONT "Everything is speculation," he said.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jim Lewis is survived by his wife, Leslie, and 10-year-old son, Zachary. Funeral arrangements for Lewis tentatively have been set for Sunday at 3 p.m. at Pinelake Church at 6071 Mississippi 25 in Brandon.
1 CONT
1 CONT Information on services for Eisner was not available Thursday.
1 CONT
1 CONT The plane's two passengers are being treated for their injuries. Robert Paulk of Gulfport is listed in critical condition at the Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minn. Johnny Fayard, 51, also of Gulfport, was unconscious but in stable co
1 CONC ndition at Gunderson Lutheran Hospital in La Cross, Wis., according to his wife, Tanya Fayard, who was at the hospital on Thursday.
1 CONT
1 CONT The Cessna jet crashed in a landing attempt at the Cresco airport around 11:10 a.m.
1 CONT
1 CONT The flight, which began in Oxford, was destined for Rochester, but Fayard said her husband's eventual destination was the Mayo Clinic, where he was scheduled to receive a brace for his foot and leg.
1 CONT
1 CONT Johnny Fayard suffers from reflex sympathetic dystrophy, or RSD, a painful, neurological condition that usually develops from an injury.
1 CONT
1 CONT Tanya Fayard said she has not heard what caused crash. "We have no clue," she said.
1 CONT
1 CONT The National Weather Service reported thunderstorms moving through the Cresco area at the time.
1 CONT
1 CONT Two men were killed Wednesday in an unrelated small plane accident in Petal.
1 CONT
1 CONT Life-long Petal resident Ernest R. "Buddy" Myrick, 92, and 49-year-old Jim Hartman of Gulfport were killed when the single-engine plane crashed during or shortly after takeoff from a private airstrip near the intersection of Smith
1 CONC ville Drive and Corinth Road in Petal. National Transportation Safety Board air safety investigator Tim LeBaron said preliminary results of the NTSB investigation will be completed by next week, but a full investigation likely wil
1 CONC l take a year to complete.
1 CONT
1 CONT He said investigators aren't sure which man was piloting the plane.
1 CONT
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT The Hattiesburg American contributed to this report.
