1 CONT WILL OF SAMUEL ROSAMOND - Page 3 -
1 CONT
1 CONT 1  Codicil
1 CONT
1 CONT I, Samuel Rosemon, in the foregoing or annexed last will and testament having further considered the same do think proper to make constitute and publish the following codicil thereto in the following manner--
1 CONT
1 CONT First, I will and request of my executors to dispose of the plantation and lands whereon I now reside at public sale.  
1 CONT
1 CONT Secondly, I leave my Negro man, Will, to be disposed of according to my will hearing date of September 2, 1808, and the residue of my Negroes namely, Peter, Jim, and Dudly, with Tenah, Sinah, Jenny, and Charlotte, are to be sold. 
1 CONC   And further, I give to my affectionate wife all my household and kitchen furniture with six milk cows and the stock of hogs that belongs to the mill-with a sufficient  quantity of corn for the support of the family for one year.
1 CONT
1 CONT It is my will that my executors pay yearly to my affectionate wife, Sarah Roseman, out of my estate, five pounds for each minor under age.
1 CONT
1 CONT It further is my will that the grist mill be kept in good repair and the expenses to be defrayed out of the income of the mill and the remainder to go to the use of the family.
1 CONT
1 CONT And, I do constitute Robert McCann, Esq. And Capt Barksdale Garrison, my true and lawful executors to my last will and testament.
1 CONT
1 CONT In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand Seal this 18th Day of June 1812.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Witness present:
1 CONT
1 CONT Wm FaripSaml Rosamond (SEAL)
1 CONT          his
1 CONT Sam  (X) Tucker
1 CONT         mark
1 CONT David Thomas
1 CONT
