1 CONT ca 1780 when Sarah F. was 20, she married Richard Hodges Jr., H322, M, son of Richard Hodges, M & Elizabeth (Betty) Jones, F, in South Carolina. Born  ca 1756 in Jamestown County, Virginia. Richard died in Versailles, Ripley Count
1 CONC y, Indiana  bef 7 Jan 1824, he was 68. Buried in Riley County, Indiana.
1 CONT
1 CONT From a letter to Ruth Menhel from:
1 CONT Mrs. Bernadeen Kamper, 13373 Plaza Del Ria, Apt. 2251, Peoria, AZ 85381.
1 CONT Mrs. Kemper is the ggg-granddaughter of Richard and Sarah F. (Rosamond) Hodges.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage date for Sarah and Richard is 1779 or 1780. She shows Sarah and Richard having ten children, although she did not list them. She stated that DAR records show Richard Hodges as a private and a lieutenant under Capt. Samuel
1 CONC  Rosamond's Company in South Carolina. 
1 CONT
1 CONT -------------------------- In opposition to the above ----------------------------
1 CONT The 1820 census of Ripley County, Indiana shows Richard Hodges at age less than 45, with a wife also at an age of less than 45. The 1830 census does not show Richard who died in 1824, but does show Rubin Hodges, a son of Richard a
1 CONC nd Sarah. This census shows Rubin Hodges with a female in the household between the ages of 50 - 60. If this is his mother, these two records would indicate that Sarah was born betwee 1770 and 1775.
