1 CONT "Died in Union County, Miss., April 30th, 1879, Mrs. Jane Liddell, Aged 77 years, 3 months and 2 days ...  born in Old Pendleton District, S.C. ... daughter of Samuel and Sarah Roseman. In her 17th year, she married Col. J.S. Lidd
1 CONC ell, who preceded her to the grave about ten years ... in youth joined Roberts Presbyterian Church. In the first settlement of North Mississippi by the whites, she came with her family to this section, and when Ebenezer (ARP) chur
1 CONC ch was organized she was one of the original number ... three daughters and one son survive."
1 CONT ------------------------------
1 CONT "When Jane died, only 4 children of the 12 she had had were still living:  John, Mary, Sarahann; and Martha. She lost 3 sons in the Civil War: William; Charles; and Samuel.
1 CONT ------------------------------
