1 CONT An Associate Rebormed (sic) Presbyterian Church was organized at Ebenezer, near the village of Cotton Plant, in the year 1842. Early settlers had arrive in the community in 1838 and had begun preliminary organization. The Jones, M
1 CONC cBrydes, Liddells,Stephensons, Stewarts, Craigs and Wisemans are names frequently found in the early records of this church. The organization of the church occurred on Saturday before the third Sabbath of July, the 16th of the mon
1 CONC th, 1842, with Rev. John Wilson in charge. The charter members were: Major Robert McBryde, William McBryde, James Stephenson, Miss M. L. Liddell (Mary Lucinda), Sarah McBryde, Jane Liddell (Jane Rosamond Liddell), Rachel Stephenso
1 CONC n, Andrew Jones, Elizabeth Liddell, Elizabeth Stephenson, Elizabeth Jones, Margaret McBryde. Early preachers were: John Wilson, L. McDonald, S.S. Ralston, Joseph McCreary, A. M. Borden, J. M. Young, D. Pressley, Robert McCoy, D. P
1 CONC . Robinson, S. P. Davis, J. A. Sloan, J. P. Wood."
1 CONT [End Angela Davis excerpts]
