1 CONT Legislature of Kentucky. Some of "Lige's" relatives said he was an awe some sight when he appeared in full
1 CONT regimental dress to muster the "Cornstalk Militia" (this was the name given to the troops).
1 CONT
1 CONT General "Lige" and Sarah are buried behind the present Perry Co., KY C ourthouse. They did not get the praise
1 CONT that they deserve for starting the community on the way to civilizatio n. They do deserve some recognition for
1 CONT donating the land to the city. And many years of community service. Re cently, the Perry Co. DAR erected a
1 CONT plaque in honor of both Elijah and Sarah Roark COMBS for donating the land for the city.
1 CONT One of "Lige's" sons was killed in the famous "French-Eversole" Feud.
