0 @N6000000004270555196@ NOTE http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:434296&id=I094
1 CONT
1 CONT # Robert NELSON
1 CONT # Sex: M
1 CONT # Birth: 1792 in Clarksville, Cumberland County, Tenn.
1 CONT # Note:
1 CONT
1 CONT     July 7, 1847 - John Steele (brother-in-law of Robert Nelson, Sr) gave to Robert Nelson Sr. a negro boy named Dave to benefit the children of Robert Nelson. ( Legal document - Montgomery County, Tenn.)
1 CONT
1 CONT     Nov. 4, 1848 - John Steele in his will gives Robert Nelson, Jr. and Sarah A. Nelson (his nephew and niece) approximately 110 acres of land. Steele gives to his brother-in-law Robert Nelson, Sr. approximately 100 acres of land 
1 CONC involved in a suit with one Mr. Chitson. (Legal document - Montgomery, Co., Tenn.)
1 CONT
1 CONT     Dec. 4, 1848 - Robert Nelson, Sr. deeds over the disputed 100 acres (which John Steele had given him) to his son Robert, Jr. and to his daughter Sarah A. Nelson. (Legal document - Montgomery, Co., Tenn.)
1 CONT
1 CONT     1850 Census - Sarah A. Nelson (16) living in the home of Nancy L. Poston (formerly Nancy Lowthing Nelson) in Montgomery Co., Tenn.)
1 CONT
1 CONT     Robert Nelson (16) in Tyler's School in Montgomery Co., Tenn.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Oct. 1851 - Robert Nelson, Sr. in charge of $600 trust fund left by one Thomas B. Jones (of Virginia) to Robert Nelson, Jr. and Sarah A. Nelson. (Legal document - Montogomery Co., Tenn.)
1 CONT
1 CONT     Oct 1855 - Robert Nelson appointed overseer of the road he resided on. (Legal document - Montogomery Co., Tenn.)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT     This Robert Nelson and his sister Mary Sally Nelson wife of John Carter. Inherited part of the estate of their grandfather, William Cary, dead of Williamsburg, VA. in 1859. The Sally Nelson wife of Carter was in Amite County, 
1 CONC Miss. in 1861.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Father: Thomas NELSON b: 1747
1 CONT Mother: Sally M. CARY
